window.GUIDE=window.GUIDE||{};GUIDE.en=[];
GUIDE.en.push({"n":1,"t":"건강","en":"Health","units":[{"n":1,"t":"건강에 좋은 음식","g":[{"f":"-다가 보니까","en":"while (I kept) doing X, I found / it turned out Y","core":"You did something continuously or repeatedly, and as a result you discovered something or ended up in a new state. The 보니까 part means \"looking back, I realized.\" It's a cause-and-discovery pattern.","forms":[["Verb","먹다(가) 보니까 · 살다(가) 보니까 · 만들다(가) 보니까"]],"rules":["Verbs only, and 가 is often dropped in speech: <b>먹다 보니까</b>.","No tense on the X clause: never 먹었다가 보니까.","The Y clause reports a discovery or a result, usually in the past or present: -었어요, -게 됐어요, -더라고요, -네요.","The X action is something done over time or repeatedly. That's why it pairs with 자주, 매일, 계속.","Don't confuse it with <b>-다가 보면</b> (5과), which is a general prediction: \"if you keep doing X, you'll Y.\" -다 보니까 describes something that already happened."],"ex":[["매일 잡곡밥을 **먹다 보니까** 이제는 흰쌀밥이 맛이 없어요.","After eating multigrain rice every day, white rice now tastes bland to me."],["혼자 **살다 보니까** 요리 실력이 늘었어요.","Living alone, my cooking ended up getting better."],["친구와 이야기를 **하다 보니까** 벌써 밤 12시가 됐어요.","I was chatting with a friend, and before I knew it, it was midnight."]]},{"f":"-을 겸","en":"to do X and also Y; doubling as","core":"You do one action for two (or more) purposes at the same time. The full pattern is <b>-(으)ㄹ 겸 -(으)ㄹ 겸</b>, and it also works with nouns: <b>N 겸 N</b>.","forms":[["Verb, no 받침","볼 겸 · 쉴 겸 (ㄹ-stem: 살다 → 살 겸)"],["Verb, 받침","먹을 겸 · 읽을 겸"],["Noun","아침 겸 점심 (= brunch) · 운동 겸 산책"]],"rules":["Usually followed by a verb of movement or action: 가다, 오다, 나가다, 하다.","Two purposes: <b>운동도 할 겸 친구도 만날 겸</b> (add 도 to each). One stated purpose implies there's another unstated one.","Verbs only, not adjectives. No tense on the 겸 clause.","N 겸 N also describes something with two roles: 거실 겸 서재 (a living room that doubles as a study)."],"ex":[["운동도 **할 겸** 장도 **볼 겸** 시장까지 걸어갔어요.","I walked to the market to get some exercise and do the grocery shopping."],["건강도 **챙길 겸** 직접 밥상을 차려 먹기로 했어요.","I decided to cook my own meals, partly to look after my health."],["늦게 일어나서 **아침 겸 점심**으로 비빔밥을 먹었어요.","I got up late, so I had bibimbap as a brunch."]]}],"v":[["밥상","meal table; a spread of food","Thinks of the food laid out, not just furniture. Goes with <b>밥상을 차리다 / 치우다</b> and 밥상 앞에 앉다.","엄마가 맛있는 **밥상**을 차려 주셨어요.","Mom set out a delicious meal for us."],["잡곡밥","multigrain rice","잡곡 = mixed grains (현미, 보리, 콩). Used as the healthy opposite of 흰쌀밥.","요즘 건강 때문에 **잡곡밥**을 먹어요.","I eat multigrain rice these days for my health."],["마음먹다","to make up one's mind, resolve","Usually <b>-기로 마음먹다</b>. 마음먹은 대로 = the way you intended. 마음만 먹으면 = if you just set your mind to it.","올해는 야식을 끊기로 **마음먹었어요**.","I've made up my mind to quit late-night snacks this year."],["시키다","to order (food); to make someone do","Colloquial for 주문하다, especially delivery: <b>치킨을 시켜 먹다</b>. Also causative: 동생에게 청소를 시키다.","피곤해서 저녁은 배달 음식을 **시켰어요**.","I was tired, so I ordered delivery for dinner."],["차리다","to set (a table), prepare (a meal); to set up","<b>밥상/상을 차리다</b>, 가게를 차리다 (open a shop), 정신을 차리다 (pull yourself together).","손님이 오셔서 저녁상을 **차렸어요**.","Guests came, so I set out dinner."],["그러게","I know, right; exactly","Casual agreement (polite: 그러게요). Also 그러게 내가 뭐랬어 = told you so.","A: 요즘 너무 덥지? B: **그러게**. 입맛이 없어.","A: It's so hot lately, right? B: I know. I've got no appetite."],["마침","just then; luckily, at the right moment","For a timely coincidence. Don't mix up 마치 (as if) and 마침내 (finally). 마침 잘됐다 = what perfect timing.","배가 고팠는데 **마침** 친구가 떡을 가져왔어요.","I was hungry, and just then a friend brought rice cakes."]],"x":[["데우다","to heat up, warm (already cooked food or liquid)","For reheating: 국/우유를 데우다, 전자레인지에 데우다. 끓이다 = boil. 데다 = get burned (different word).","남은 국을 **데워서** 먹었어요.","I heated up the leftover soup and ate it."],["데치다","to blanch","Quick dunk in boiling water: <b>시금치/브로콜리를 살짝 데치다</b>.","시금치를 끓는 물에 살짝 **데쳤어요**.","I lightly blanched the spinach in boiling water."],["손쉽다","easy, simple (to do by hand)","Mostly used as 손쉽게 or 손쉬운: \"easy, effortless.\" ㅂ irregular: 손쉬워요.","집에서 **손쉽게** 만들 수 있는 건강 요리예요.","It's a healthy dish you can easily make at home."],["식히다¹","to cool something down","Causative of 식다. 뜨거운 국을 식히다. Idiom: <b>머리를 식히다</b> = clear your head.","국이 너무 뜨거워서 좀 **식혀서** 먹었어요.","The soup was too hot, so I let it cool a bit first."],["손이 가다","(1) to take a lot of work; (2) to keep reaching for (food)","(1) <b>손이 많이 가는 음식</b> = labor-intensive dish. (2) 자꾸 손이 가요 = I can't stop eating it.","김밥은 **손이 많이 가서** 자주 못 만들어요.","Gimbap takes a lot of work, so I can't make it often."]]},{"n":2,"t":"건강한 생활 습관","g":[{"f":"도 -이지만","en":"X matters too, but (more importantly) Y","core":"The pattern is <b>N도 N이지만</b>, repeating the same noun. You acknowledge one factor and then shift to what you think matters more. It's like saying \"price is one thing, but…\"","forms":[["Noun, 받침","음식도 음식이지만 · 돈도 돈이지만"],["Noun, no 받침","운동도 운동이지만 · 나이도 나이지만 (이 drops after a vowel in speech)"]],"rules":["The same noun appears twice: <b>맛도 맛이지만</b>, never 맛도 가격이지만.","The second clause names the bigger or more important point, often with 더, 무엇보다, 그보다.","Useful for giving balanced opinions in speaking tests and essays."],"ex":[["**운동도 운동이지만** 잠을 충분히 자는 게 더 중요해요.","Exercise matters too, but getting enough sleep is more important."],["이 식당은 **맛도 맛이지만** 분위기가 정말 좋아요.","This restaurant's food is good, but the atmosphere is what's really great."],["**돈도 돈이지만** 건강을 해치면 아무 소용이 없어요.","Money is one thing, but if you ruin your health, it's all for nothing."]]},{"f":"-지요","en":"(of course) X, you know — stating something as obvious or known from experience","core":"The speaker presents something as a fact they know well, often from their own experience, or as common sense the listener should accept: \"Of course it takes time,\" \"You know, I struggled too.\" In your book, a 선배 uses it to reassure a 후배 and then gives advice. The tone is confident but warm.","forms":[["Verb","걸리지요 · 고생했지요 · 없지요"],["Adjective","힘들지요 · 중요하지요 · 외로웠지요"],["Noun","당연하지요 · 처음이지요 · 문제지요"],["Casual (반말)","걸리지 · 했지 · 중요하지"]],"rules":["Stem + 지요, regardless of 받침. Past: <b>-았/었지요</b>. Spoken short form: <b>-죠</b>. Casual: <b>-지</b>.","Falling intonation. With rising intonation, -지요? asks for confirmation (\"right?\"), which is a different use.","Typical flow in this unit: <b>experience or general truth + -지요</b>, then advice: 시간이 걸리지. 녹음해서 들어 봐.","Often with 당연히, 원래, 누구나, 처음에는, 나도, which all reinforce the \"that's just how it is\" feel.","Compare: -잖아요 also presents shared knowledge, but implies \"you already know this.\" -지요 just states it as obvious."],"ex":[["강의를 제대로 알아듣기까지는 시간이 **걸리지**. 녹음해서 여러 번 들어 봐.","It takes time before you can really follow lectures, you know. Record them and listen several times."],["나도 처음에는 보고서 쓰느라 고생을 많이 **했지**. 다양한 글을 많이 읽고 써 봐.","I struggled a lot with reports at first too. Read and write lots of different kinds of writing."],["아르바이트와 공부를 둘 다 잘할 수는 **없지요**. 하나를 선택해서 열심히 하는 게 좋아요.","Of course you can't do both a part-time job and studying well. It's better to choose one and focus on it."]]}],"v":[["방해","disturbance, hindrance","<b>방해(가) 되다</b>, 방해하다, 수면 방해. N에 방해가 되다 = get in the way of N.","자기 전에 휴대폰을 보면 숙면에 **방해**가 돼요.","Looking at your phone before bed interferes with deep sleep."],["숙면","deep, sound sleep","Formal. <b>숙면을 취하다</b> = get sound sleep. Common in health articles.","따뜻한 우유는 **숙면**에 도움이 돼요.","Warm milk helps you sleep soundly."],["놓다¹","to put, place; to leave (in a state)","Basic sense: put. Also auxiliary <b>-아/어 놓다</b> (켜 놓다 = leave on). 마음을 놓다 = relax, stop worrying.","휴대폰을 침대에서 먼 곳에 **놓고** 자요.","I put my phone somewhere far from the bed when I sleep."],["들이다¹","to form (a habit)","This sense: <b>습관을 들이다</b> = build a habit. (들이다² in 5과 = spend money/time.)","아이에게 일찍 자는 습관을 **들이는** 게 중요해요.","It's important to get kids into the habit of going to bed early."],["잠들다","to fall asleep","Same as 잠이 들다. 잠들기 전에 = before falling asleep. 자다 is the state of sleeping; 잠들다 is the moment of drifting off.","책을 읽다가 **잠들었어요**.","I fell asleep while reading."],["아무래도","after all; it seems (all things considered)","Speaker's conclusion after thinking it over: <b>아무래도 -는 것 같다</b>. Also \"no matter how you look at it.\"","**아무래도** 커피 때문에 잠을 못 자는 것 같아요.","It seems like I can't sleep because of coffee after all."]],"x":[["바르다","proper, correct, upright","Adjective: <b>바른 자세</b>, 바른 생활 습관. 르 irregular: 발라요. (Not 바르다 = apply cream, a different verb.)","**바른** 자세로 앉으면 허리가 덜 아파요.","Sitting with good posture makes your back hurt less."],["이롭다","beneficial","Formal. <b>몸에 이롭다</b>. ㅂ irregular: 이로워요. Opposite of 해롭다.","녹차는 몸에 **이로운** 성분이 많아요.","Green tea has a lot of beneficial compounds."],["해롭다","harmful","<b>N에 해롭다</b>: 건강에 해롭다. ㅂ irregular: 해로워요.","담배는 건강에 **해로워요**.","Cigarettes are bad for your health."],["해치다","to harm, damage","Transitive verb, takes an object: <b>건강을 해치다</b>. 해롭다 is the adjective \"harmful.\"","무리한 다이어트는 건강을 **해칠** 수 있어요.","Extreme dieting can damage your health."],["몸에 배다","to become second nature, ingrained","배다 = soak in (냄새가 옷에 배다). <b>습관이 몸에 배다</b>.","일찍 일어나는 습관이 **몸에 배어서** 주말에도 6시에 깨요.","Waking early is so ingrained that I wake up at 6 even on weekends."]]}]});
GUIDE.en.push({"n":2,"t":"한국어 학습","en":"Learning Korean","units":[{"n":1,"t":"한국어 학습 목적","g":[{"f":"어찌나 -는지","en":"so (much) X that Y","core":"Emphasizes how extreme something was, then gives the result. <b>어찌나</b> (= 얼마나, more emphatic) intensifies, and -는지 sets up the consequence clause.","forms":[["Verb","어찌나 먹는지 · 어찌나 웃었는지"],["Adjective","어찌나 비싼지 · 어찌나 추웠는지"],["Noun","어찌나 미인인지"]],"rules":["Verb present -는지, adjective present -(으)ㄴ지, past -았/었는지.","The second clause is the result or consequence, often with -았/었어요 or -(으)ㄹ 정도였어요.","Mostly used for things the speaker experienced or saw. It's conversational and expressive.","얼마나 -는지 means the same, and also works with 모르다: 얼마나 맛있는지 몰라요."],"ex":[["한국 드라마가 **어찌나 재미있는지** 밤새 봤어요.","The Korean drama was so fun that I watched it all night."],["그 가수를 **어찌나 좋아했는지** 혼자 한국어를 공부하기 시작했어요.","I liked that singer so much that I started studying Korean on my own."],["시험이 **어찌나 어려웠는지** 반도 못 풀었어요.","The exam was so hard I couldn't even finish half of it."]]},{"f":"-도록¹","en":"so that; in order for","core":"Purpose or goal. The action in the main clause is done so that the -도록 clause happens. Compared with -(으)려고 or -기 위해, it focuses on bringing about a result or state, often for someone else.","forms":[["Verb / adjective stem","들리도록 · 잊지 않도록 · 늦지 않도록 · 건강하도록"]],"rules":["Stem + 도록, regardless of 받침.","Subjects often differ: <b>학생들이 이해하도록</b> 선생님이 천천히 설명했어요.","Very common with negatives: <b>-지 않도록</b> = so as not to.","No tense on the 도록 clause.","Also used for instructions: 내일까지 제출하<b>도록</b> 하세요 (formal command).","Different from -도록² (7과), which means \"to the point that\" and expresses degree."],"ex":[["뒤에 앉은 사람도 잘 **들리도록** 크게 말해 주세요.","Please speak loudly so the people in the back can hear well."],["단어를 **잊어버리지 않도록** 매일 복습해요.","I review every day so I don't forget the words."],["한국 기업에 **취직할 수 있도록** 비즈니스 한국어를 배우고 있어요.","I'm learning business Korean so I can get a job at a Korean company."]]}],"v":[["계기","occasion, trigger (that led to something)","<b>N이/가 계기가 되다</b>, <b>N을/를 계기로</b>. Classic interview question: 무슨 계기로 한국어를 배우게 됐어요?","한국 여행이 **계기**가 되어 한국어를 배우게 됐어요.","A trip to Korea is what got me into learning Korean."],["기업","company, enterprise","More formal or economic than 회사. 대기업 (big company), 중소기업 (SMEs), 기업 문화.","외국 **기업**에서 한국어를 할 수 있는 사람을 찾고 있어요.","Foreign companies are looking for people who speak Korean."],["관련되다","to be related","<b>N와/과 관련된 N</b>, N와 관련이 있다. 관련 = related (관련 자료).","IT와 **관련된** 일을 하고 싶어요.","I want to do work related to IT."],["진출하다","to advance into, enter (a market or field)","<b>해외/시장에 진출하다</b>. Also in sports: 결승에 진출하다 = advance to the finals.","그 회사는 작년에 한국 시장에 **진출했어요**.","That company entered the Korean market last year."],["우연히","by chance","<b>우연히 만나다 / 알게 되다 / 보다</b>. 우연 = coincidence.","유튜브에서 **우연히** 한국 노래를 듣게 됐어요.","I happened to hear a Korean song on YouTube."]],"x":[["개발","development (of products, tech, skills)","개발하다, 앱 개발, 능력 개발. Note: self-improvement is properly spelled <b>자기계발</b> (계발 = cultivating ability), not 자기개발.","저는 게임 **개발**에 관심이 있어요.","I'm interested in game development."],["능력","ability, capability","<b>능력이 있다 / 뛰어나다</b>, 능력을 키우다/기르다. 한국어 능력 시험 = TOPIK.","외국어 **능력**이 있으면 취업에 유리해요.","Having foreign-language ability is an advantage when job-hunting."],["동기","motive, motivation","학습 동기, <b>동기를 부여하다</b> (motivate). Homonym: 동기 = cohort peer (입사 동기).","한국어를 공부하는 **동기**가 뭐예요?","What's your motivation for studying Korean?"],["의사소통","communication","의사 = intention (not doctor). <b>의사소통이 되다 / 안 되다</b>, 의사소통 능력.","이제는 한국 사람과 **의사소통**하는 데 문제가 없어요.","Now I have no trouble communicating with Korean people."],["호기심","curiosity","<b>호기심이 많다</b>, 호기심을 느끼다/갖다, 호기심에 (out of curiosity).","**호기심**에 한글을 배워 봤는데 재미있었어요.","I tried learning Hangeul out of curiosity, and it was fun."],["흥미","interest","<b>흥미가 있다 / 생기다</b>, 흥미를 느끼다/잃다. 흥미롭다 = interesting. A bit more formal than 관심.","역사에 **흥미**가 생겨서 한국 역사 책을 읽고 있어요.","I got interested in history, so I'm reading a book on Korean history."]]},{"n":2,"t":"효과적인 학습 방법","g":[{"f":"-을 게 아니라","en":"rather than doing X, (you should) do Y","core":"Rejects one course of action as not the right approach and suggests a better one. Often used for advice: \"Don't just X, Y instead.\" (게 = 것이)","forms":[["Verb, no 받침","볼 게 아니라 · 외울 게 아니라 (ㄹ-stem)"],["Verb, 받침","읽을 게 아니라 · 앉아 있을 게 아니라"]],"rules":["Verbs only. No tense on the first clause.","The second clause is usually advice or a command/suggestion: -(으)세요, -는 게 좋겠어요, -아/어야 해요, -(으)ㅂ시다.","Often with 그냥 or 무조건 in the first clause to show the rejected way is thoughtless: <b>그냥 외울 게 아니라</b>.","Compare with N이/가 아니라 (not N but M), which works with nouns only."],"ex":[["단어를 그냥 **외울 게 아니라** 문장으로 만들어 보세요.","Rather than just memorizing words, try making sentences with them."],["번역기에 **의존할 게 아니라** 사전을 찾아보는 게 좋아요.","Instead of relying on a translator, it's better to look things up in a dictionary."],["혼자 **고민할 게 아니라** 선생님께 여쭤봐요.","Don't just worry about it alone. Ask the teacher."]]},{"f":"-기에는","en":"for doing X; to X (judging suitability)","core":"Gives a standard of judgment: \"for the purpose of X, it is (too much / not enough / good).\" Typically followed by an evaluation like 좋다, 어렵다, 부족하다, 이르다, 너무 -다.","forms":[["Verb","혼자 먹기에는 · 공부하기에는 · 포기하기에는"]],"rules":["Verb stem + 기에는. Can shorten to <b>-기엔</b> in speech.","The main clause is an evaluation, usually an adjective: 많다, 비싸다, 이르다, 아깝다, 적당하다.","Often implies \"not suitable\": 초보자가 보기에는 어려워요.","Also N이/가 -기에는 for the person doing it: 아이가 읽기에는 어려운 책."],"ex":[["이 교재는 초급 학생이 **공부하기에는** 좀 어려워요.","This textbook is a bit hard for beginners to study with."],["포기하**기에는** 아직 일러요.","It's still too early to give up."],["드라마는 듣기 연습을 **하기에는** 좋지만 문법을 배우**기에는** 부족해요.","Dramas are good for listening practice but not enough for learning grammar."]]}],"v":[["매체","medium, media","대중 매체 (mass media), 다양한 매체를 통해, 영상 매체.","요즘은 다양한 **매체**를 통해 한국어를 배울 수 있어요.","These days you can learn Korean through many different media."],["수준","level, standard","<b>수준이 높다 / 낮다</b>, N에 수준이 맞다, 생활 수준. 자기 수준에 맞는 책 = a book at your level.","제 **수준**에 맞는 책을 고르는 게 어려워요.","It's hard to pick books that match my level."],["효과적","effective","-적 noun: 효과적이다, 효과적인 방법, 효과적으로. 효과 = effect. Compare 효율적 (efficient), 10과.","소리 내서 읽는 것이 발음 연습에 **효과적**이에요.","Reading aloud is effective for pronunciation practice."],["의존하다","to depend on, rely on","<b>N에 의존하다</b>. Often carries a slightly negative sense of over-reliance.","사전에만 **의존하지** 말고 문맥으로 뜻을 추측해 보세요.","Don't rely only on the dictionary. Try guessing the meaning from context."],["상당히","considerably, quite","Formal-ish \"quite, fairly.\" More measured than 아주 or 너무.","한국어 실력이 **상당히** 늘었네요.","Your Korean has improved considerably."],["서서히","gradually, slowly","Slow, steady change: <b>서서히 늘다 / 좋아지다 / 익숙해지다</b>. 점점 is more neutral.","처음에는 힘들었지만 **서서히** 익숙해졌어요.","It was tough at first, but I gradually got used to it."]],"x":[["암기하다","to memorize","Formal or academic. Everyday word: 외우다. 암기력 = memory ability.","시험 전에 단어를 열심히 **암기했어요**.","I memorized vocabulary hard before the test."],["유창하다","fluent","Mostly for languages and speech: <b>유창하게 말하다</b>. 유창한 한국어.","저도 언젠가 한국어를 **유창하게** 하고 싶어요.","I want to speak Korean fluently someday too."],["완벽하다","perfect","완벽하게, 완벽주의자 (perfectionist).","**완벽하게** 말하려고 하지 말고 자신 있게 말해 보세요.","Don't try to speak perfectly. Just speak with confidence."],["향상되다","to improve (level, ability)","Intransitive: <b>실력이 향상되다</b>. Transitive: 실력을 향상시키다. More formal than 늘다.","매일 일기를 쓰니까 쓰기 실력이 **향상됐어요**.","Keeping a daily diary improved my writing."],["꾸준히","steadily, consistently","Regular effort over time: <b>꾸준히 연습하다 / 운동하다</b>.","**꾸준히** 공부하면 누구나 실력이 늘어요.","Anyone improves if they study steadily."]]}]});
GUIDE.en.push({"n":3,"t":"성격과 환경","en":"Personality and environment","units":[{"n":1,"t":"성격","g":[{"f":"-었던 것 같다","en":"I think it was / it seems (it) was (recollection)","core":"A soft, uncertain statement about the past. You're recalling something and aren't 100% sure, or you're being modest or indirect. The -었던 part marks a completed past state or a past that no longer continues.","forms":[["Verb","갔던 것 같다 · 먹었던 것 같다"],["Adjective","조용했던 것 같다 · 작았던 것 같다"],["Noun","학생이었던 것 같다 · 친구였던 것 같다"]],"rules":["Works with verbs, adjectives, and 이다.","Compare: <b>-(으)ㄴ 것 같다</b> (verb past: 간 것 같다 = I think he went) is a guess about a recent event. <b>-었던 것 같다</b> feels more like looking back on something finished, or recalling a past state that's changed.","With adjectives, <b>-었던 것 같다</b> is the natural past guess: 어렸을 때 조용했던 것 같아요.","Great for talking about how your personality used to be."],"ex":[["어렸을 때는 정말 **내성적이었던 것 같아요**.","I think I was really introverted as a kid."],["그 사람을 예전에 어디서 **만났던 것 같은데** 기억이 안 나요.","I think I met that person somewhere before, but I can't remember."],["고등학교 때는 지금보다 더 **활발했던 것 같아요**.","I think I was livelier in high school than I am now."]]},{"f":"-더니¹","en":"(I saw that) X, and then / but now Y","core":"Based on something the speaker observed in the past, followed by a change, contrast, or a result. Two main uses: (1) <b>contrast or change</b>: 어제는 춥더니 오늘은 따뜻하네요. (2) <b>cause and result</b>: 열심히 공부하더니 합격했어요.","forms":[["Verb / adjective stem","춥더니 · 공부하더니 · 조용하더니"],["Noun","학생이더니"]],"rules":["Stem + 더니, regardless of 받침.","Usually about <b>someone else</b> or about the weather and things, not the speaker. You observed it directly.","The subject of both clauses is normally the same.","For the speaker's own action, use <b>-었더니</b> (I did X and found Y), which is a different pattern: 약을 먹었더니 괜찮아졌어요.","No past tense before 더니 in this usage: 춥더니, not 추웠더니 (that would switch to the 었더니 pattern)."],"ex":[["민수 씨는 예전에는 **덜렁거리더니** 요즘은 정말 꼼꼼해졌어요.","Minsu used to be so scatterbrained, but these days he's really meticulous."],["동생이 아침부터 **울먹거리더니** 결국 울음을 터뜨렸어요.","My little brother was on the verge of tears all morning and finally burst out crying."],["어제는 날씨가 **맑더니** 오늘은 비가 오네요.","It was clear yesterday, but today it's raining."]]}],"v":[["무표정","blank expression, expressionless","<b>무표정하다</b>, 무표정한 얼굴, 무표정으로 (with a blank face). 무- = without.","그 사람은 항상 **무표정**이라서 기분을 알 수가 없어요.","He always has a blank face, so you can't tell his mood."],["예전","the past, former times","<b>예전에</b> (in the past), 예전부터 (for a long time), <b>예전 같지 않다</b> (not like before).","**예전**에는 수줍음이 많았는데 지금은 아니에요.","I used to be really shy, but not anymore."],["꼼꼼하다","meticulous, thorough","Positive: careful with details. 꼼꼼하게 확인하다. Opposite: 덜렁거리다.","제 친구는 **꼼꼼해서** 실수를 거의 안 해요.","My friend is meticulous, so she hardly makes mistakes."],["내성적이다","introverted","Opposite: 외향적이다. Neutral description, not negative.","저는 **내성적**이라서 처음 만난 사람과 말하는 게 어려워요.","I'm introverted, so talking to new people is hard for me."],["덜렁거리다","to be careless, scatterbrained","Verb (not adjective): 그는 덜렁거려요. Same as 덜렁대다. A person like this is a 덜렁이.","저는 **덜렁거려서** 우산을 자주 잃어버려요.","I'm so scatterbrained that I often lose my umbrella."],["울먹거리다","to be on the verge of tears","Voice shaking, almost crying. Same as 울먹이다.","아이가 엄마를 찾으면서 **울먹거렸어요**.","The child was on the verge of tears, looking for his mom."],["활발하다","lively, active, outgoing","For personality. Also for activity: 활발한 토론, 활발하게 활동하다.","언니는 성격이 **활발해서** 친구가 많아요.","My sister is outgoing, so she has lots of friends."]],"x":[["느긋하다","easygoing, unhurried, relaxed","Positive or neutral: not rushed. Can become negative if it means too slow.","그는 성격이 **느긋해서** 급한 일이 있어도 화를 안 내요.","He's so easygoing that he doesn't get angry even when things are urgent."],["소극적이다","passive, reserved, hesitant","Hesitant to take part or speak up. Opposite: 적극적이다.","수업 시간에 너무 **소극적**이면 실력이 잘 안 늘어요.","If you're too passive in class, your skills won't improve much."],["수동적이다","passive (only acts when told)","Waits for instructions or reacts rather than acts. Opposite: 능동적이다. 소극적 is about hesitancy; 수동적 is about lack of initiative.","시키는 일만 하는 **수동적**인 태도는 좋지 않아요.","A passive attitude where you only do what you're told isn't good."],["적극적이다","active, proactive, enthusiastic","<b>적극적으로 참여하다</b>. Highly valued in Korean workplaces and schools.","그 학생은 모든 활동에 **적극적**으로 참여해요.","That student actively participates in every activity."],["주도적이다","self-directed, taking the lead","Leading or initiating: 주도적으로 이끌다. 주도하다 = lead.","팀 프로젝트에서 **주도적**인 역할을 맡았어요.","I took a leading role in the team project."]]},{"n":2,"t":"환경의 영향","g":[{"f":"-는다고 해서","en":"just because X (doesn't mean Y)","core":"Rejects an assumed connection: X being true doesn't automatically mean Y. Usually followed by a negative or rhetorical clause: 아니다, -는 것은 아니다, 다 -는 건 아니다.","forms":[["Verb","간다고 해서 · 먹는다고 해서 · 했다고 해서"],["Adjective","비싸다고 해서 · 작다고 해서"],["Noun","학생이라고 해서 · 부자라고 해서"]],"rules":["Uses the reported-speech -ㄴ/는다고, -다고, -(이)라고 forms, so past and future are possible: <b>잘했다고 해서</b>.","The second clause denies the expected result: <b>-는 것은 아니다</b>, 다 -지는 않다, -(으)ㄹ 수는 없다.","Often with 다 or 꼭: 형제라고 해서 성격이 <b>다</b> 같은 건 아니에요.","Can be shortened to <b>-는다고</b> in speech."],"ex":[["형제**라고 해서** 성격이 다 비슷한 건 아니에요.","Just because they're siblings doesn't mean their personalities are all alike."],["조용**하다고 해서** 소심한 사람은 아니에요.","Being quiet doesn't make someone timid."],["부모님이 이기적이**라고 해서** 아이도 이기적으로 자라는 건 아니지요.","Just because the parents are selfish doesn't mean the child grows up selfish."]]},{"f":"처럼","en":"like, as (comparison)","core":"Particle attached to a noun: \"like N, in the same way as N.\" Expresses similarity in manner or degree.","forms":[["Noun","엄마처럼 · 그림처럼 · 바보처럼"],["As adjective","N 같은 N (아빠 같은 사람). 처럼 modifies verbs; 같은 modifies nouns."]],"rules":["<b>N처럼 + verb/adjective</b>: 아빠처럼 키가 커요.","Compare <b>N 같이</b> (same meaning, slightly more casual) and <b>N 같은 N</b> (before nouns).","Common similes: 그림처럼 아름답다, 꿈처럼, 거짓말처럼, 쥐 죽은 듯이 (cf. -는 듯이, 10과).","Can follow other particles: 예전<b>처럼</b>, 지금<b>처럼</b>, 말한 것<b>처럼</b>."],"ex":[["저는 아빠**처럼** 성격이 느긋한 편이에요.","Like my dad, I'm on the easygoing side."],["예전**처럼** 친구들과 자주 만나지 못해요.","I can't meet friends as often as before."],["언니**처럼** 다정한 사람이 되고 싶어요.","I want to become an affectionate person like my sister."]]}],"v":[["불평","complaint, grumbling","<b>불평하다</b>, 불평을 늘어놓다 (pile on complaints). 불평 is complaining out loud; 불만 is the feeling of dissatisfaction.","그는 항상 회사에 대해 **불평**만 해요.","He's always just complaining about his company."],["영향","influence, effect","<b>N에게 영향을 주다 / 미치다 / 받다</b>. 영향력 = influence (10과).","저는 엄마에게 많은 **영향**을 받았어요.","I was greatly influenced by my mom."],["이기적","selfish","-적 noun: 이기적이다, 이기적인 사람. Opposite: 이타적 (altruistic).","**이기적**인 행동은 주변 사람을 힘들게 해요.","Selfish behavior makes things hard for people around you."],["정","affection, attachment (Korean 정)","A warm bond built over time, with no clean English equivalent. <b>정이 많다</b> (warm-hearted), <b>정이 들다</b> (grow attached), 정을 주다.","이 동네에 오래 살아서 **정**이 많이 들었어요.","I've lived in this neighborhood so long I've grown really attached to it."],["평생","lifetime, all one's life","<b>평생 (동안)</b>, 평생 잊지 못하다. Also an adverb: 평생 함께하다.","어렸을 때 배운 습관은 **평생** 가요.","Habits learned in childhood last a lifetime."],["소심하다","timid, faint-hearted","Overly cautious and easily hurt by small things. Slightly negative. Opposite: 대범하다.","저는 **소심해서** 작은 일에도 걱정을 많이 해요.","I'm timid, so I worry a lot even about little things."],["타고나다","to be born with","<b>타고난 성격 / 재능</b>, 성격은 타고나는 걸까요? Key to the nature vs. nurture topic.","그는 음악적 재능을 **타고났어요**.","He was born with musical talent."]],"x":[["긍정적이다","positive","긍정적으로 생각하다. Opposite: 부정적이다.","**긍정적**인 사람과 있으면 기분이 좋아져요.","Being around positive people lifts my mood."],["냉정하다","cold, cool-headed","Two faces: negative (cold-hearted: 냉정한 사람) or neutral-positive (calm and objective: 냉정하게 판단하다).","화가 나도 **냉정하게** 생각하려고 해요.","Even when I'm angry, I try to think calmly."],["다정하다","affectionate, warm, kind","Warmth shown in actions and words. 다정한 말투.","우리 할머니는 언제나 **다정하세요**.","My grandmother is always so warm."],["대범하다","bold, broad-minded","Not bothered by small things. Opposite: 소심하다.","그녀는 **대범해서** 실수해도 금방 털고 일어나요.","She's so unfazed that even when she makes a mistake, she brushes it off quickly."],["모나다","angular, abrasive (personality)","Literally \"having corners.\" <b>모난 성격</b> = prickly. Proverb: 모난 돌이 정 맞는다 (the nail that sticks out gets hammered).","**모난** 성격 때문에 친구와 자주 싸워요.","He often fights with friends because of his prickly personality."],["못되다","mean, nasty, wicked","<b>못된 버릇 / 사람</b>. Written as one word. (못 되다 = can't become, a different meaning.)","친구를 놀리는 건 **못된** 행동이에요.","Teasing your friends is mean."],["부정적이다","negative","부정적인 영향, 부정적으로 생각하다.","**부정적**인 말은 아이에게 나쁜 영향을 줘요.","Negative words have a bad influence on children."],["원만하다","amiable, well-rounded; smooth","For personality and relationships. Also: 문제를 <b>원만하게 해결하다</b> (settle smoothly).","그는 성격이 **원만해서** 누구와도 잘 지내요.","He's easy to get along with, so he's on good terms with everyone."]]}]});
GUIDE.en.push({"n":4,"t":"나의 진로","en":"My career path","units":[{"n":1,"t":"진로 고민","g":[{"f":"-고 보니까","en":"after (doing) X, I realized / found","core":"Once an action was completed, the speaker realized something new, often something they didn't know before or something unexpected. Focus is on discovery after completing one action.","forms":[["Verb","하고 보니까 · 듣고 보니까 · 졸업하고 보니까"],["Noun (이다)","알고 보니까 (= 알고 보니, \"it turns out\")"]],"rules":["Verbs only, no tense before -고.","Compare with <b>-다(가) 보니까</b> (1과): that one is about continuous or repeated action leading to a discovery. -고 보니까 is about completing one action, then discovering.","Short form <b>-고 보니</b> is common, especially <b>알고 보니</b> (as it turns out).","Second clause often has -더라고요, -네요, -었어요."],"ex":[["대학교를 **졸업하고 보니까** 하고 싶은 일이 따로 있었어요.","After graduating, I realized there was something else I wanted to do."],["설명을 **듣고 보니까** 생각보다 간단한 문제였어요.","After hearing the explanation, it turned out to be a simpler problem than I thought."],["**알고 보니** 그 사람이 박람회 담당자였어요.","It turned out that person was the one in charge of the fair."]]},{"f":"-을 텐데","en":"(since) X is probably the case, …","core":"Expresses the speaker's assumption or expectation (텐데 = 터이다 + -ㄴ데) and uses it as background for advice, concern, or a contrasting statement.","forms":[["Verb / adj, no 받침","바쁠 텐데 · 피곤할 텐데"],["Verb / adj, 받침","좋을 텐데 · 많을 텐데"],["Past","했을 텐데 · 왔을 텐데"],["Noun","학생일 텐데 · 주말일 텐데"]],"rules":["Common pattern: <b>assumption + advice</b>: 피곤할 텐데 좀 쉬세요.","Also <b>assumption + contrast</b>: 많이 바쁠 텐데 와 줘서 고마워요.","Ending a sentence with <b>-(으)ㄹ 텐데요</b> shows worry or hope: 비가 오면 안 될 텐데요.","<b>-었을 텐데</b> = \"would have\" (counterfactual): 미리 알았으면 도와줬을 텐데."],"ex":[["취업 준비 때문에 **바쁠 텐데** 너무 무리하지 마세요.","You must be busy preparing for jobs, so don't push yourself too hard."],["혼자 결정하기 **어려울 텐데** 진로 상담을 받아 보세요.","It's probably hard to decide on your own, so try getting career counseling."],["미리 **알았으면** 박람회에 **갔을 텐데** 아쉬워요.","If I'd known in advance, I would have gone to the fair. What a shame."]]}],"v":[["담당자","person in charge","담당하다 = be in charge of. <b>담당자에게 문의하다</b> (contact the person in charge).","자세한 내용은 **담당자**에게 문의하세요.","For details, please contact the person in charge."],["박람회","fair, expo","취업 박람회 (job fair), 유학 박람회, 박람회에 참가하다.","다음 주에 취업 **박람회**가 열려요.","There's a job fair next week."],["부담","burden, pressure","<b>부담이 되다 / 크다</b>, <b>부담을 주다 / 느끼다</b>. 부담스럽다 (10과). Also financial: 비용 부담.","부모님께 경제적인 **부담**을 드리고 싶지 않아요.","I don't want to put a financial burden on my parents."],["일거양득","two birds with one stone","Four-character idiom (사자성어): 一擧兩得. Similar: 꿩 먹고 알 먹고.","운동도 하고 돈도 버니까 **일거양득**이에요.","I get exercise and earn money. It's two birds with one stone."],["진로","career path, future course","<b>진로를 정하다 / 고민하다</b>, 진로 상담 (career counseling).","졸업이 다가오니까 **진로** 고민이 많아요.","Graduation is coming, so I'm worried a lot about my career path."],["시도하다","to try, attempt","Trying something new: <b>새로운 것을 시도하다</b>. More deliberate than 해 보다.","두려워하지 말고 여러 가지 일을 **시도해** 보세요.","Don't be afraid. Try out lots of different things."],["게다가","moreover, on top of that","Adds a further point, usually in the same direction (often piling up good or bad things).","월급이 많고 **게다가** 집에서도 가까워요.","The pay is good, and on top of that it's close to home."]],"x":[["다재다능","multi-talented","多才多能. 다재다능하다, 다재다능한 사람.","그는 노래, 춤, 연기까지 하는 **다재다능**한 사람이에요.","He's a multi-talented person who sings, dances, and even acts."],["상부상조","mutual aid","相扶相助. Helping each other, as in traditional village life.","이웃끼리 **상부상조**하며 사는 게 좋아요.","It's good for neighbors to live helping one another."],["우왕좌왕","going back and forth in confusion","右往左往. 우왕좌왕하다: not knowing what to do, running around.","갑자기 정전이 돼서 사람들이 **우왕좌왕**했어요.","The power suddenly went out, and people ran around in confusion."],["우유부단","indecisive","優柔不斷. 우유부단하다, 우유부단한 성격.","저는 **우유부단**해서 메뉴 하나 고르는 데도 오래 걸려요.","I'm so indecisive it takes me forever just to pick a menu item."],["유비무환","preparedness averts disaster","有備無患. Used when advising preparation.","**유비무환**이라고 미리 자격증을 따 두세요.","As they say, be prepared. Get your certificate in advance."],["작심삼일","resolutions that last three days","作心三日. For failed resolutions.","운동하기로 했는데 또 **작심삼일**이 됐어요.","I resolved to work out, but it fizzled out after three days again."],["전화위복","a blessing in disguise","轉禍爲福. A misfortune that turns into good fortune.","회사에서 떨어진 게 오히려 **전화위복**이 됐어요.","Getting rejected by that company turned out to be a blessing in disguise."]]},{"n":2,"t":"취업 박람회","g":[{"f":"-는지요?","en":"I wonder / may I ask whether…? (very polite question)","core":"A softened, polite question, as if wondering aloud. Common in formal settings like interviews, customer service, and talking to superiors. It sounds less direct than -아/어요?","forms":[["Verb","하는지요 · 있는지요 · 했는지요"],["Adjective","괜찮은지요 · 바쁘신지요"],["Noun","학생인지요 · 언제인지요"]],"rules":["Same forms as -는지: verb -는지요, adjective -(으)ㄴ지요, past -았/었는지요.","Often with honorific -(으)시-: <b>어떻게 되시는지요?</b>","Typical with question words: 언제, 어떻게, 왜, 무엇.","Rising intonation. Very useful phrasing for job fairs and interviews."],"ex":[["실례지만 지원 자격이 어떻게 **되는지요**?","Excuse me, but may I ask what the eligibility requirements are?"],["외국인도 **지원할 수 있는지요**?","I was wondering whether foreigners can apply as well?"],["면접은 언제 **보는지요**?","May I ask when the interview is?"]]},{"f":"-는 경우에","en":"in the case that X; if X","core":"Sets up a hypothetical or specific situation and what happens or should be done in that case. More formal than -(으)면, common in rules, notices, and instructions.","forms":[["Verb (present)","지원하는 경우에 · 늦는 경우에"],["Verb (past/completed)","합격한 경우에 · 잃어버린 경우에"],["Adjective","급한 경우에 · 어려운 경우에"],["Noun","N의 경우에 / N인 경우에 (외국인의 경우에)"]],"rules":["Verb present -는, past -(으)ㄴ, adjective -(으)ㄴ, noun <b>N의 경우(에)</b> or <b>N인 경우(에)</b>.","에 is often dropped: <b>-는 경우</b>.","Often used with 만약, 혹시.","Feels official, so it's common in job postings: 경력자인 경우 우대합니다."],"ex":[["면접에 **늦는 경우에는** 미리 담당자에게 연락하세요.","If you're going to be late to the interview, contact the person in charge in advance."],["한국어 능력 시험 4급 이상인 **경우** 우대합니다.","Applicants with TOPIK level 4 or above will be given preference."],["외국인**의 경우에는** 비자 서류가 필요해요.","In the case of foreigners, visa documents are required."]]}],"v":[["답변","answer, response","More formal than 대답. <b>질문에 답변하다</b>, 답변을 드리다. Used in interviews and customer service.","면접관의 질문에 자신 있게 **답변했어요**.","I answered the interviewer's questions confidently."],["영업","sales; business operation","영업팀 (sales team), 영업직, <b>영업 시간</b> (business hours), 영업 중 (open).","저는 **영업** 쪽 일에 관심이 있어요.","I'm interested in sales work."],["자격","qualification, eligibility","<b>자격이 있다</b>, 지원 자격, 자격증 (certificate), 자격을 갖추다.","이 일은 특별한 **자격**이 필요 없어요.","This job doesn't require any special qualifications."],["지원자","applicant","지원하다 = apply (支援 support is a homonym). 지원서 = application form.","올해는 **지원자**가 작년보다 많아요.","There are more applicants this year than last year."],["쪽","side, direction; field, area","이쪽/저쪽, and colloquially a field: <b>마케팅 쪽 일</b>, 디자인 쪽으로. Also = page.","어느 **쪽**으로 진로를 정할지 고민 중이에요.","I'm thinking about which direction to take my career."],["대하다","to treat; (N에 대해) about","<b>N에 대해(서)</b> = about, regarding. <b>사람을 친절하게 대하다</b> = treat people kindly.","회사에 **대해서** 궁금한 점이 있으면 물어보세요.","If you have any questions about the company, ask."]],"x":[["가치관","values, worldview","<b>가치관이 다르다 / 맞다</b>. Values that guide judgment.","결혼할 때는 **가치관**이 잘 맞는 게 중요해요.","When you marry, it's important that your values match."],["근무지","place of work","Location of employment: 근무지가 서울이다, 근무지 변경.","**근무지**가 집에서 너무 멀어서 고민이에요.","The workplace is too far from home, so I'm torn."],["발전","development, progress","<b>발전하다</b>, 발전 가능성 (growth potential), 경제 발전.","이 회사는 **발전** 가능성이 높아 보여요.","This company seems to have high growth potential."],["복지","welfare; employee benefits","사내 복지, <b>복지가 좋다</b>. Also social welfare: 복지 정책.","월급보다 **복지**를 더 중요하게 생각해요.","I think benefits are more important than salary."],["연봉","annual salary","<b>연봉이 높다</b>, 연봉 협상 (salary negotiation). 월급 = monthly pay.","**연봉**은 회사 규정에 따릅니다.","Salary is according to company policy."]]}]});
GUIDE.en.push({"n":5,"t":"생활 속의 경제","en":"Economics in daily life","units":[{"n":1,"t":"소비 형태","g":[{"f":"-는걸요","en":"but actually…; (mild counterpoint or realization)","core":"Gently pushes back on what the other person said by giving a fact that goes against their view or expectation. Softer than a flat contradiction. Second use: light surprise or admiration at something just noticed.","forms":[["Verb (present)","가는걸요 · 먹는걸요"],["Adjective (present)","비싼걸요 · 많은걸요"],["있다 / 없다","재미있는걸요 · 없는걸요"],["Past (all)","갔는걸요 · 비쌌는걸요"],["Noun","3만 원인걸요 · 학생이었는걸요"]],"rules":["Falling or flat intonation.","Don't confuse with <b>-(으)ㄹ걸요</b>, which is a guess with rising intonation: 아마 자고 있을걸요?","Statements only, not questions or requests.","Often follows 그래도, 그런데, 벌써, which reinforces the \"but actually\" feel.","Friendly 존댓말. Contradicting a boss or teacher this way can sound a bit cheeky.","Textbooks write it attached: -는걸요."],"ex":[["A: 이 가방 사지 그래요? B: 너무 **비싼걸요**.","A: Why don't you buy this bag? B: It's way too expensive, though."],["그래도 새로 사는 것보다 대여하는 게 더 **저렴한걸요**.","Still, renting is cheaper than buying new."],["생각보다 요리를 잘하**는걸요**!","Wow, you cook better than I expected!"]]},{"f":"-게요?","en":"(so) you're going to…? / then you mean…?","core":"A question about the listener's intention or the logical consequence of what they said. Two common uses: (1) \"What are you going to do / use it for?\" (뭐 하게요?) (2) \"Then you'd end up…?\" Questioning an implied result, often with surprise.","forms":[["Verb stem","하게요? · 사게요? · 먹게요? · 버리게요?"]],"rules":["Verb stem + 게요? regardless of 받침. Rising intonation.","Mainly for the listener's intention or plan. Use it in conversation, often with 왜, 뭐, 어떻게, 그럼.","<b>뭐 하게요?</b> = \"What for?\" Very common when someone asks to borrow or buy something.","<b>그럼 + -게요?</b> questions a consequence: 그럼 혼자 다 먹게요?","Casual form: <b>-게?</b>"],"ex":[["A: 돈 좀 빌려줄 수 있어요? B: 갑자기 왜요? 뭐 **사게요**?","A: Can you lend me some money? B: Why all of a sudden? What are you going to buy?"],["이 소파를 그냥 **버리게요**? 수거료도 내야 하는데요.","You're just going to throw out this sofa? You'll have to pay a collection fee, though."],["그렇게 다 사면 이번 달 생활비는 어떻게 **하게요**?","If you buy all that, what are you going to do about living expenses this month?"]]}],"v":[["수거료","collection fee","For picking up waste or large items: 대형 폐기물 수거료. 수거하다 = collect. -료 = fee (사용료, 수수료).","냉장고를 버리려면 **수거료**를 내야 해요.","You have to pay a collection fee to throw out a fridge."],["대여하다","to rent (out), lend","Formal or business for 빌리다. Rental services: 자전거/정장 대여.","여행 갈 때 캐리어를 **대여했어요**.","I rented a suitcase for my trip."],["들이다²","to spend (money, time, effort)","<b>돈/시간/공/노력을 들이다</b>. 돈을 들이지 않고 = without spending money. (들이다¹ = 습관을 들이다.)","돈을 많이 **들이지** 않고 방을 꾸몄어요.","I decorated my room without spending much money."],["아쉽다","regrettable, a shame; lacking","A soft disappointment: something was missing or ended too soon. ㅂ irregular: 아쉬워요. Not as strong as 후회하다.","세일이 어제 끝나서 **아쉬워요**.","It's a shame the sale ended yesterday."],["저렴하다","inexpensive, affordable","A polite, neutral word for 싸다 with no \"cheap quality\" nuance. Common in ads.","이 가게는 품질도 좋고 가격도 **저렴해요**.","This store has good quality and affordable prices."],["포함되다","to be included","<b>N에 포함되다</b>, 배송비 포함 (shipping included). Transitive: 포함하다.","가격에 세금이 **포함돼** 있어요?","Is tax included in the price?"]],"x":[["고가","high price","高價. 고가의 제품, 고가 브랜드. Opposite: 저가.","**고가**의 물건일수록 꼼꼼히 비교해 보세요.","The more expensive the item, the more carefully you should compare."],["공급","supply","공급하다, 공급이 부족하다. Paired with 수요.","**공급**이 줄어서 가격이 올랐어요.","Supply dropped, so prices went up."],["생산","production","생산하다, 대량 생산 (mass production), 생산자 (producer).","이 공장에서는 하루에 천 개를 **생산**해요.","This factory produces a thousand units a day."],["수요","demand","<b>수요와 공급</b> (supply and demand). 수요가 늘다/많다.","여름에는 에어컨 **수요**가 많아요.","Demand for air conditioners is high in summer."],["저가","low price","低價. <b>저가 항공</b> (budget airline), 저가 상품.","**저가** 항공을 이용하면 싸게 여행할 수 있어요.","You can travel cheaply if you use budget airlines."],["구매하다","to purchase","Formal 사다. 구매자 (buyer), 온라인 구매, 구매 후기 (purchase review).","온라인으로 **구매하면** 할인을 받을 수 있어요.","You can get a discount if you purchase online."]]},{"n":2,"t":"결제 방식","g":[{"f":"-었어야 하다","en":"should have (done)","core":"Expresses regret or criticism about something that wasn't done in the past: \"should have X.\" In the negative: <b>-지 말았어야 하다</b> = shouldn't have.","forms":[["Verb, ㅏ/ㅗ","샀어야 했다 · 왔어야 했다"],["Verb, other","먹었어야 했다 · 확인했어야 했다"],["Negative","사지 말았어야 했다"]],"rules":["Usually ends as <b>-었어야 했어요</b> (past regret) or <b>-었어야 해요</b> (should've, said now).","About yourself = regret. About others = criticism or reproach.","Often paired with 미리, 진작, 그때.","Close in meaning to -(으)ㄹ걸 그랬다 (I wish I had), which is softer and more personal."],"ex":[["할부로 사기 전에 이자를 **확인했어야 했어요**.","I should have checked the interest before buying on installments."],["그렇게 비싼 걸 충동적으로 **사지 말았어야 했는데**.","I shouldn't have bought something that expensive on impulse."],["간편 결제 앱을 미리 **설치했어야 했어요**.","I should have installed the easy-pay app in advance."]]},{"f":"-다가 보면","en":"if you keep doing X, (eventually) Y","core":"A general prediction or advice: continuing an action over time will lead to a result. Often encouraging (\"you'll get used to it\") or warning (\"you'll end up overspending\").","forms":[["Verb","쓰다(가) 보면 · 살다(가) 보면 · 하다(가) 보면"]],"rules":["Verbs only. 가 often dropped: <b>-다 보면</b>.","Second clause is future, general, or advice: -게 될 거예요, -(으)ㄹ 수 있어요, -기 마련이에요, -아/어요.","No past tense in the second clause. For past results use <b>-다 보니까</b> (1과).","Great for encouragement: 계속 하다 보면 잘하게 될 거예요."],"ex":[["카드를 생각 없이 **쓰다 보면** 돈이 금방 없어져요.","If you keep using your card without thinking, your money disappears fast."],["처음엔 어렵지만 **사용하다 보면** 익숙해질 거예요.","It's hard at first, but if you keep using it, you'll get used to it."],["한국에 **살다 보면** 이런 일이 종종 생겨요.","When you live in Korea, this kind of thing happens now and then."]]}],"v":[["가맹점","affiliated store, franchise branch","Franchise locations or stores that accept a certain card or payment: <b>가맹점 할인</b>, 카드 가맹점.","이 카드는 **가맹점**에서 10% 할인돼요.","This card gets 10% off at affiliated stores."],["시스템","system","Loanword, used as in English: 결제 시스템, 시스템을 도입하다.","새 결제 **시스템** 때문에 처음에는 좀 헷갈렸어요.","The new payment system was a bit confusing at first."],["표시","mark, label, indication","<b>표시하다</b>, 가격 표시 (price tag), 표시가 되어 있다. Also shows feelings: 감사의 표시.","카드 사용 가능 **표시**가 있는 가게에서만 돼요.","It only works at stores with the card-accepted sign."],["도입하다","to introduce, adopt (a system or policy)","For bringing in systems or policies: <b>제도/시스템을 도입하다</b>. Not for introducing people (that's 소개하다).","그 식당은 키오스크 주문을 **도입했어요**.","That restaurant introduced kiosk ordering."],["당분간","for the time being, for a while","<b>당분간 -(으)ㄹ 예정이다</b>. A temporary period: 당분간 휴업 (temporarily closed).","공사 때문에 **당분간** 현금만 받습니다.","We're accepting cash only for the time being due to construction."],["이래저래","for one reason or another; this and that","Several small reasons combined: <b>이래저래 바쁘다 / 돈이 들다</b>.","이번 달은 **이래저래** 돈 쓸 일이 많았어요.","This month there was one thing after another to spend money on."]],"x":[["선불","prepayment","先拂. 선불로 내다, <b>선불 카드</b> (prepaid card), 선불 요금제.","이 식당은 **선불**이에요. 먼저 계산하세요.","This restaurant is pay-first. Please pay up front."],["할부","installment payment","<b>3개월 할부로 사다</b>. Opposite: 일시불 (lump sum). Cashiers ask: 일시불로 해 드릴까요?","노트북을 6개월 **할부**로 샀어요.","I bought the laptop on six-month installments."],["후불","postpayment, pay later","後拂. 후불 교통카드, 후불 결제.","이 교통카드는 **후불**이라서 다음 달에 돈이 나가요.","This transit card is postpaid, so the money comes out next month."],["지불하다","to pay","Formal or written: <b>요금/비용을 지불하다</b>. Everyday: 내다, 계산하다.","현금으로 **지불하면** 할인해 드려요.","We'll give you a discount if you pay in cash."],["가상 계좌 입금","virtual account deposit","Common Korean online-shopping payment: a temporary bank account number to transfer to. 입금하다 = deposit.","**가상 계좌**로 **입금**하면 주문이 완료돼요.","The order is complete once you deposit to the virtual account."],["간편 결제","easy / simple payment","Mobile pay services like 카카오페이, 네이버페이, 삼성페이.","요즘은 지갑 없이 **간편 결제**로 다 해요.","These days I do everything with mobile pay, no wallet."]]}]});
GUIDE.en.push({"n":6,"t":"의사소통과 표현","en":"Communication and expression","units":[{"n":1,"t":"불평과 불만","g":[{"f":"까지","en":"even (on top of everything else)","core":"Beyond its basic meaning \"until / up to,\" 까지 can mean \"even\": adding something extreme or unexpected to a list, often when complaining. \"Not only that, but even X.\"","forms":[["Noun","너까지 · 주말까지 · 밤늦게까지"],["With particles","나한테까지 · 동생까지도"]],"rules":["Attaches to nouns, and can stack with other particles: <b>나한테까지</b>.","Often follows a list of complaints: 비도 오고 바람도 불고, 우산<b>까지</b> 잃어버렸어요.","Similar to 마저 and 조차. 까지 can be positive or negative; 조차 and 마저 are usually negative.","Can add 도 for emphasis: <b>까지도</b>."],"ex":[["옆집 사람이 음악을 크게 틀고, 밤에는 노래**까지** 불러요.","My neighbor blasts music, and at night he even sings."],["친구가 약속에 늦었는데 사과**까지** 안 했어요.","My friend was late and didn't even apologize."],["가족들**까지** 제 말을 무시하니까 정말 속상해요.","Even my family ignores what I say, and it really upsets me."]]},{"f":"-더라고요","en":"(I noticed / saw that) X (personal observation)","core":"Reports something the speaker personally saw, heard, or felt in the past, shared with the listener as new information. It sounds like \"I found that…\" or \"You know, it was…\"","forms":[["Verb / adjective","가더라고요 · 맛있더라고요 · 불친절하더라고요"],["Past completed","끝났더라고요 · 왔더라고요"],["Noun","학생이더라고요 · 외국인이더라고요"]],"rules":["Stem + 더라고요. Past -았/었더라고요 = when I saw it, it had already happened.","Based on direct experience. You can't use it for things you only heard secondhand (use -대요).","Normally not for your own actions (\"I went\" ✗ 제가 가더라고요), except for your own feelings or reactions: 저도 모르게 눈물이 <b>나더라고요</b>.","Casual: <b>-더라</b>."],"ex":[["그 식당 직원이 정말 **불친절하더라고요**.","The staff at that restaurant were really unfriendly."],["가서 보니까 이미 문을 **닫았더라고요**.","When I went, they had already closed."],["지하철에서 큰 소리로 통화하는 사람이 **많더라고요**.","There were a lot of people talking loudly on the phone on the subway."]]}],"v":[["매너","manners, etiquette","Loanword, common in everyday Korean: <b>매너가 좋다 / 없다</b>, 비매너 (bad manners), 매너 있게.","공공장소에서는 **매너**를 지켜야 해요.","You should mind your manners in public places."],["무시하다","to ignore; to look down on","Two senses: disregard (말을 무시하다) and belittle (사람을 무시하다). The second is stronger and very insulting.","제 의견을 계속 **무시해서** 기분이 나빴어요.","He kept ignoring my opinion, which made me feel bad."],["배려하다","to be considerate of","<b>N을/를 배려하다</b>, 배려심 (consideration). Core Korean social value.","다른 사람을 **배려하는** 마음이 중요해요.","A considerate attitude toward others is important."],["불쾌하다","unpleasant, offended, displeased","More formal or stronger than 기분 나쁘다. 불쾌감 = displeasure.","반말을 들어서 좀 **불쾌했어요**.","I was a bit offended to be spoken to in 반말."],["지나치다","(1) excessive; (2) to pass by","(1) Adjective: 지나친 간섭, 지나치게 (excessively). (2) Verb: 정류장을 지나치다 (miss the stop).","그건 좀 **지나친** 행동이었던 것 같아요.","I think that was a bit excessive."],["가만히","still, quietly; without doing anything","<b>가만히 있다</b> = stay still, or keep quiet without reacting. 가만히 두다 = leave alone.","부당한 일을 당하면 **가만히** 있지 말고 말하세요.","If you're treated unfairly, don't just stay quiet. Speak up."]],"x":[["갈등","conflict","<b>갈등이 생기다</b>, 갈등을 해결하다/해소하다. 세대 갈등 (generational conflict).","룸메이트와 청소 문제로 **갈등**이 생겼어요.","I had a conflict with my roommate over cleaning."],["감정","emotion, feeling","<b>감정을 표현하다 / 조절하다 / 숨기다</b>, 감정적 (emotional).","화가 나도 **감정**을 조절하려고 노력해요.","Even when angry, I try to control my emotions."],["의사","intention, will","(Not doctor.) <b>의사를 전달하다 / 밝히다</b>, 의사소통. Formal.","분명하게 자기 **의사**를 표현하는 게 좋아요.","It's good to express your intentions clearly."],["해소","relief, resolution","For stress or conflict: <b>스트레스 해소</b>, 갈등 해소, 해소하다.","저는 운동으로 스트레스를 **해소**해요.","I relieve stress through exercise."],["간섭하다","to interfere, meddle","<b>N에 간섭하다</b>, 사생활에 간섭하다. Negative.","제 일에 너무 **간섭하지** 마세요.","Please don't meddle in my business so much."],["겪다","to go through, experience (hardship)","Used for difficulties: <b>어려움 / 갈등 / 문화 차이를 겪다</b>. 경험하다 is more neutral.","처음 한국에 왔을 때 문화 차이를 많이 **겪었어요**.","When I first came to Korea, I went through a lot of culture shock."],["전달하다","to convey, deliver","<b>메시지/의견/마음을 전달하다</b>. Passive: 전달되다 (9과).","제 마음이 잘 **전달됐으면** 좋겠어요.","I hope my feelings come across well."],["피하다","to avoid","<b>N을/를 피하다</b>, 비를 피하다, 눈을 피하다. 피할 수 없다 = unavoidable.","싸우기 싫어서 그 사람을 **피했어요**.","I didn't want to fight, so I avoided that person."]]},{"n":2,"t":"위로와 격려","g":[{"f":"-는지","en":"how / whether / what… (embedded question)","core":"Turns a question into a clause inside a larger sentence: \"I know how hard it is,\" \"I don't know whether…\" In comfort and encouragement, it often pairs with 얼마나 to show sympathy: 얼마나 힘든지 알아요.","forms":[["Verb","하는지 · 했는지 · 할지 (future)"],["Adjective","힘든지 · 속상한지 · 힘들었는지"],["Noun","누구인지 · 무엇인지"]],"rules":["Verb present -는지, adjective -(으)ㄴ지, past -았/었는지, future -(으)ㄹ지.","Followed by verbs of knowing, wondering, or asking: 알다, 모르다, 궁금하다, 물어보다, 생각하다.","<b>얼마나 -는지 모르다</b> = \"you have no idea how…\" (emphatic): 얼마나 걱정했는지 몰라요.","Don't confuse with <b>-(으)ㄴ 지</b> + time (spaced), which means \"since\": 한국에 온 지 3년 됐어요."],"ex":[["네가 지금 얼마나 **속상한지** 잘 알아.","I know how upset you are right now."],["시험 결과가 나왔다는 얘기를 듣고 얼마나 **걱정했는지** 몰라요.","You have no idea how worried I was when I heard the results were out."],["무엇이 문제**인지** 같이 생각해 봐요.","Let's think together about what the problem is."]]},{"f":"-겠지요","en":"surely / probably X, right? (hopeful assumption)","core":"The speaker's presumption (-겠-) plus seeking agreement (-지요). In comfort and encouragement, it expresses a hopeful expectation: \"Things will surely get better, right?\" Also used to guess another person's feelings sympathetically.","forms":[["Present / future","좋아지겠지요 · 힘들겠지요"],["Past","힘들었겠지요 · 놀랐겠지요"],["Noun","학생이겠지요"]],"rules":["Stem + 겠지요. Past: <b>-았/었겠지요</b> (must have been).","Shortened <b>-겠죠</b> is very common in speech.","Comfort: <b>곧 괜찮아지겠지요</b>. Empathy: <b>많이 힘들었겠지요</b>.","Less certain than -(으)ㄹ 거예요. It invites the listener to agree."],"ex":[["열심히 했으니까 좋은 결과가 **있겠지요**.","You worked hard, so surely you'll get a good result."],["떨어져서 많이 **속상했겠지요**. 다음에는 꼭 붙을 거예요.","You must have been really upset to fail. You'll definitely pass next time."],["시간이 지나면 다 **괜찮아지겠죠**.","With time, everything will be fine, right?"]]}],"v":[["심정","feelings, state of mind","Heavier, more formal than 마음 or 기분. <b>그 심정 이해해요</b> (I understand how you feel). 답답한 심정.","시험에 떨어진 친구의 **심정**을 알 것 같아요.","I think I understand how my friend who failed the exam feels."],["연속","consecutive, in a row","<b>3년 연속</b>, 연속으로, 연속해서.","면접에서 세 번 **연속**으로 떨어졌어요.","I failed interviews three times in a row."],["의욕","drive, motivation, will (to do)","<b>의욕이 생기다 / 없다 / 넘치다</b>, 의욕을 잃다. More like energy to act than 동기 (reason).","요즘 아무것도 하기 싫고 **의욕**이 없어요.","Lately I don't feel like doing anything. I have no drive."],["따다","to obtain, earn; to pick","Get qualifications or achievements: <b>자격증 / 점수 / 메달을 따다</b>. Also 과일을 따다 (pick fruit).","드디어 운전면허를 **땄어요**!","I finally got my driver's license!"],["딱","exactly; just; firmly","<b>딱 한 번</b> (just once), 딱 맞다 (fits perfectly), 딱 잘라 말하다 (say flatly). Very common.","**딱** 한 번만 더 해 보세요.","Try just one more time."],["분명히","clearly; surely, definitely","Both clarity (분명히 말하다) and certainty (분명히 잘될 거예요).","너는 **분명히** 잘할 수 있을 거야.","You'll definitely do well."]],"x":[["격려하다","to encourage","<b>N을/를 격려하다</b>, 격려의 말, 격려를 받다.","선생님이 저를 많이 **격려해** 주셨어요.","My teacher encouraged me a lot."],["공감하다","to empathize, relate","<b>N에 공감하다</b>, 공감 능력, 공감이 가다 (be relatable).","친구의 이야기에 정말 **공감했어요**.","I could really relate to my friend's story."],["속상하다","upset, distressed, hurt","Everyday emotional pain or frustration. Very common, softer than 화나다.","열심히 준비했는데 결과가 안 좋아서 **속상해요**.","I prepared so hard but the result was bad, so I'm upset."],["우울하다","depressed, gloomy, down","Everyday mood (비가 와서 우울해요) and clinical (우울증 = depression).","날씨가 흐리면 기분이 **우울해져요**.","When the weather's gray, I start feeling down."],["지치다","to be exhausted, worn out","Physically or emotionally drained, usually over time: <b>일에 지치다</b>, 지친 몸. Stronger than 피곤하다.","매일 야근을 해서 너무 **지쳤어요**.","I work overtime every day, so I'm completely worn out."]]}]});
GUIDE.en.push({"n":7,"t":"일상생활","en":"Daily life","units":[{"n":1,"t":"공공질서","g":[{"f":"-도록²","en":"to the point that; until","core":"Expresses degree or extent: the main action was done so much (or for so long) that the 도록 clause happened. Usually describes a time passing or a physical, visible result.","forms":[["Verb / adjective stem","새도록 · 넘도록 · 쉬도록 · 아프도록"]],"rules":["Stem + 도록 regardless of 받침.","No tense on the 도록 clause: never 지났도록 or 쉬었도록.","Time passing: <b>밤이 새도록</b>, 밤늦도록, 몇 시간이 지나도록.","Physical result showing degree: <b>목이 쉬도록</b>, 배가 터지도록, 눈물이 나도록.","Often with a negative: \"even after X, still not…\": 한 시간이 지나도록 연락이 없어요.","The 도록 clause usually has its own subject (목이, 밤이).","Set phrases: 죽도록, 귀가 따갑도록, 입이 닳도록.","Different from -도록¹ (2과), which means \"so that\" and expresses purpose."],"ex":[["옆집 개가 밤이 **새도록** 짖어서 한숨도 못 잤어요.","The neighbor's dog barked all night until dawn, so I didn't sleep a wink."],["목이 **쉬도록** 노래를 불렀어요.","I sang until my voice went hoarse."],["30분이 **지나도록** 버스가 안 와요.","Thirty minutes have gone by and the bus still hasn't come."]]},{"f":"만이라도","en":"at least (just) X","core":"만 (only) + 이라도 (even if it's). Sets a minimum the speaker would accept or asks for: \"if not everything, then at least X.\"","forms":[["Noun","조금만이라도 · 한 번만이라도 · 주말만이라도"],["Verb (via -기만이라도)","듣기만이라도 · 와 주기만이라도"]],"rules":["Attaches to nouns or quantity expressions: <b>한 번만이라도</b>, 오늘만이라도, 5분만이라도.","With verbs: <b>-기만이라도 하다</b>: 얼굴을 보기만이라도 하고 싶어요.","The second clause is usually a request, wish, or suggestion: -아/어 주세요, -(으)면 좋겠다, -아/어야지요.","Implies the ideal would be more, but this minimum is acceptable."],"ex":[["다른 건 몰라도 공공장소에서**만이라도** 조용히 해 주세요.","I won't ask anything else, but at least be quiet in public places."],["반려동물을 산책시킬 때 목줄**만이라도** 꼭 해 주세요.","When walking your pet, please at least use a leash."],["바쁘더라도 **하루에 10분만이라도** 운동하세요.","Even if you're busy, exercise for at least 10 minutes a day."]]}],"v":[["목줄","leash, collar","For pets: <b>목줄을 하다 / 채우다</b>. Required by law for dogs in public in Korea.","공원에서는 반려견에게 **목줄**을 꼭 해야 해요.","You must put a leash on your dog in the park."],["반려동물","companion animal, pet","Now preferred over 애완동물 (which implies a plaything). 반려견 = dog, 반려묘 = cat.","**반려동물**을 키우는 사람이 점점 늘고 있어요.","More and more people are raising pets."],["다가오다","to approach, come near","Physical (사람이 다가오다) or time (시험이 다가오다). Opposite: 멀어지다.","큰 개가 갑자기 **다가와서** 깜짝 놀랐어요.","A big dog suddenly came up to me and I was startled."],["짖다","to bark","For dogs: <b>개가 짖다</b>. 멍멍 짖다.","밤마다 옆집 개가 **짖어서** 시끄러워요.","The neighbor's dog barks every night. It's noisy."],["책임지다","to take responsibility","<b>N을/를 책임지다</b>. 책임 = responsibility (책임감, 10과).","반려동물을 키우면 끝까지 **책임져야** 해요.","If you raise a pet, you have to take responsibility to the end."],["마구","recklessly, wildly, at random","Done carelessly or excessively: <b>마구 버리다 / 뛰다 / 먹다</b>. Same as 막 (colloquial).","길에 쓰레기를 **마구** 버리면 안 돼요.","You shouldn't throw trash around on the street."],["몇몇","some, a few (people or things)","<b>몇몇 사람들</b>. Like 일부. Points to a small group without numbers.","**몇몇** 사람들 때문에 공원이 더러워졌어요.","The park got dirty because of a few people."],["오히려","rather, on the contrary","Result opposite to expectation: \"Instead of getting better, it got worse.\"","사과는커녕 **오히려** 저한테 화를 냈어요.","Far from apologizing, he actually got angry at me."]],"x":[["공공질서","public order","<b>공공질서를 지키다</b> (obey public order).","모두가 **공공질서**를 지키면 살기 좋은 사회가 돼요.","If everyone respects public order, society becomes a better place to live."],["고성방가하다","to make a loud racket (singing or shouting in public)","高聲放歌. Mostly used about drunk people at night; can be a legal offense.","밤늦게 **고성방가하는** 사람들 때문에 잠을 못 잤어요.","I couldn't sleep because of people singing and shouting late at night."],["새치기하다","to cut in line","<b>줄을 서다</b> (stand in line) vs. 새치기하다. Considered very rude.","줄을 서 있는데 누가 **새치기했어요**.","I was standing in line and someone cut in."],["무단 횡단하다","to jaywalk","무단 = without permission, 횡단 = crossing. 횡단보도 = crosswalk.","**무단 횡단하면** 위험하고 벌금도 내야 해요.","Jaywalking is dangerous, and you have to pay a fine."],["신경을 쓰다","to pay attention to, care about; to worry","<b>N에 신경(을) 쓰다</b>. 신경 쓰지 마세요 = don't worry about it. 신경이 쓰이다 = to bother you.","다른 사람에게 피해를 주지 않도록 **신경을 써야** 해요.","You need to be careful not to cause trouble for others."]]},{"n":2,"t":"맛집","g":[{"f":"-길래","en":"since / because (I saw that) X, I did Y","core":"A reason based on something the speaker noticed or heard, followed by the speaker's reaction or action. Feels natural and conversational: \"I saw X, so I did Y.\"","forms":[["Verb / adjective","맛있길래 · 사람이 많길래 · 하길래"],["Past","왔길래 · 끝났길래"],["Noun","맛집이길래 · 세일이길래"]],"rules":["Stem + 길래. Past: -았/었길래.","The reason is usually something outside the speaker (another person, a situation). The result is the speaker's own action.","The second clause can't be a command or suggestion (✗ 맛있길래 가세요). Use -(으)니까 for that.","Also used in questions asking for reasons: <b>뭘 먹었길래</b> 배가 아파요? (What on earth did you eat that…?)"],"ex":[["줄이 **길길래** 맛집인 줄 알고 저도 서 봤어요.","There was a long line, so I figured it was a good restaurant and got in line too."],["입소문이 **났길래** 한번 가 봤는데 정말 맛있더라고요.","I heard it was getting buzz, so I tried it, and it was really good."],["도대체 뭘 **넣었길래** 이렇게 고소해요?","What on earth did you put in this to make it so nutty?"]]},{"f":"-던걸요","en":"I found that X, actually (recollection + counterpoint)","core":"Combines -더- (recalling what the speaker experienced) with -ㄴ걸요 (mild counterpoint or surprise, 5과). The speaker reports a past personal impression, often one that goes against the listener's expectation.","forms":[["Verb / adjective","맛있던걸요 · 사람이 많던걸요 · 잘하던걸요"],["Past completed","닫았던걸요 · 끝났던걸요"],["Noun","맛집이던걸요"]],"rules":["Stem + 던걸요. Past completed: -았/었던걸요.","Based on direct experience. You saw or tasted it yourself.","Often contradicts or surprises: A: 그 집 별로래요. B: 저는 <b>맛있던걸요</b>.","Compare: -는걸요 (present fact) vs. -던걸요 (something I experienced back then)."],"ex":[["A: 그 식당 비싸지 않아요? B: 아니요, 생각보다 **저렴하던걸요**.","A: Isn't that place expensive? B: No, it was cheaper than I expected."],["어제 가 보니까 벌써 문을 **닫았던걸요**.","When I went yesterday, it had already closed, you know."],["처음엔 느끼할 줄 알았는데 의외로 **담백하던걸요**.","I thought it'd be greasy, but it was surprisingly light."]]}],"v":[["비결","secret (to success)","<b>N의 비결</b>, 맛의 비결, 성공 비결. Not a hidden secret (that's 비밀), but a key technique.","이 집 김치찌개 맛의 **비결**이 뭐예요?","What's the secret to this place's kimchi stew?"],["입소문","word of mouth","<b>입소문이 나다</b> (get buzz), 입소문을 타다 (spread by word of mouth).","그 빵집은 **입소문**이 나서 손님이 많아졌어요.","That bakery got popular through word of mouth, and now it has lots of customers."],["최근","recently; latest","<b>최근에</b>, 최근 몇 년 (the past few years), 최근 뉴스. More formal than 요즘.","**최근**에 이 근처에 새 식당이 생겼어요.","A new restaurant opened near here recently."],["고소하다","nutty, savory (sesame, roasted)","Taste of sesame oil, roasted nuts, or fresh-baked bread. Fun extra senses: \"serves you right\" (gloating), and homonym 고소하다 = to sue.","참기름을 넣으니까 **고소해요**.","It's nutty because I added sesame oil."],["꼽히다","to be ranked (among), counted as","<b>N(으)로 꼽히다</b>, 최고의 맛집으로 꼽히다. Active: 꼽다.","이곳은 서울 최고의 냉면집으로 **꼽혀요**.","This place is considered one of the best naengmyeon restaurants in Seoul."],["담백하다","light, clean (not greasy or heavy)","Positive taste word for simple, non-oily food. Also describes personality (plain, unpretentious).","이 국물은 기름기가 없어서 **담백해요**.","This broth isn't oily, so it tastes light and clean."],["붐비다","to be crowded","<b>사람들로 붐비다</b>. Places, not people: 식당이 붐비다.","점심시간에는 식당이 직장인들로 **붐벼요**.","At lunchtime, the restaurant is packed with office workers."],["색다르다","unusual, novel, different","Different in an interesting, fresh way. Positive: <b>색다른 맛 / 경험</b>.","오늘은 **색다른** 음식을 먹어 보고 싶어요.","I want to try something different today."]],"x":[["느끼하다","greasy, rich, heavy; (people) cheesy, sleazy","Food: oily or creamy overload (often negative). People: 느끼한 말 = cheesy or sleazy line.","크림 파스타는 좀 **느끼해서** 많이 못 먹어요.","Cream pasta is a bit heavy, so I can't eat much of it."],["매콤하다","pleasantly spicy","Mildly and appealingly spicy. Softer and more positive than 맵다.","**매콤한** 떡볶이가 먹고 싶어요.","I'm craving some spicy tteokbokki."],["비리다","fishy","Unpleasant fishy or raw smell or taste: 생선이 비리다, 비린내.","이 생선은 하나도 안 **비리네요**.","This fish isn't fishy at all."],["새콤하다","pleasantly sour, tangy","Appealingly sour. Often 새콤달콤 (sweet and sour).","**새콤한** 레몬 소스가 잘 어울려요.","The tangy lemon sauce goes really well with it."],["쌉쌀하다","slightly bitter","Pleasant mild bitterness: 녹차, 도라지, 다크 초콜릿. Softer than 쓰다.","이 차는 맛이 좀 **쌉쌀해요**.","This tea is a bit bitter."],["짭짤하다","nicely salty, savory; (money) lucrative","Food: appealingly salty. Slang: 짭짤한 수입 = a tidy income.","감자칩은 **짭짤해서** 자꾸 손이 가요.","Potato chips are so salty that I keep reaching for more."]]}]});
GUIDE.en.push({"n":8,"t":"문제와 해결","en":"Problems and solutions","units":[{"n":1,"t":"고장과 수리","g":[{"f":"-는다 -는다 하는 것이","en":"I kept meaning to X, but (still didn't)","core":"Repeating the verb shows the speaker kept intending or saying they would do something, but it still didn't happen. Often used when admitting procrastination.","forms":[["Verb, no 받침","고친다 고친다 하는 것이 · 간다 간다 하는 것이"],["Verb, 받침","읽는다 읽는다 하는 것이"],["Short","-는다 -는다 하는 게"]],"rules":["Same verb twice in the -ㄴ/는다 plain form.","Usually followed by a past negative or a result: 아직 못 했어요, 결국 잊어버렸어요, 벌써 한 달이 지났어요.","Spoken form: <b>-ㄴ다 -ㄴ다 하는 게</b>.","Self-reflective or apologetic tone."],"ex":[["세면대를 **고친다 고친다 하는 것이** 벌써 한 달이 지났어요.","I kept meaning to fix the sink, and a whole month has already gone by."],["전화**한다 한다 하는 게** 계속 잊어버렸어요.","I kept meaning to call but kept forgetting."],["운동을 **시작한다 시작한다 하는 것이** 아직도 못 했어요.","I kept saying I'd start exercising, but I still haven't."]]},{"f":"-는 수밖에 없다","en":"there's no choice but to X","core":"The only option available. 수 = way/means, 밖에 없다 = nothing but. \"I have no choice but to…\"","forms":[["Verb, no 받침","교체하는 수밖에 없다 · 사는 수밖에 없다"],["Verb, 받침","참는 수밖에 없다 · 기다리는 수밖에"]],"rules":["Verb + -는 수밖에 없다 (present form, even for future or past situations).","Past: <b>-는 수밖에 없었다</b> (had no choice but).","Often after a reason: 고칠 수 없으니까 새로 <b>사는 수밖에 없어요</b>.","Similar: -(으)ㄹ 수밖에 없다 = can't help but / inevitably (more about natural result). Both appear in 4급."],"ex":[["너무 낡아서 새것으로 **교체하는 수밖에 없어요**.","It's too worn out, so there's no choice but to replace it."],["주말이라 수리 기사님이 안 오셔서 월요일까지 **기다리는 수밖에 없었어요**.","It was the weekend and the repairman couldn't come, so I had no choice but to wait until Monday."],["열쇠를 잃어버렸으니 열쇠 기사님을 **부르는 수밖에 없겠네요**.","I lost my key, so I guess there's no choice but to call a locksmith."]]}],"v":[["세면대","washbasin, bathroom sink","For washing face or hands. Kitchen sink = 싱크대.","**세면대**에서 물이 새요.","Water is leaking from the bathroom sink."],["키","key","Loanword for keys and keycards: 카드 키, 차 키. 열쇠 is the native word. (Homonym 키 = height.)","현관 **키**를 집 안에 두고 나왔어요.","I left the front-door key inside and came out."],["교체하다","to replace (parts)","<b>N을/를 N(으)로 교체하다</b>, 부품/배터리를 교체하다. Swapping old for new.","고장 난 전구를 새것으로 **교체했어요**.","I replaced the broken light bulb with a new one."],["부르다","to call (a person to come)","<b>수리 기사를 부르다</b>, 택시를 부르다. Also: sing (노래를 부르다), be full (배가 부르다).","보일러가 고장 나서 기사님을 **불렀어요**.","The boiler broke, so I called a repairman."],["새다","to leak","<b>물/가스가 새다</b>. Also: 밤을 새다 (stay up all night). 빛이 새다.","천장에서 물이 **새서** 집주인에게 연락했어요.","Water was leaking from the ceiling, so I contacted the landlord."],["다 되다","to run out; to be finished","<b>배터리가 다 되다</b> (die), 수명이 다 되다 (reach end of life), 밥이 다 되다 (rice is ready).","휴대폰 배터리가 **다 돼서** 전화를 못 했어요.","My phone battery died, so I couldn't call."]],"x":[["나가다","(power) to go out; (bulb) to burn out","Beyond \"go out\": <b>전기가 나가다</b> (power outage), 전구가 나가다.","갑자기 전기가 **나가서** 깜깜해졌어요.","The power suddenly went out and it got pitch dark."],["낡다","old, worn out","Things only, from use: <b>낡은 집 / 옷</b>. For people, use 늙다. 오래되다 = old (in time).","집이 **낡아서** 고칠 데가 많아요.","The house is old, so there are many things to fix."],["설치하다","to install","<b>에어컨/프로그램을 설치하다</b>. Also for setting up equipment.","새 에어컨을 **설치하는** 데 하루가 걸렸어요.","It took a day to install the new air conditioner."],["손보다","to fix up, repair","Informal: light repair or touch-up. <b>문을 좀 손보다</b>.","오래된 자전거를 좀 **손봐서** 다시 타요.","I fixed up my old bike a bit and ride it again."],["금이 가다","to crack","<b>유리/벽에 금이 가다</b>. Figurative: 우정에 금이 가다 (friendship cracks).","휴대폰 화면에 **금이 갔어요**.","My phone screen cracked."]]},{"n":2,"t":"이웃 간의 문제","g":[{"f":"-는 바람에","en":"because of (an unexpected event), so (bad result)","core":"An unexpected or unwanted event caused a usually negative result. Similar to -아/어서 but stresses that it happened suddenly or uncontrollably.","forms":[["Verb","오는 바람에 · 쿵쿵거리는 바람에 · 고장 나는 바람에"]],"rules":["Verbs only, always present -는 form even for past events: 비가 <b>오는 바람에</b> 늦었어요.","The result clause is in the past: -았/었어요.","No commands or suggestions in the result clause.","Usually negative results. A positive result is possible but sounds ironic or lucky: 버스를 놓치는 바람에 오히려 친구를 만났어요."],"ex":[["윗집에서 밤늦게 **쿵쿵거리는 바람에** 잠을 못 잤어요.","I couldn't sleep because the upstairs neighbors were stomping late at night."],["옆집 사람이 차를 막아 **놓는 바람에** 회사에 늦었어요.","My neighbor blocked my car in, so I was late for work."],["갑자기 물이 **새는 바람에** 아랫집에 피해를 끼쳤어요.","Water suddenly leaked, so I caused damage to the downstairs unit."]]},{"f":"-어서야","en":"(1) only after X; (2) if it's like X, how can… (rhetorical)","core":"Two uses. (1) <b>Only when / not until</b>: something happened only after X. (2) <b>Rhetorical complaint</b>: \"If things are like X, how could Y be possible?\" Used with -겠어요? or -(으)ㄹ 수 있겠어요? This second use is common in 이웃 문제 situations.","forms":[["Verb / adj, ㅏ/ㅗ","와서야 · 많아서야"],["Verb / adj, other","들어서야 · 시끄러워서야"],["하다","해서야 · 조용해서야"]],"rules":["(1) Only after: 밤 12시가 <b>넘어서야</b> 조용해졌어요. Often with 겨우, 비로소, 그제야.","(2) Rhetorical: <b>이렇게 시끄러워서야</b> 잠을 잘 수 있겠어요? The answer is obviously no.","No past tense on -어서야.","Rhetorical use is a strong but indirect complaint. Good for writing a polite but firm note to a neighbor."],"ex":[["관리실에 항의를 하고 **나서야** 소음이 멈췄어요.","The noise stopped only after I complained to the management office."],["밤마다 이렇게 **시끄러워서야** 어떻게 살 수 있겠어요?","How is anyone supposed to live with it this loud every night?"],["주차를 이렇게 **해서야** 다른 사람들이 어떻게 지나가요?","If you park like this, how are other people supposed to get by?"]]}],"v":[["요청하다","to request","Formal ask: <b>N에게 N을/를 요청하다</b>, 도움을 요청하다, 협조 요청.","관리실에 수리를 **요청했어요**.","I requested a repair from the management office."],["웬만하다","fairly decent; tolerable","Adjective: <b>웬만한 일</b> = ordinary or minor matters. Adverb <b>웬만하면</b> = if possible, if it's not too much trouble.","**웬만하면** 밤 10시 이후에는 세탁기를 돌리지 마세요.","If possible, please don't run the washing machine after 10 p.m."],["쿵쿵거리다","to thump, stomp","Onomatopoeic 쿵쿵 + -거리다 (repeated sound or action). Heard in every 층간 소음 (floor-noise) complaint.","윗집 아이들이 뛰어서 천장이 **쿵쿵거려요**.","The upstairs kids are running, so the ceiling is thumping."],["항의하다","to protest, lodge a complaint","<b>N에게 항의하다</b>. Stronger and more formal than 불평하다; directed at someone responsible.","소음 때문에 윗집에 **항의했어요**.","I complained to the upstairs neighbors about the noise."],["도대체","on earth, what in the world","Strengthens questions of frustration: <b>도대체 왜 / 뭐 / 언제</b>.","**도대체** 몇 시까지 시끄럽게 할 거예요?","Until what time on earth are you going to keep making noise?"],["종종","often, from time to time","Occasionally but fairly regularly. Between 가끔 and 자주.","아파트에서는 이런 문제가 **종종** 생겨요.","Problems like this come up from time to time in apartments."]],"x":[["손해","loss (usually financial)","<b>손해를 보다</b> (suffer a loss), 손해를 입다. Opposite: 이익.","싸게 팔아서 **손해**를 봤어요.","I sold it cheaply and took a loss."],["피해","damage, harm (to others)","<b>피해를 주다 / 끼치다 / 입다</b>, 피해자 (victim). Broader than 손해.","다른 사람에게 **피해**를 주지 않도록 조심하세요.","Be careful not to cause harm to others."],["끼치다","to cause (trouble, harm)","Mostly in set phrases: <b>폐를 끼치다</b> (impose on), 피해를 끼치다, 영향을 끼치다.","늦게까지 시끄럽게 해서 폐를 **끼쳐** 죄송합니다.","I'm sorry for imposing on you by being noisy so late."],["따지다","to argue, demand an explanation; to weigh","(1) Confront someone: 왜 그랬냐고 따지다. (2) Calculate carefully: 장단점을 따지다.","참다못해 윗집에 가서 **따졌어요**.","I couldn't take it anymore and went upstairs to confront them."],["무책임하다","irresponsible","무- (without) + 책임. 무책임한 행동.","쓰레기를 아무 데나 버리는 건 **무책임한** 행동이에요.","Dumping trash anywhere is irresponsible behavior."],["요구하다","to demand","Stronger than 요청하다 (request): you claim it as your right. 요구 사항.","피해에 대한 보상을 **요구했어요**.","I demanded compensation for the damage."],["위반하다","to violate","For rules or laws: <b>규칙/법/교통 신호를 위반하다</b>.","주차 규칙을 **위반하면** 벌금을 내야 해요.","If you violate parking rules, you have to pay a fine."],["저지르다","to commit (a mistake, crime)","Negative actions: <b>실수/잘못/범죄를 저지르다</b>. 르 irregular: 저질러요.","제가 큰 실수를 **저질렀어요**.","I made a big mistake."]]}]});
GUIDE.en.push({"n":9,"t":"정보화 사회","en":"The information society","units":[{"n":1,"t":"가짜 뉴스","g":[{"f":"에 비해서","en":"compared to N","core":"Compares something to a reference point. Formal-sounding and very common in writing, news, and TOPIK essays.","forms":[["Noun","예전에 비해서 · 작년에 비해 · 신문에 비해서"],["Verb (via -는 것에)","노력하는 것에 비해서 · 가격에 비해서"]],"rules":["<b>N에 비해(서)</b>. 서 is often dropped in writing: 에 비해.","The main clause usually has a comparative adjective, often with 더 or 훨씬: 예전에 비해 정보가 훨씬 많아졌다.","<b>N에 비해 + adj</b> can mean \"relative to\": 가격에 비해 품질이 좋다 (good quality for the price).","Synonym: N보다. 에 비해서 is more formal and analytical."],"ex":[["인터넷 뉴스는 신문**에 비해서** 정보가 빨리 전달돼요.","Compared to newspapers, internet news spreads information faster."],["예전**에 비해** 가짜 뉴스가 훨씬 많아졌어요.","Fake news has increased a lot compared to before."],["이 기사는 길이**에 비해서** 내용이 별로 없어요.","For its length, this article doesn't have much content."]]},{"f":"-을 수가 있어야지요","en":"but how could I X (it's impossible) — complaint","core":"A rhetorical complaint: the speaker wanted or tried to do X, but it was impossible given the situation. Literally \"one would need to be able to X,\" meaning \"but I can't.\"","forms":[["Verb, no 받침","볼 수가 있어야지요 · 잘 수가 있어야지요"],["Verb, 받침","믿을 수가 있어야지요 · 읽을 수가 있어야지요"]],"rules":["Verb + -(으)ㄹ 수가 있어야지요. Short: <b>-(으)ㄹ 수가 있어야죠</b>.","Usually after giving the reason: 너무 시끄러워서 잠을 <b>잘 수가 있어야지요</b>.","Expresses frustration. It sounds like an excuse or a complaint.","There's a broader pattern <b>-아/어야지요</b> (\"it should be X, but it isn't\"): 말이 통해야지요."],"ex":[["가짜 뉴스가 너무 많아서 뭘 **믿을 수가 있어야지요**.","There's so much fake news, how am I supposed to believe anything?"],["기사가 너무 전문적이라서 **이해할 수가 있어야지요**.","The article is so technical, how is anyone supposed to understand it?"],["광고가 계속 나와서 영상을 **볼 수가 있어야지요**.","Ads keep popping up, so I can't even watch the video."]]}],"v":[["난리","chaos, uproar, fuss","<b>난리가 나다</b> = all hell breaks loose. Often exaggerated: SNS에서 난리가 났어요 (it went viral or caused an uproar).","그 가짜 뉴스 때문에 인터넷이 **난리**가 났어요.","The internet went into an uproar over that fake news."],["여부","whether or not","Formal noun: <b>사실 여부</b> (whether it's true), 참석 여부, 합격 여부.","기사를 공유하기 전에 사실 **여부**를 확인하세요.","Check whether it's true before sharing an article."],["의심","doubt, suspicion","<b>의심하다</b>, 의심스럽다, 의심이 들다 (get suspicious).","출처가 없는 기사는 **의심**해 봐야 해요.","You should be suspicious of articles with no source."],["작업","work, task, operation","A specific job or process: 편집 작업, 작업 중, 작업하다. More concrete than 일.","영상 편집 **작업**에 시간이 많이 걸려요.","Video editing work takes a lot of time."],["전문적","professional, specialized, technical","-적 noun: 전문적인 지식, 전문적으로. 전문가 = expert.","이 내용은 **전문적**이라서 이해하기 어려워요.","This content is technical, so it's hard to understand."],["가리다","to distinguish, tell apart; to cover; to be picky","(1) <b>진실을 가리다</b>, 옳고 그름을 가리다. (2) 얼굴을 가리다 (cover). (3) 음식을 가리다 (be picky).","어떤 뉴스가 진짜인지 **가리기**가 어려워요.","It's hard to tell which news is real."],["넘쳐나다","to overflow, be flooded with","Too much of something: <b>정보가 넘쳐나다</b>.","인터넷에는 정보가 **넘쳐나요**.","The internet is overflowing with information."],["전달되다","to be delivered, conveyed","Passive of 전달하다 (6과). <b>정보/메시지가 전달되다</b>.","SNS로 소식이 순식간에 **전달돼요**.","News spreads in an instant via social media."]],"x":[["분석하다","to analyze","데이터를 분석하다, 분석 결과.","전문가들이 그 기사를 **분석했어요**.","Experts analyzed the article."],["삭제하다","to delete","<b>파일/게시물을 삭제하다</b>. Everyday: 지우다.","가짜 뉴스는 결국 **삭제됐어요**.","The fake news was eventually deleted."],["입력하다","to input, enter (data)","<b>비밀번호/정보를 입력하다</b>.","아이디와 비밀번호를 **입력하세요**.","Enter your ID and password."],["저장하다","to save, store","<b>파일을 저장하다</b>, 저장 공간 (storage).","작업한 파일을 꼭 **저장하세요**.","Be sure to save the file you worked on."],["전송하다","to send, transmit (data)","<b>파일/메시지를 전송하다</b>. More technical than 보내다.","사진을 이메일로 **전송했어요**.","I sent the photo by email."]]},{"n":2,"t":"휴대 전화 사용 제한","g":[{"f":"에 따르면","en":"according to N","core":"Cites a source of information. Almost always followed by reported speech (-ㄴ/는다고 하다, -대요, -(이)래요).","forms":[["Noun","뉴스에 따르면 · 조사에 따르면 · 전문가에 따르면"]],"rules":["<b>N에 따르면 + -ㄴ/는다고 해요 / -대요</b>: the reported form is expected.","N is a source: 뉴스, 신문, 조사 결과, 연구, 전문가, 친구 말.","Formal, so it's very common in presentations, essays, and news.","Don't confuse with 에 따라(서) = depending on / in accordance with."],"ex":[["조사**에 따르면** 학생의 70%가 휴대 전화 사용 제한에 반대한다고 해요.","According to a survey, 70% of students are against restricting phone use."],["뉴스**에 따르면** 내년부터 수업 중 휴대폰 사용이 금지된대요.","According to the news, phone use during class will be banned starting next year."],["전문가**에 따르면** 자기 전에 휴대폰을 보는 것은 수면에 방해가 된다고 합니다.","According to experts, looking at your phone before bed interferes with sleep."]]},{"f":"-는다고 보다","en":"to view / consider that X (opinion)","core":"States an opinion or judgment, often formal and analytical: \"I see it as…\", \"I believe that…\" Common in debates and opinion essays.","forms":[["Verb","필요하다고 보다 · 제한해야 한다고 보다 · 간다고 보다"],["Adjective","중요하다고 보다 · 옳다고 보다"],["Noun","문제라고 보다 · 권리라고 보다"]],"rules":["Uses indirect quote forms: verb -ㄴ/는다고, adjective -다고, noun -(이)라고.","<b>저는 -다고 봐요 / 봅니다</b>: a softer and more objective-sounding way to give an opinion than -다고 생각해요.","Passive version: <b>-다고 볼 수 있다</b> (it can be seen that).","Very useful in 토론 (debate) phrases."],"ex":[["저는 학교에서 휴대 전화 사용을 어느 정도 **제한해야 한다고 봅니다**.","I believe phone use at school should be restricted to some extent."],["휴대폰을 마음대로 쓰는 것도 학생의 **권리라고 봐요**.","I see using a phone freely as a student's right too."],["이 문제는 학생과 선생님이 함께 합의하는 게 가장 **중요하다고 봐요**.","I think the most important thing here is for students and teachers to reach agreement together."]]}],"v":[["권리","right (entitlement)","<b>권리가 있다</b>, 권리를 주장하다/지키다. Paired with 의무 (duty).","누구나 자유롭게 의견을 말할 **권리**가 있어요.","Everyone has the right to speak their opinion freely."],["인권","human rights","<b>인권 침해</b> (violation of human rights), 인권을 보호하다.","휴대폰을 강제로 걷는 것은 **인권** 침해라고 주장하는 사람도 있어요.","Some people argue that forcibly collecting phones is a violation of human rights."],["의견","opinion","<b>의견을 말하다 / 나누다 / 제시하다</b>, 의견이 다르다.","이 문제에 대해서 여러분의 **의견**은 어때요?","What's your opinion on this issue?"],["판단","judgment, decision","<b>판단하다</b>, 판단을 내리다, 스스로 판단하다. 판단력 (10과).","학생들도 스스로 **판단**할 수 있는 능력이 있어요.","Students also have the ability to make their own judgments."],["제한하다","to restrict, limit","<b>사용/시간/속도를 제한하다</b>. 제한 시간 (time limit).","학교에서 휴대폰 사용 시간을 **제한하고** 있어요.","The school is restricting phone usage time."],["합의하다","to reach an agreement","Both sides agree after discussion: <b>N와 합의하다</b>, 합의를 보다. Compare 동의하다 (agree with one opinion).","학생회와 학교가 규칙에 **합의했어요**.","The student council and the school agreed on the rules."],["마음대로","as one pleases, freely","Can be neutral (freely) or negative (without permission). <b>마음대로 하세요</b> = do as you like.","수업 시간에 휴대폰을 **마음대로** 쓰면 안 돼요.","You can't just use your phone however you want during class."]],"x":[["대립","confrontation, opposition","Opposing sides: <b>의견이 대립하다</b>, 찬반 대립.","이 문제에 대해서 의견이 **대립**하고 있어요.","Opinions are divided on this issue."],["동의","agreement, consent","<b>N에 동의하다</b> (agree with), 동의를 구하다 (ask for consent).","저도 그 의견에 **동의**해요.","I agree with that opinion too."],["방안","measure, plan, way (to solve)","Formal: <b>해결 방안을 마련하다 / 제시하다</b>.","문제를 해결할 수 있는 **방안**을 찾아야 해요.","We need to find a way to solve the problem."],["토론","debate","Sides argue for or against (찬성 vs. 반대). Compare 토의.","오늘 수업에서 휴대폰 사용에 대해 **토론**했어요.","In class today, we debated phone use."],["토의","discussion (cooperative)","A group discusses together to find a solution. 토론 = opposing sides; 토의 = working toward an answer together.","학급 회의에서 규칙에 대해 **토의**했어요.","At the class meeting, we discussed the rules."],["마련하다","to prepare, arrange (funds, measures)","<b>대책/방안/돈/자리를 마련하다</b>. Getting something ready, often with effort.","학교는 새로운 규칙을 **마련했어요**.","The school put together new rules."],["설득하다","to persuade","<b>N을/를 설득하다</b>, 설득력 (persuasiveness).","부모님을 **설득하는** 게 쉽지 않았어요.","Persuading my parents wasn't easy."],["제시하다","to present, propose","<b>의견/방안/근거를 제시하다</b>. Formal; essays and debates.","주장을 할 때는 근거를 **제시해야** 해요.","When you make a claim, you have to present evidence."]]}]});
GUIDE.en.push({"n":10,"t":"현대인의 모습","en":"Modern people","units":[{"n":1,"t":"현대인과 일","g":[{"f":"만 아니면","en":"if it weren't for N; if only not for N","core":"만 (only) + 아니면 (if not). The speaker names the one obstacle preventing something: \"If it weren't for X, I could…\"","forms":[["Noun","일만 아니면 · 시험만 아니면 · 회사만 아니면"],["Verb (via -는 것만)","야근하는 것만 아니면"]],"rules":["Attaches to nouns: <b>N만 아니면</b>.","The second clause is what would be possible without the obstacle: -(으)ㄹ 텐데, -았/었을 거예요, -(으)ㄹ 수 있을 텐데.","Often wistful or complaining.","Past situation: <b>N만 아니었으면</b> (if it hadn't been for N)."],"ex":[["야근**만 아니면** 이 회사가 정말 좋을 텐데요.","If it weren't for the overtime, this company would be really great."],["내일 발표**만 아니면** 오늘 같이 놀 수 있을 텐데.","If it weren't for tomorrow's presentation, I could hang out with you today."],["그 실수**만 아니었으면** 좋은 성과를 거둘 수 있었을 거예요.","If it hadn't been for that mistake, we could have gotten good results."]]},{"f":"-는 듯이","en":"as if X; like X","core":"Describes the manner of an action by comparing it to something: \"as if,\" \"like.\" Often literary or vivid. Similar to -는 것처럼.","forms":[["Verb (present)","죽은 듯이 · 기다렸다는 듯이 · 아무 일도 없었다는 듯이"],["Verb","날아가는 듯이 · 쏟아지는 듯이"],["Adjective","아픈 듯이 · 피곤한 듯이"]],"rules":["Verb present -는 듯이, past -(으)ㄴ 듯이, future -(으)ㄹ 듯이, adjective -(으)ㄴ 듯이.","이 can be dropped: <b>-는 듯</b>.","Popular with quoted forms: <b>-다는 듯이</b> (as if to say): 기다렸다는 듯이 (as if they'd been waiting).","Set phrases: 죽은 듯이 자다 (sleep like the dead), 물 쓰듯이 (spend like water), 밥 먹듯이 (as often as eating, i.e. constantly).","Compare -는 듯하다 (it seems that), which ends a sentence."],"ex":[["그는 피곤해서 **죽은 듯이** 잤어요.","He was so tired that he slept like the dead."],["현대인들은 야근을 **밥 먹듯이** 해요.","Modern people work overtime constantly."],["퇴근 시간이 되자 모두 **기다렸다는 듯이** 사무실을 나갔어요.","When it was time to leave, everyone walked out of the office as if they'd been waiting for it."]]}],"v":[["경쟁","competition","<b>경쟁하다</b>, 경쟁이 치열하다 (fierce), 경쟁력 (competitiveness, 10과-2).","요즘은 취업 **경쟁**이 정말 치열해요.","Job competition is really fierce these days."],["장시간","long hours, a long time","Formal: <b>장시간 근무 / 운전</b>. Opposite: 단시간.","**장시간** 앉아서 일하면 허리가 아파요.","Sitting and working for long hours hurts your back."],["효율적","efficient","-적 noun: 효율적인 방법, 효율적으로. 효율 = efficiency. 효과적 = effective (gets results); 효율적 = efficient (little waste).","시간을 **효율적**으로 쓰는 게 중요해요.","It's important to use your time efficiently."],["뒤떨어지다","to fall behind, lag","<b>N에 뒤떨어지다</b>, 시대에 뒤떨어지다 (be behind the times).","새로운 기술을 배우지 않으면 시대에 **뒤떨어질** 수 있어요.","If you don't learn new technology, you could fall behind the times."],["살아남다","to survive","For tough competition or harsh conditions: 경쟁에서 살아남다.","치열한 경쟁 속에서 **살아남으려면** 계속 공부해야 해요.","To survive in fierce competition, you have to keep studying."],["온종일","all day long","Same as 하루 종일, slightly more literary.","**온종일** 컴퓨터 앞에 앉아 있었어요.","I sat in front of the computer all day long."]],"x":[["성과","results, achievements","<b>성과를 거두다 / 올리다 / 내다</b>, 성과급 (performance bonus).","이번 프로젝트에서 좋은 **성과**를 거뒀어요.","We achieved good results on this project."],["현대인","modern people","현대 (modern era) + -인 (person). Common essay subject: 현대인의 삶.","**현대인**은 늘 시간에 쫓기며 살아요.","Modern people always live chased by time."],["거두다","to achieve, reap (results); to collect","<b>성과/성공/승리를 거두다</b>. Literal: 곡식을 거두다 (harvest).","그 팀은 큰 성공을 **거두었어요**.","That team achieved great success."],["깨지다","to break; (record) be broken","<b>기록이 깨지다</b>, 유리가 깨지다. Also figurative: 약속이 깨지다.","그 선수 덕분에 세계 기록이 **깨졌어요**.","Thanks to that athlete, the world record was broken."],["올리다","to raise; to achieve; to post","<b>성과/매출을 올리다</b>, 월급을 올리다, 사진을 올리다 (post online).","이번 달에 매출을 많이 **올렸어요**.","We boosted sales a lot this month."],["향하다","to face, head toward","<b>N을/를 향하다</b>, N(으)로 향하다, 꿈을 향해 (toward one's dream).","모두가 같은 목표를 **향해** 노력하고 있어요.","Everyone is working toward the same goal."]]},{"n":2,"t":"현대인의 소통 수단","g":[{"f":"-는 법이다","en":"it's natural that X; X always happens (general truth)","core":"States a general truth, law of nature, or common wisdom: \"That's just how it is.\" Often used to comfort, advise, or explain.","forms":[["Verb","하는 법이다 · 생기는 법이다 · 있는 법이다"],["Adjective","힘든 법이다 · 어려운 법이다"]],"rules":["Verb -는 법이다, adjective -(으)ㄴ 법이다. Present tense only.","Sounds wise or proverb-like: <b>누구나 실수하는 법이에요</b>.","Often follows a condition: 노력하면 결과가 <b>있는 법이에요</b>.","Similar: -기 마련이다 (bound to happen)."],"ex":[["처음에는 누구나 **실수하는 법이에요**.","Everyone makes mistakes at first. That's just how it is."],["자주 연락하지 않으면 사이가 **멀어지는 법이지요**.","If you don't keep in touch, you naturally grow apart."],["새로운 방식에는 장점과 단점이 다 **있는 법이에요**.","Every new method has its pros and cons."]]},{"f":"-는다고 할 수 있다","en":"it can be said that X","core":"A cautious, objective way to state a conclusion or definition. Common in essays, presentations, and TOPIK 쓰기.","forms":[["Verb","변했다고 할 수 있다 · 선호한다고 할 수 있다"],["Adjective","편리하다고 할 수 있다"],["Noun","소통 수단이라고 할 수 있다"]],"rules":["Indirect quote forms: verb -ㄴ/는다고, adjective -다고, noun -(이)라고.","Formal written register: <b>-다고 할 수 있다 / 있습니다</b>.","Good for conclusions: 따라서 … <b>-다고 할 수 있다</b>.","Similar: -다고 볼 수 있다 (9과)."],"ex":[["스마트폰은 현대인의 가장 중요한 소통 수단**이라고 할 수 있다**.","The smartphone can be said to be modern people's most important means of communication."],["요즘 젊은 사람들은 전화보다 채팅을 **선호한다고 할 수 있어요**.","You could say young people these days prefer chatting over calling."],["이처럼 SNS는 사람들의 관계를 **바꾸었다고 할 수 있습니다**.","In this way, it can be said that social media has changed people's relationships."]]}],"v":[["일부분","a part, portion","Same as 일부, emphasizing a portion of a whole: 생활의 일부분.","휴대폰은 이제 생활의 **일부분**이 됐어요.","Phones have now become part of daily life."],["채팅","chat (online)","Loanword: 채팅하다, 단체 채팅방 (group chat, 단톡방).","친구들과 매일 **채팅**으로 이야기해요.","I chat with my friends every day."],["멀어지다","to grow distant","Physical or emotional: <b>사이가 멀어지다</b>, 친구와 멀어지다. Opposite: 가까워지다.","연락을 안 하다 보니 친구와 **멀어졌어요**.","Not keeping in touch, I grew distant from my friend."],["부담스럽다","burdensome, uncomfortable, too much","Feeling pressure or awkwardness: 전화가 부담스럽다, 비싼 선물이 부담스럽다. Very common in Korean social life.","저는 갑자기 오는 전화가 좀 **부담스러워요**.","Sudden phone calls feel like a bit much to me."],["선호하다","to prefer","Formal: <b>N보다 N을/를 선호하다</b>. Everyday: 더 좋아하다.","요즘은 통화보다 메시지를 **선호하는** 사람이 많아요.","Lots of people prefer texting over calling these days."],["흔하다","common, ordinary","Easy to find, seen often: 흔한 일, 흔히 (commonly). Opposite: 드물다.","요즘은 영상 통화가 아주 **흔해요**.","Video calls are really common these days."],["굳이","bother to; insist on (unnecessarily)","Doing something not needed: <b>굳이 -(으)ㄹ 필요가 없다</b>, 굳이 왜? (why bother?).","문자로 하면 되는데 **굳이** 전화할 필요가 있어요?","We can just text, so is there any need to bother calling?"]],"x":[["경쟁력","competitiveness","경쟁 + -력 (power, ability). <b>경쟁력이 있다 / 높다</b>, 경쟁력을 키우다.","외국어 능력은 취업 **경쟁력**을 높여 줘요.","Language skills boost your competitiveness in job-hunting."],["긴장감","tension, nervousness","긴장 + -감 (feeling). <b>긴장감이 돌다 / 있다</b>, 긴장감을 느끼다.","면접장에는 **긴장감**이 가득했어요.","The interview room was full of tension."],["사교성","sociability","사교 + -성 (quality). <b>사교성이 좋다 / 있다</b>.","그는 **사교성**이 좋아서 누구와도 금방 친해져요.","He's very sociable, so he quickly becomes friends with anyone."],["영향력","influence (power)","영향 + -력. <b>영향력이 크다 / 있다</b>, 인플루언서 = 영향력 있는 사람.","SNS의 **영향력**이 점점 커지고 있어요.","The influence of social media is growing."],["책임감","sense of responsibility","책임 + -감. <b>책임감이 강하다 / 있다</b>.","그녀는 **책임감**이 강해서 맡은 일을 끝까지 해요.","She has a strong sense of responsibility, so she sees her tasks through."],["친밀감","sense of closeness, intimacy","친밀 + -감. <b>친밀감을 느끼다 / 높이다</b>.","자주 만나면 **친밀감**이 생겨요.","Meeting often builds a sense of closeness."],["판단력","judgment (ability)","판단 + -력. <b>판단력이 좋다 / 뛰어나다 / 흐려지다</b>.","너무 피곤하면 **판단력**이 떨어져요.","When you're too tired, your judgment suffers."],["편리성","convenience","편리 + -성. Formal and analytical. 편리함 is more casual.","간편 결제는 **편리성** 때문에 인기가 많아요.","Easy-pay is popular because of its convenience."]]}]});
GUIDE.en.push({"n":11,"t":"현대인과 도시 생활","en":"Modern people and city life","units":[{"n":1,"t":"효율적인 시간 관리","g":[{"f":"-는다든가 -는다든가","en":"like X or Y; X, Y, that sort of thing (listing examples)","core":"Lists two or more examples of actions or states, implying there are others too. It's like saying \"things like X or Y.\" Usually followed by 하다 or a general verb that sums up the examples.","forms":[["Verb","운동을 한다든가 책을 읽는다든가 · 간다든가 먹는다든가"],["Adjective","크다든가 작다든가 · 비싸다든가"],["Noun","친구라든가 가족이라든가"],["Short form (no quote)","-든가 -든가: 운동을 하든가 책을 읽든가"]],"rules":["Uses the plain quoted forms: verb -ㄴ/는다든가, adjective -다든가, noun -(이)라든가.","Typical frame: <b>X-는다든가 Y-는다든가 하다</b>: 운동을 한다든가 산책을 한다든가 해요.","Often used when giving advice or suggestions: 자투리 시간에 단어를 외운다든가 하면 좋아요.","Compare <b>-든지 -든지</b> (15과): that one is about choice (\"either X or Y, it doesn't matter\"). -는다든가 is about giving examples.","Nouns can also take <b>N(이)라든가</b>: 휴대폰이라든가 노트북이라든가."],"ex":[["자투리 시간에는 단어를 **외운다든가** 뉴스를 **본다든가** 하면 시간을 낭비하지 않을 수 있어요.","In spare moments, you can avoid wasting time by doing things like memorizing words or watching the news."],["주말에는 집안일을 **한다든가** 장을 **본다든가** 해서 바빠요.","On weekends I'm busy with things like housework and grocery shopping."],["계획을 세울 때는 시간**이라든가** 장소**라든가** 구체적으로 정하는 게 좋아요.","When making plans, it's good to decide things concretely, like the time and place."]]},{"f":"-는다니까","en":"(1) I'm telling you X! (emphasis); (2) since (someone) says X, …","core":"Two uses. (1) <b>Emphasis</b>: insisting on something you already said, often with frustration: \"I told you, X!\" (2) <b>Reason from what someone said</b>: \"Since they say X, (do/did Y).\" This is short for -는다고 하니까.","forms":[["Verb","간다니까 · 먹는다니까 · 했다니까"],["Adjective","바쁘다니까 · 괜찮다니까"],["Noun","사실이라니까 · 내일이라니까"]],"rules":["Plain quoted forms: verb -ㄴ/는다니까, adjective -다니까, noun -(이)라니까.","Emphasis use usually ends the sentence: <b>정말 괜찮다니까요</b>. Casual: -는다니까.","Reason use connects to a second clause: 비가 <b>온다니까</b> 우산 가져가세요.","With commands and suggestions, use -(으)라니까 / -자니까: 빨리 하<b>라니까</b> (I told you to hurry!).","Tone matters: the emphasis use can sound impatient, so soften with -요 to elders."],"ex":[["내일 하면 늦는다니까요. 미루지 말고 오늘 **한다니까요**!","I'm telling you, it'll be too late tomorrow. Don't put it off. Do it today!"],["친구가 그 앱이 시간 관리에 좋다**니까** 한번 써 볼까 해요.","My friend says that app is good for time management, so I'm thinking of trying it."],["A: 정말 다 했어? B: 다 **했다니까**.","A: Did you really finish everything? B: I told you, I did."]]}],"v":[["구체적","concrete, specific","-적 noun: 구체적이다, <b>구체적으로 말하다 / 계획하다</b>. Opposite: 추상적.","목표를 **구체적**으로 세워야 실천하기 쉬워요.","Setting concrete goals makes them easier to follow through on."],["계획적","planned, systematic","계획적이다, 계획적으로 (in a planned way). Describes people too: 계획적인 사람 = someone who plans everything.","저는 **계획적**인 편이라서 매일 할 일을 미리 정해요.","I'm a planner, so I decide my tasks for each day in advance."],["자투리","scraps, leftover bits","Originally leftover fabric. Now very common as <b>자투리 시간</b> = spare moments between things (on the bus, waiting in line).","출퇴근하는 **자투리** 시간에 단어를 외워요.","I memorize vocabulary in the spare time during my commute."],["낭비하다","to waste","<b>시간/돈/에너지를 낭비하다</b>. 낭비 = waste: 시간 낭비 (a waste of time).","휴대폰을 보면서 시간을 너무 많이 **낭비했어요**.","I wasted too much time looking at my phone."],["미루다","to put off, postpone","<b>일을 내일로 미루다</b>. 미루는 습관 = procrastination habit. Also: blame-shift (책임을 남에게 미루다).","숙제를 계속 **미루다가** 결국 밤을 새웠어요.","I kept putting off my homework and ended up pulling an all-nighter."],["반성하다","to reflect on (one's faults), regret","Reflecting on your own mistakes to improve. Stronger moral tone than 후회하다. 반성문 = written apology.","하루를 마치면서 시간을 잘 썼는지 **반성해요**.","At the end of each day, I reflect on whether I used my time well."]],"x":[["만족스럽다","satisfying, satisfactory","Adjective describing the thing: <b>결과가 만족스럽다</b>. ㅂ irregular: 만족스러워요.","이번 시험 결과는 꽤 **만족스러워요**.","I'm pretty satisfied with this exam result."],["만족하다","to be satisfied","Verb for the person: <b>N에 만족하다</b>. 지금 생활에 만족해요.","저는 지금 하는 일에 **만족해요**.","I'm satisfied with the work I do now."],["불만족스럽다","unsatisfactory, disappointing","불- + 만족스럽다. Formal-ish. Everyday: 마음에 안 들다.","서비스가 **불만족스러워서** 환불을 요청했어요.","The service was unsatisfactory, so I asked for a refund."],["실천하다","to put into practice","Turning plans or resolutions into action: <b>계획/약속을 실천하다</b>. Pairs with 계획 and 결심.","계획만 세우지 말고 **실천하는** 게 중요해요.","It's important to actually follow through, not just make plans."],["점검하다","to check, inspect, review","Systematic checking: <b>안전/일정/진행 상황을 점검하다</b>. 정기 점검 = regular maintenance.","일주일에 한 번 계획을 잘 지켰는지 **점검해요**.","Once a week I check whether I stuck to my plan."]]},{"n":2,"t":"도심 속 자연","g":[{"f":"-더니²","en":"(I saw that) X kept happening, and as a result Y","core":"Based on something the speaker observed over time, followed by the result it led to. Book 1's -더니¹ focused on contrast or change (어제는 춥더니 오늘은 따뜻하다). This -더니² focuses on cause and result: \"X happened, and then (because of that) Y.\" Check your class notes for your teacher's exact split.","forms":[["Verb / adjective stem","공부하더니 · 기침을 하더니 · 바쁘더니"],["Noun","학생이더니"]],"rules":["Stem + 더니. The X part is something the speaker saw, usually about someone or something else, not the speaker.","The Y part is the result: 열심히 연습하<b>더니</b> 결국 대회에서 1등을 했어요.","The subject of both clauses is usually the same.","For your own action leading to a discovery, use <b>-었더니</b> (that's 16과's -더니³): 공원에 갔더니 사람이 많았어요.","No past tense before -더니 here."],"ex":[["동네에 공원이 **생기더니** 사람들이 많이 산책하기 시작했어요.","A park opened in the neighborhood, and people started taking lots of walks."],["친구가 매일 공원에서 **뛰더니** 건강이 훨씬 좋아졌어요.","My friend ran in the park every day, and his health got much better."],["아침부터 하늘이 **흐리더니** 오후에 비가 쏟아졌어요.","The sky had been cloudy since morning, and in the afternoon it poured."]]},{"f":"-었다 하면","en":"whenever (once) X happens, (always) Y","core":"Once X happens, Y follows every time without exception. It emphasizes a habit or pattern, often with a bit of exaggeration: \"The moment I sit down, I fall asleep.\"","forms":[["Verb, ㅏ/ㅗ","갔다 하면 · 왔다 하면 · 봤다 하면"],["Verb, other","먹었다 하면 · 시작했다 하면 · 앉았다 하면"]],"rules":["Verbs only. Always in the -았/었다 form, but the meaning is general, not past.","The second clause describes what always happens: 다, 항상, 무조건, -기 일쑤이다.","Often a bit humorous or exaggerated: 그 친구는 입을 <b>열었다 하면</b> 자랑이에요.","Similar meaning: -기만 하면. -었다 하면 sounds more vivid and colloquial."],"ex":[["저는 공원 벤치에 **앉았다 하면** 한 시간은 그냥 지나가요.","Once I sit down on a park bench, an hour just slips by."],["그 친구는 등산을 **갔다 하면** 사진을 수백 장씩 찍어 와요.","Whenever that friend goes hiking, she comes back with hundreds of photos."],["비가 **왔다 하면** 이 길은 물에 잠겨요.","Every time it rains, this road floods."]]}],"v":[["도심","city center, downtown","都心. <b>도심 속</b> (in the middle of the city), 도심 공원. More formal than 시내.","**도심** 속에도 조용히 쉴 수 있는 공원이 많아요.","There are lots of parks in the middle of the city where you can rest quietly."],["안정","stability; calm","<b>마음의 안정</b> (peace of mind), 안정을 찾다/취하다, 안정적. Also 안정시키다 (15과).","숲길을 걸으면 마음이 **안정**되는 느낌이에요.","Walking a forest path makes me feel calm."],["한산하다","quiet, not crowded","For places without many people: <b>거리가 한산하다</b>. Opposite: 붐비다 (7과).","평일 오전에는 공원이 **한산해서** 좋아요.","I like the park on weekday mornings because it's not crowded."],["온통","entirely, all over","Everything is covered or filled with one thing: <b>온통 N(이)다</b>, 온통 눈으로 덮이다.","가을이 되니까 산이 **온통** 빨갛게 물들었어요.","Now that it's autumn, the whole mountain has turned red."],["틈틈이","in spare moments, whenever there's a chance","틈 = gap. Doing something in between other things. Similar to 자투리 시간에.","바빠도 **틈틈이** 공원에 나가서 바람을 쐬어요.","Even when I'm busy, I go out to the park whenever I can to get some fresh air."]],"x":[["길눈이 어둡다","to have a poor sense of direction","Literally \"one's road-eye is dark.\" Opposite: 길눈이 밝다.","저는 **길눈이 어두워서** 지도 앱 없이는 못 다녀요.","I have no sense of direction, so I can't get around without a map app."],["눈이 높다","to have high standards","Usually about partners or purchases: 눈이 높아서 아무거나 안 사요.","친구가 **눈이 높아서** 아직 마음에 드는 집을 못 찾았어요.","My friend has high standards, so she still hasn't found a place she likes."],["눈이 빠지게 기다리다","to wait eagerly, impatiently","Literally \"wait until your eyes fall out.\"","주문한 책이 오기를 **눈이 빠지게 기다리고** 있어요.","I'm waiting anxiously for the book I ordered."],["발이 넓다","to know a lot of people, be well connected","Literally \"wide feet.\"","그 사람은 **발이 넓어서** 어디를 가도 아는 사람이 있어요.","He knows so many people that he runs into someone he knows wherever he goes."],["발이 묶이다","to be stuck, stranded","Literally \"feet get tied.\" For weather, strikes, cancellations: 폭설로 발이 묶이다.","태풍 때문에 공항에서 이틀 동안 **발이 묶였어요**.","I was stranded at the airport for two days because of the typhoon."],["손을 잡다","to join hands, team up","Literal (hold hands) and figurative (cooperate): 두 회사가 손을 잡다.","구청과 주민들이 **손을 잡고** 동네 공원을 만들었어요.","The district office and residents teamed up to build a neighborhood park."],["손이 크다","to be generous (especially with food)","Makes or gives a lot. Often about cooking way too much.","우리 엄마는 **손이 커서** 음식을 항상 너무 많이 하세요.","My mom is so generous that she always makes way too much food."],["입에 담다","to say, utter (usually something bad)","Mostly negative: <b>입에 담을 수 없는 말</b> = words too vulgar to repeat.","그런 욕은 **입에 담기도** 싫어요.","I don't even want to say a curse like that."],["입이 무겁다","to be tight-lipped, able to keep a secret","Opposite: 입이 가볍다 (a blabbermouth).","그 친구는 **입이 무거워서** 비밀을 말해도 괜찮아요.","She's good at keeping secrets, so it's fine to tell her."],["입이 짧다","to be a picky or light eater","Eats very little or only certain foods.","동생이 **입이 짧아서** 반찬을 거의 안 먹어요.","My younger sibling is a picky eater and barely touches the side dishes."]]}]});
GUIDE.en.push({"n":12,"t":"문화의 이해","en":"Understanding culture","units":[{"n":1,"t":"예절과 언어 표현","g":[{"f":"-는다고 해도","en":"even if (it's said that) X; even supposing X","core":"Concedes a situation, even a hypothetical one, and says the result doesn't change. Stronger and more hypothetical than -아/어도. Literally \"even if one says that X.\"","forms":[["Verb","간다고 해도 · 먹는다고 해도 · 했다고 해도"],["Adjective","친하다고 해도 · 어리다고 해도"],["Noun","친구라고 해도 · 가족이라고 해도"]],"rules":["Quoted forms: verb -ㄴ/는다고 해도, adjective -다고 해도, noun -(이)라고 해도.","Short form in speech: <b>-는대도</b>, <b>-대도</b>, <b>-(이)래도</b>.","Often with 아무리: <b>아무리</b> 친하다고 해도 예의는 지켜야 해요.","The second clause usually holds firm: -아/어야 하다, -(으)면 안 되다, -지 않다.","Compare -는다고 해서 (3과): \"just because X doesn't mean Y.\" -는다고 해도 = \"even if X, still Y.\""],"ex":[["아무리 **친하다고 해도** 처음 만난 어른께는 존댓말을 써야 해요.","No matter how close you are, you should use formal speech with an elder you've just met."],["나이가 **어리다고 해도** 무조건 반말을 하면 실례예요.","Even if someone is younger, it's rude to just automatically use casual speech."],["한국 문화를 잘 **안다고 해도** 실수할 때가 있어요.","Even if you know Korean culture well, there are times you make mistakes."]]},{"f":"-을 걸 그랬다","en":"I should have (done) X; I wish I had","core":"Expresses mild personal regret about something you didn't do. Softer and more conversational than -었어야 했다 (5과). Negative: <b>-지 말 걸 그랬다</b> (I shouldn't have).","forms":[["Verb, no 받침","갈 걸 그랬다 · 물어볼 걸 그랬다"],["Verb, 받침","먹을 걸 그랬다 · 읽을 걸 그랬다"],["Negative","하지 말 걸 그랬다"],["Short (casual)","-(으)ㄹ걸: 미리 물어볼걸."]],"rules":["Verbs only. The regret is about the past, but no past tense on the verb.","Ending: <b>-(으)ㄹ 걸 그랬어요</b>. Casual short form: <b>-(으)ㄹ걸</b> (falling tone).","Mostly about the speaker's own choices. For criticizing others, -었어야지요 or -지 그랬어요 is more common.","Don't confuse with -(으)ㄹ걸요? (rising tone), which is a guess: 아마 벌써 갔을걸요?","Compared with -었어야 했다: -을 걸 그랬다 sounds softer, more like a sigh to yourself."],"ex":[["선배한테 반말을 해 버렸어요. 처음부터 존댓말을 **쓸 걸 그랬어요**.","I ended up using casual speech with an upperclassman. I should have used formal speech from the start."],["한국 예절에 대해서 미리 좀 **알아볼 걸 그랬어요**.","I wish I'd looked into Korean etiquette a bit beforehand."],["그런 농담은 **하지 말 걸 그랬어요**. 분위기가 이상해졌어요.","I shouldn't have made that joke. The mood got weird."]]}],"v":[["존댓말","honorific speech","Opposite: 반말. <b>존댓말을 쓰다 / 하다</b>. Also called 높임말.","처음 만난 사람에게는 **존댓말**을 쓰는 게 기본이에요.","Using formal speech with someone you've just met is the basic rule."],["놓다²","to drop (formal speech), speak casually","This sense: <b>말을 놓다</b> = switch to 반말. 말씀 낮추세요 / 편하게 말 놓으세요 = please speak casually to me.","우리 이제 친해졌으니까 말 **놓을까요**?","We're close now, so shall we drop the formalities?"],["숙이다","to bow, lower (one's head)","<b>고개/머리를 숙이다</b>. Also figurative: 고개를 숙이다 = be humble, admit defeat.","어른께 인사할 때는 고개를 **숙여요**.","When you greet an elder, you bow your head."],["존중하다","to respect","<b>N을/를 존중하다</b>: 의견/문화/선택을 존중하다. More about recognizing value than 존경하다 (admire someone above you).","서로 다른 문화를 **존중하는** 태도가 필요해요.","We need an attitude of respecting each other's cultures."],["무조건","unconditionally, no matter what","Can be positive (무조건 믿어요) or critical (thoughtlessly): 무조건 따르다.","나이가 많다고 **무조건** 옳은 건 아니에요.","Being older doesn't automatically make someone right."],["아무튼","anyway, in any case","Wraps up or changes the subject: 아무튼 고마워요. Same as 어쨌든.","**아무튼** 처음 만났을 때는 존댓말을 쓰는 게 안전해요.","Anyway, it's safest to use formal speech when you first meet."]],"x":[["격식적","formal","For speech, settings, dress: 격식적인 자리, 격식을 차리다 (observe formalities).","면접 같은 **격식적**인 자리에서는 '-습니다'를 써요.","In formal settings like interviews, use '-습니다'."],["비격식적","informal","비- + 격식적. 해요체 is 비격식적 존댓말.","친구들 사이에서는 **비격식적**인 표현을 많이 써요.","Among friends, people use a lot of informal expressions."],["연령","age","Formal word for 나이: 연령대 (age group), 연령 제한.","**연령**에 따라 쓰는 말이 달라지기도 해요.","The words people use sometimes differ depending on age."],["인간관계","human relationships","<b>인간관계가 좋다 / 넓다</b>, 인간관계를 맺다.","말투는 **인간관계**에 큰 영향을 줘요.","The way you talk has a big effect on your relationships."],["지위","status, position","Social or job rank: 사회적 지위, 지위가 높다.","한국어는 상대방의 **지위**에 따라 말투가 달라져요.","In Korean, how you speak changes depending on the other person's status."],["공손하다","polite, courteous","Respectful in manner and words: 공손하게 인사하다. Stronger and more humble than 친절하다.","그 학생은 항상 **공손하게** 말해요.","That student always speaks courteously."]]},{"n":2,"t":"문화 차이","g":[{"f":"치고","en":"(1) for an N (surprisingly); (2) every N without exception","core":"Particle attached to nouns with two uses. (1) <b>Exception</b>: \"for an N, it's unusual\": 외국인치고 매운 걸 잘 먹네요. (2) <b>No exception</b>: \"there's no N that doesn't…\", always with a negative: 한국 사람치고 김치 싫어하는 사람 없어요.","forms":[["Noun","외국인치고 · 아이치고 · 겨울치고"],["Emphasis","N치고는 (exception use)"]],"rules":["Nouns only: <b>N치고(는)</b>.","Exception use: compares to a typical expectation of N. Often <b>치고는</b>: 처음치고는 잘했어요.","No-exception use: followed by a negative or rhetorical question: <b>N치고 -지 않는 N이 없다</b>.","Exception use can sound like a backhanded compliment (외국인치고 잘하네요). Use it carefully about people.","Weather and prices are common topics: 11월치고 따뜻하다, 서울치고 싸다."],"ex":[["11월**치고** 날씨가 꽤 포근하네요.","It's pretty mild for November."],["한국 사람**치고** 명절 음식 안 좋아하는 사람은 드물어요.","It's rare to find a Korean who doesn't like holiday food."],["처음 해 보는 거**치고는** 정말 잘했어요.","For your first time, you did really well."]]},{"f":"-는 것처럼","en":"as if; like (the way) X","core":"Compares an action or situation to another one: \"like X,\" \"as X does,\" or \"as if X.\" The clause-version of N처럼 (3과).","forms":[["Verb (present)","하는 것처럼 · 먹는 것처럼"],["Verb (past)","본 것처럼 · 말한 것처럼"],["Adjective","좋은 것처럼 · 아픈 것처럼"],["Noun","N인 것처럼 (가족인 것처럼)"]],"rules":["Verb present -는, past -(으)ㄴ, future -(으)ㄹ, adjective -(으)ㄴ, noun -인 + 것처럼.","Two senses: <b>the same way</b> (아까 말한 것처럼 = as I said earlier) and <b>as if, pretending</b> (모르는 것처럼 행동하다).","Compare <b>-는 듯이</b> (10과): similar \"as if,\" but more literary.","Often with 마치 for \"as if\": 마치 한국 사람인 것처럼 말해요."],"ex":[["한국에서는 처음 만난 사람이 나이를 묻는 게 **당연한 것처럼** 느껴져요.","In Korea, it feels as though it's natural for someone you've just met to ask your age."],["아까 **말한 것처럼** 한국에서는 두 손으로 물건을 건네요.","As I said earlier, in Korea you hand things over with both hands."],["처음엔 다 **이해한 것처럼** 고개를 끄덕였는데, 사실 하나도 몰랐어요.","At first I nodded as if I understood everything, but actually I had no idea."]]}],"v":[["일행","party, group (traveling together)","People you're with: <b>일행이 있다</b>. At restaurants: 일행이 몇 분이세요? (How many in your party?)","**일행**이 아직 안 와서 먼저 자리에 앉아 있었어요.","The rest of my group hadn't arrived yet, so I sat down first."],["건네다","to hand over; to say (to someone)","<b>물건을 건네다</b> (hand over); <b>말을 건네다</b> (speak to, strike up a conversation).","어른께 물건을 **건넬** 때는 두 손으로 드려요.","When handing something to an elder, use both hands."],["포근하다","mild, cozy, soft and warm","Weather (mild winter day), blankets, atmosphere: 포근한 날씨, 포근한 이불.","겨울인데 오늘은 날씨가 **포근하네요**.","It's winter, but the weather today is mild."],["간혹","occasionally, now and then","Less frequent than 가끔, slightly formal.","**간혹** 문화 차이 때문에 오해가 생기기도 해요.","Now and then, misunderstandings happen because of cultural differences."],["왠지","somehow, for some reason","Spelled 왠지 (from 왜인지). Don't confuse with 웬 (what kind of).","**왠지** 그 사람이 화가 난 것 같았어요.","For some reason, that person seemed angry."]],"x":[["고유문화","native culture, indigenous culture","고유 = inherent, unique: 고유한 전통, 고유 명사.","각 나라에는 그 나라만의 **고유문화**가 있어요.","Each country has its own unique culture."],["대중가요","pop songs","Popular music. K-pop is a kind of 대중가요.","**대중가요**를 들으면서 한국어를 공부했어요.","I studied Korean by listening to pop songs."],["대중문화","popular culture","대중 = the masses. Movies, dramas, music, etc.","한국 **대중문화**가 전 세계적으로 인기가 많아요.","Korean pop culture is very popular all over the world."],["주거","housing, residence","Formal: 주거 문화, 주거 환경, 주거비.","한국의 **주거** 문화 중에 온돌이 제일 신기했어요.","Of all Korean housing culture, the ondol floor heating amazed me the most."],["충격","shock","<b>충격을 받다</b>, 문화 충격 (culture shock), 충격적이다.","처음 한국에 왔을 때 문화 **충격**을 많이 받았어요.","I got a lot of culture shock when I first came to Korea."],["현대","modern times","현대 사회, 현대인 (10과), 현대적. Contrast: 전통.","**현대** 사회에서는 전통 예절이 많이 바뀌었어요.","Traditional etiquette has changed a lot in modern society."],["받아들이다","to accept, embrace","Ideas, cultures, situations: <b>문화를 받아들이다</b>, 현실을 받아들이다.","새로운 문화를 열린 마음으로 **받아들이려고** 해요.","I try to accept new cultures with an open mind."],["접하다","to come into contact with, encounter","<b>N을/를 접하다</b>: 문화/정보/소식을 접하다. Formal.","인터넷을 통해 다양한 나라의 문화를 **접할** 수 있어요.","You can come across the cultures of many countries through the internet."]]}]});
GUIDE.en.push({"n":13,"t":"여행과 발견","en":"Travel and discovery","units":[{"n":1,"t":"여행과 날씨","g":[{"f":"-는 김에","en":"while (you're) at it; taking the opportunity","core":"While doing X, you also take the chance to do Y, which you might not have planned. The opportunity comes from X.","forms":[["Verb (present)","가는 김에 · 나가는 김에"],["Verb (past)","온 김에 · 시작한 김에"],["Noun","N 하는 김에 (청소하는 김에)"]],"rules":["Verbs only. Present -는 김에 (while doing), past -(으)ㄴ 김에 (now that X has happened): 부산에 <b>온 김에</b>.","The second action is extra, taking advantage of the first.","Compare <b>-을 겸</b> (1과): -을 겸 sets multiple purposes up front. -는 김에 is opportunistic, piggybacking on something already happening.","Very common in everyday speech: 나가는 김에 우유 좀 사다 줘."],"ex":[["제주도에 출장 **간 김에** 하루 더 있으면서 여행을 했어요.","Since I was in Jeju on a business trip anyway, I stayed an extra day and traveled around."],["날씨가 화창해서 산책하**는 김에** 사진도 많이 찍었어요.","The weather was so nice that I took lots of pictures while I was out walking."],["말이 **나온 김에** 이번 주말에 바다 보러 갈래요?","Now that we're on the subject, want to go see the ocean this weekend?"]]},{"f":"만 해도","en":"just N alone; even (as recently as) N","core":"Picks one example or point in time to show something is true, often to emphasize a contrast or how much things have changed. \"Just yesterday it was…\" or \"Just this one thing alone…\"","forms":[["Noun (time)","어제만 해도 · 작년만 해도 · 10년 전만 해도"],["Noun (example)","서울만 해도 · 우리 반만 해도 · 저만 해도"]],"rules":["Attaches to nouns: <b>N만 해도</b>.","Time use: shows a recent contrast with now: <b>어제만 해도</b> 따뜻했는데 오늘은 추워요.","Example use: one case stands for a general point: <b>서울만 해도</b> 공원이 수천 개예요.","Often followed by -었는데 to set up the contrast."],"ex":[["**어제만 해도** 화창했는데 오늘은 하루 종일 비가 오네요.","Just yesterday it was sunny, but today it's been raining all day."],["**지난주만 해도** 일교차가 크지 않았는데 갑자기 추워졌어요.","Even last week the temperature didn't swing much, but it suddenly got cold."],["**저만 해도** 날씨 때문에 여행 계획을 몇 번이나 바꿨어요.","Take me, for example: I've changed my travel plans several times because of the weather."]]}],"v":[["발길","steps, footsteps (going somewhere)","<b>발길을 돌리다</b> (turn back), 발길이 끊기다 (no one comes anymore), 발길이 닿다.","비가 너무 많이 와서 결국 **발길**을 돌렸어요.","It was raining so hard that we ended up turning back."],["빗줄기","streaks of rain, rainfall","<b>빗줄기가 굵어지다 / 약해지다</b>.","갑자기 **빗줄기**가 굵어져서 카페에 들어갔어요.","The rain suddenly got heavier, so we went into a café."],["넘다","to exceed; to go over","Numbers (30도가 넘다), time (12시가 넘다), and crossing (산을 넘다).","한낮 기온이 30도가 **넘어서** 너무 더웠어요.","The midday temperature went over 30 degrees, so it was too hot."],["돌리다","to turn; to redirect","<b>발길/방향을 돌리다</b>. Also 세탁기를 돌리다 (run the washer), 화제를 돌리다 (change the subject).","날씨 때문에 차를 **돌려서** 집으로 왔어요.","We turned the car around and came home because of the weather."],["부옇다","hazy, cloudy (whitish)","Sky or air with dust or fog: <b>하늘이 부옇다</b>. ㅎ irregular: 부예요. Common with 미세먼지.","미세먼지 때문에 하늘이 **부옇게** 보여요.","The sky looks hazy because of the fine dust."],["화창하다","sunny and clear (pleasant)","Nice, bright weather, often spring: <b>화창한 봄날</b>.","**화창한** 날씨 덕분에 여행을 즐겁게 했어요.","Thanks to the sunny weather, we had a fun trip."]],"x":[["일교차","daily temperature range","Difference between day and night temperatures: <b>일교차가 크다</b>. Classic weather-forecast phrase, especially in spring and fall.","요즘 **일교차**가 커서 감기 걸리기 쉬워요.","The temperature swings a lot these days, so it's easy to catch a cold."],["걷히다","to clear up, lift","For clouds, fog, haze: <b>안개/구름이 걷히다</b>.","오후가 되니까 안개가 **걷혔어요**.","The fog lifted in the afternoon."],["굵어지다","to get thicker, heavier","For rain: <b>빗줄기가 굵어지다</b>. 굵다 = thick.","오후부터 빗줄기가 점점 **굵어질** 거라고 해요.","They say the rain will get heavier starting in the afternoon."],["벌어지다","to widen; to happen, break out","(1) A gap widens: 일교차가 벌어지다, 차이가 벌어지다. (2) An event happens: 싸움이 벌어지다.","아침과 낮의 기온 차이가 10도 이상 **벌어졌어요**.","The temperature gap between morning and midday widened to more than 10 degrees."],["짙다","thick, dense; dark (color)","For fog, color, makeup: <b>안개가 짙다</b>, 짙은 색.","**짙은** 안개 때문에 비행기가 늦게 출발했어요.","The plane left late because of thick fog."]]},{"n":2,"t":"혼자 떠나는 여행","g":[{"f":"-다가는","en":"if you keep doing X, (something bad) will happen","core":"A warning: continuing X will lead to a bad result. Stronger than -다 보면 (5과), which can be neutral or positive.","forms":[["Verb","이렇게 하다가는 · 계속 일하다가는"],["Adjective","이렇게 바쁘다가는"]],"rules":["Stem + 다가는. Often with 이렇게, 계속, 매일, 그러.","The second clause is a bad result, usually future or a guess: -(으)ㄹ 거예요, -겠어요, -(으)ㄹ지도 몰라요.","No commands or suggestions in the second clause.","Short form in speech: <b>-다간</b>: 그러다간 큰일 나요.","Compare -다 보면: neutral or encouraging. -다가는: always a warning."],"ex":[["이렇게 쉬지 않고 **일하다가는** 몸이 완전히 망가질 거예요.","If you keep working nonstop like this, you'll completely wreck your body."],["계획 없이 **여행하다가는** 숙소를 못 구할 수도 있어요.","If you travel without a plan, you might not be able to find a place to stay."],["이렇게 매일 야근**하다가는** 혼자 여행 갈 시간도 없겠어요.","If I keep working late every day like this, I won't even have time for a solo trip."]]},{"f":"-게 마련이다","en":"(it's) bound to X; X naturally happens","core":"States that something naturally or inevitably happens, as a general rule of life. Very close to -는 법이다 (10과).","forms":[["Verb / adjective stem","실수하게 마련이다 · 힘들게 마련이다 · 변하게 마련이다"]],"rules":["Stem + 게 마련이다, regardless of 받침. Same as <b>-기 마련이다</b>.","Present tense for general truths: 누구나 처음에는 <b>실수하게 마련이에요</b>.","Often used to comfort or reassure, like -는 법이다.","Not for one-off specific events. It's for things that happen to everyone."],"ex":[["혼자 여행을 하면 처음에는 누구나 외롭**게 마련이에요**.","Anyone traveling alone is bound to feel lonely at first."],["낯선 곳에 가면 새로운 것을 깨닫**게 마련이지요**.","When you go somewhere unfamiliar, you naturally come to realize new things."],["좋은 시간은 빨리 지나가**게 마련이에요**.","Good times always pass quickly."]]}],"v":[["석양","sunset, the setting sun","夕陽. Literary and visual: <b>석양이 지다</b>, 아름다운 석양.","바닷가에서 본 **석양**을 잊을 수가 없어요.","I can't forget the sunset I saw at the beach."],["벗어나다","to get away from, escape","<b>N에서 벗어나다</b>: 일상/도시/스트레스에서 벗어나다.","가끔은 바쁜 일상에서 **벗어나고** 싶어요.","Sometimes I want to get away from my busy daily life."],["식히다²","to cool down (one's head or mind)","This sense: <b>머리를 식히다</b> = clear your head, take a breather.","머리 좀 **식히려고** 혼자 바다에 갔어요.","I went to the ocean alone to clear my head."],["여유롭다","relaxed, leisurely, unhurried","Having time or space to spare: <b>여유로운 시간</b>. ㅂ irregular: 여유로워요. 여유 = leeway.","혼자 여행하니까 **여유롭게** 구경할 수 있었어요.","Traveling alone, I could look around at my own pace."],["오로지","solely, only","Emphatic \"only\": <b>오로지 N만</b>. Stronger and more literary than 오직.","이번 여행은 **오로지** 저를 위한 시간이었어요.","This trip was time just for me."],["완전히","completely, totally","완전하다 = complete. In speech also 완전 (slang intensifier: 완전 좋아).","여행을 다녀와서 기분이 **완전히** 달라졌어요.","After the trip, my mood was completely different."]],"x":[["시야","field of vision; perspective","Literal (시야가 넓다 = wide view) and figurative (broad-minded): <b>시야를 넓히다</b>.","여행을 통해서 **시야**가 넓어졌어요.","Traveling broadened my perspective."],["깨닫다","to realize","ㄷ irregular: 깨달아요, 깨달았어요. A moment of insight. Stronger than 알게 되다.","혼자 여행하면서 많은 것을 **깨달았어요**.","I realized a lot of things while traveling alone."],["사라지다","to disappear, vanish","Physical or emotional: 스트레스가 사라지다.","바다를 보니까 걱정이 다 **사라지는** 것 같았어요.","Looking at the ocean, it felt like all my worries disappeared."],["새롭다","new, fresh","ㅂ irregular: 새로워요. Also <b>새롭게 느껴지다</b> (feel fresh again).","익숙한 곳도 혼자 가니까 **새롭게** 느껴졌어요.","Even familiar places felt new when I went alone."],["재충전하다","to recharge","Mostly about energy or the mind: <b>몸과 마음을 재충전하다</b>.","여행으로 에너지를 **재충전했어요**.","I recharged my energy with a trip."]]}]});
GUIDE.en.push({"n":14,"t":"대중문화","en":"Pop culture","units":[{"n":1,"t":"방송과 영상","g":[{"f":"-는다고요","en":"(1) You said X? (checking, surprise); (2) I said X! (repeating, emphasis)","core":"Two uses. (1) <b>Checking or surprise</b> (rising tone): repeating what the other person said: \"X, you say?\" (2) <b>Emphasis</b> (falling tone): repeating what you said because they didn't catch it or didn't believe you: \"I said X.\"","forms":[["Verb","간다고요 · 먹는다고요 · 했다고요"],["Adjective","재미있다고요 · 바쁘다고요"],["Noun","범인이라고요 · 학생이라고요"],["Questions / commands","-냐고요 / -(으)라고요 / -자고요"]],"rules":["Quoted forms: verb -ㄴ/는다고요, adjective -다고요, noun -(이)라고요.","Rising intonation = surprise or checking: 그 사람이 범인이<b>라고요</b>?","Falling intonation = repeating yourself: 저 내일 못 간<b>다고요</b>.","Repeating a question: <b>-냐고요</b> (뭐 하냐고요). A command: <b>-(으)라고요</b>. A suggestion: <b>-자고요</b>.","The emphasis use can sound a little annoyed, depending on tone."],"ex":[["A: 그 드라마 범인이 주인공 친구였어. B: 네? 친구가 범인이**라고요**?","A: The culprit in that drama was the main character's friend. B: What? The friend was the culprit?"],["A: 뭐라고 했어요? B: 그 예능 정말 재미있**다고요**.","A: What did you say? B: I said that variety show is really fun."],["A: 지금 몇 시냐고요? 벌써 열두 시예요.","A: You're asking what time it is? It's already twelve."]]},{"f":"-었더라면","en":"if (only) X had happened (counterfactual)","core":"Imagines a past situation that didn't happen, then states the different result. Often expresses regret or relief. Stronger and more \"hypothetical past\" than -었으면.","forms":[["Verb / adj, ㅏ/ㅗ","봤더라면 · 알았더라면"],["Verb / adj, other","들었더라면 · 했더라면"],["Noun","N이었더라면 / 였더라면"]],"rules":["Second clause is usually <b>-었을 거예요</b>, <b>-었을 텐데</b> (17과), or <b>-었을 것이다</b>.","For regret: 미리 <b>알았더라면</b> 그 방송을 봤을 텐데.","For relief: 그때 <b>안 갔더라면</b> 큰일 날 뻔했어요.","Same meaning as -었으면, but -었더라면 sounds more dramatic and clearly counterfactual."],"ex":[["그 프로그램을 처음부터 **봤더라면** 내용을 더 잘 이해했을 거예요.","If I'd watched the show from the beginning, I'd have understood it better."],["그 배우가 **출연했더라면** 시청률이 훨씬 높았을 텐데요.","If that actor had been in it, the ratings would have been much higher."],["미리 **알았더라면** 표를 예매했을 거예요.","If I'd known in advance, I would have booked tickets."]]}],"v":[["범인","culprit, criminal","For crime stories and mysteries: <b>범인을 잡다 / 찾다</b>.","드라마 마지막 회에서 **범인**이 밝혀졌어요.","The culprit was revealed in the final episode of the drama."],["소재","subject matter, material (for a story)","What a story or show is about: <b>N을/를 소재로 하다</b> (to use N as material).","이 영화는 실제 사건을 **소재**로 만들었어요.","This movie was based on a real event."],["예능","variety / entertainment programs","Short for 예능 프로그램. Korean-specific genre: reality and game shows with celebrities.","저는 드라마보다 **예능**을 더 자주 봐요.","I watch variety shows more often than dramas."],["오가다","to come and go; to be exchanged","Going back and forth: <b>대화/의견이 오가다</b>, 사람들이 오가다.","방송 중에 출연자들 사이에 재미있는 대화가 **오갔어요**.","There was a fun back-and-forth between the guests during the broadcast."],["일어나다","to happen, occur","Besides \"get up\": <b>사건/문제가 일어나다</b>.","방송 중에 예상하지 못한 일이 **일어났어요**.","Something unexpected happened during the broadcast."],["출연하다","to appear (on a show, in a film)","<b>N에 출연하다</b>. 출연자 = cast member, guest.","좋아하는 배우가 그 예능에 **출연했어요**.","My favorite actor appeared on that variety show."],["흥미롭다","interesting, intriguing","Formal-ish for 재미있다, about ideas or content. ㅂ irregular: 흥미로워요. 흥미 (2과).","실제 사건을 다룬 다큐멘터리라서 더 **흥미로웠어요**.","It was even more interesting because it was a documentary about a real event."]],"x":[["사회자","host, MC (of an event or show)","<b>사회를 보다</b> = to host or MC.","그 **사회자**는 말을 정말 재미있게 해요.","That host is really funny."],["시청자","viewer (TV)","시청하다 = watch (TV). 시청률 = ratings.","이 프로그램은 **시청자**들의 의견을 많이 반영해요.","This program reflects a lot of viewers' opinions."],["제작자","producer, maker","제작하다 = produce, make.","**제작자**가 인터뷰에서 다음 시즌 계획을 말했어요.","The producer talked about plans for the next season in an interview."],["진행자","host, presenter","Runs the show. Very close to 사회자; 진행자 is common for news and talk shows.","**진행자**가 출연자들에게 질문을 했어요.","The host asked the guests questions."],["출연자","cast member, guest","Anyone who appears on a program.","이번 주 **출연자**가 누구인지 궁금해요.","I'm curious who this week's guests are."],["평가자","evaluator, judge","For audition shows and contests: 심사위원 is also common.","**평가자**들의 점수가 생각보다 낮았어요.","The judges' scores were lower than I expected."],["담당하다","to be in charge of","<b>N을/를 담당하다</b>, 담당자 (4과).","그 PD가 인기 예능을 **담당하고** 있어요.","That producer is in charge of a popular variety show."],["시청하다","to watch (TV, broadcast)","Formal for 보다 with TV: 시청해 주셔서 감사합니다.","요즘은 TV보다 휴대폰으로 방송을 **시청하는** 사람이 많아요.","These days lots of people watch broadcasts on their phones rather than on TV."],["제작하다","to produce, make","Films, shows, products: 드라마를 제작하다.","그 회사는 다큐멘터리를 주로 **제작해요**.","That company mainly produces documentaries."],["사회를 보다","to host, MC","Idiomatic: 결혼식/행사에서 사회를 보다.","친구 결혼식에서 제가 **사회를 봤어요**.","I MC'd my friend's wedding."]]},{"n":2,"t":"1인 방송","g":[{"f":"에 관한","en":"about, regarding (before a noun)","core":"Noun-modifying version of 에 대해서 (4과): <b>N에 관한 N</b> = \"an N about N.\" Formal and very common in written Korean and presentations.","forms":[["Noun + noun","환경에 관한 영상 · 여행에 관한 책"],["Adverbial","N에 관해(서) = N에 대해(서)"]],"rules":["Before a noun: <b>N에 관한 N</b>. Before a verb: <b>N에 관해(서)</b>.","<b>N에 대한 N</b> means the same and is more common in speech. 에 관한 is a bit more formal.","Common with content words: 영상, 정보, 책, 기사, 연구, 이야기, 강의."],"ex":[["저는 요리**에 관한** 1인 방송을 자주 봐요.","I often watch one-person broadcasts about cooking."],["그 유튜버는 한국 문화**에 관한** 콘텐츠를 만들어요.","That YouTuber makes content about Korean culture."],["오늘은 1인 방송의 장단점**에 관해서** 이야기해 보겠습니다.","Today I'll talk about the pros and cons of one-person broadcasting."]]},{"f":"-는다면야","en":"if X (is the case), then of course…","core":"-는다면 (if) + 야 (emphasis). Sets a condition and says that under that condition, the result is naturally fine or obviously true. Often used to agree on a condition: \"Well, if you put it that way, sure.\"","forms":[["Verb","한다면야 · 도와준다면야 · 했다면야"],["Adjective","재미있다면야 · 싸다면야"],["Noun","친구라면야 · 무료라면야"]],"rules":["Quoted forms: verb -ㄴ/는다면야, adjective -다면야, noun -(이)라면야.","Second clause is usually positive or agreeing: 좋지요, 괜찮아요, 할 수 있지요, 당연하지요.","Implies \"only under that condition\": the speaker is conditional or reluctant otherwise.","Casual: -는다면야 is often followed by -지 (그럼 좋지)."],"ex":[["콘텐츠가 정말 **재미있다면야** 광고가 좀 있어도 괜찮아요.","If the content is really fun, a few ads are fine."],["네가 같이 **해 준다면야** 나도 1인 방송 한번 해 보고 싶지.","If you'll do it with me, then sure, I'd like to try one-person broadcasting."],["시청자들이 **원한다면야** 실시간 방송을 더 자주 할게요.","If the viewers want it, then I'll do live broadcasts more often."]]}],"v":[["반응","reaction, response","<b>반응이 좋다 / 뜨겁다</b>, 반응을 보이다.","새 영상에 대한 시청자들의 **반응**이 정말 좋았어요.","Viewers' reaction to the new video was really good."],["실시간","real time","<b>실시간 방송</b> (live stream), 실시간 검색어, 실시간으로.","**실시간**으로 시청자와 대화할 수 있어서 재미있어요.","It's fun because you can talk with viewers in real time."],["콘텐츠","content","Loanword. 영상 콘텐츠, 콘텐츠를 만들다.","요즘은 누구나 **콘텐츠**를 만들 수 있어요.","These days anyone can make content."],["끌다","to attract, draw; to drag","<b>인기를 끌다</b> (become popular), 관심/시선을 끌다.","그 채널은 짧은 영상으로 큰 인기를 **끌었어요**.","That channel became really popular with short videos."],["반영하다","to reflect, incorporate","<b>의견을 반영하다</b>. Passive: 반영되다.","시청자 의견을 **반영해서** 다음 영상을 만들어요.","I make the next video incorporating viewers' feedback."],["참여하다","to participate","<b>N에 참여하다</b>. 참여형 방송 = interactive broadcast.","시청자들이 직접 방송에 **참여할** 수 있어요.","Viewers can take part in the broadcast directly."],["그때그때","each time, as things come up","Handling things as they happen, not in advance: <b>그때그때 다르다</b>.","방송 내용은 시청자 반응에 따라 **그때그때** 달라져요.","The content of the stream changes each time depending on the viewers' reactions."]],"x":[["기획","planning (a project)","<b>기획하다</b>, 기획안, 기획자. More project-oriented than 계획.","좋은 콘텐츠는 **기획**부터 꼼꼼해야 해요.","Good content needs careful planning from the start."],["생중계","live broadcast","<b>생중계하다</b>, 경기를 생중계로 보다.","오늘 경기는 인터넷으로 **생중계**돼요.","Today's game is being broadcast live online."],["양방향","two-way, interactive","Opposite: 일방향 (one-way). 양방향 소통.","1인 방송은 **양방향** 소통이 가능하다는 게 장점이에요.","The upside of one-person broadcasting is that two-way communication is possible."],["편집","editing","<b>편집하다</b>, 영상 편집, 편집자.","10분짜리 영상 **편집**에 하루가 걸렸어요.","Editing a 10-minute video took a whole day."],["조회 수","view count","<b>조회 수가 높다 / 오르다</b>. 조회하다 = look up.","그 영상은 하루 만에 **조회 수**가 백만이 넘었어요.","That video passed a million views in one day."]]}]});
GUIDE.en.push({"n":15,"t":"여가 생활","en":"Leisure","units":[{"n":1,"t":"남산 둘레길","g":[{"f":"-는가 하면","en":"(some) X, while (others) Y; not only X, but also Y","core":"Presents contrasting or varied cases side by side: \"Some people X, while others Y.\" It can also add a second example in the same direction: \"X, and on top of that, Y.\"","forms":[["Verb","걷는가 하면 · 쉬는가 하면 · 했는가 하면"],["Adjective","조용한가 하면 · 많은가 하면"],["Noun","N인가 하면"]],"rules":["Verb -는가 하면, adjective -(으)ㄴ가 하면, past -았/었는가 하면.","Classic frame: <b>어떤 사람은 -는가 하면 어떤 사람은 -는다</b>.","Good for describing variety: places, people, opinions. Useful in TOPIK writing too.","Short form <b>-는가 하면</b> also works for the same subject: 이 길은 숲이 있는가 하면 전망대도 있어요."],"ex":[["둘레길에서 천천히 산책하**는 사람이 있는가 하면** 뛰는 사람도 있어요.","On the trail, some people stroll slowly while others run."],["남산 둘레길은 조용한 숲길이 **있는가 하면** 서울 시내가 다 보이는 곳도 있어요.","The Namsan trail has quiet forest paths, and also spots where you can see all of downtown Seoul."],["주말에 집에서 **쉬는 사람이 있는가 하면** 밖에서 운동하는 사람도 있지요.","Some people rest at home on weekends, while others exercise outdoors."]]},{"f":"-는다는","en":"(N) that says X; (N) that X (quoted content)","core":"Short for -는다고 하는. Turns quoted or reported content into a modifier for a noun: \"the news that…\", \"the story that…\" The noun is usually something with content: 소문, 이야기, 말, 생각, 뉴스, 소식, 의견.","forms":[["Verb","간다는 · 먹는다는 · 했다는"],["Adjective","좋다는 · 아름답다는"],["Noun","N(이)라는 (매력이라는)"],["Question / command","-냐는 / -(으)라는 / -자는"]],"rules":["Quoted forms: verb -ㄴ/는다는, adjective -다는, noun -(이)라는.","Followed by content nouns: <b>-다는 소문 / 이야기 / 말 / 생각 / 뜻 / 소식</b>.","Compare <b>N(이)라는 N</b> (a thing called N): 둘레길이라는 산책로.","Questions: -냐는 질문. Commands: -(으)라는 말. Suggestions: -자는 의견."],"ex":[["남산 둘레길이 가을에 특히 **아름답다는** 이야기를 들었어요.","I heard that the Namsan trail is especially beautiful in the fall."],["걷기만 해도 스트레스가 **풀린다는** 말이 정말 맞는 것 같아요.","I think the saying that just walking relieves stress is really true."],["'금강산도 식후경'**이라는** 말처럼 걷기 전에 밥부터 먹었어요.","As the saying 'even Geumgangsan after a meal' goes, we ate first before walking."]]}],"v":[["둘레","circumference; perimeter","Around the edge of something: 둘레길 = trail circling a mountain. 허리둘레 = waist size.","**둘레**가 7km 정도인 길이라서 두 시간쯤 걸려요.","The trail is about 7 km around, so it takes roughly two hours."],["매력","charm, appeal","<b>매력이 있다 / 넘치다</b>, 매력적이다, 매력을 느끼다.","남산 둘레길의 **매력**은 도심 가까이에 숲이 있다는 거예요.","The charm of the Namsan trail is that there's a forest right near downtown."],["산책로","walking path, trail","산책 + -로 (road). 공원 산책로.","이 **산책로**는 밤에도 조명이 있어서 안전해요.","This walking path is lit at night, so it's safe."],["삶","life","Noun from 살다. More reflective than 생활: <b>삶의 질</b> (quality of life), 바쁜 삶.","바쁜 **삶** 속에서도 걷는 시간은 꼭 가지려고 해요.","Even in a busy life, I try to make time for walking."],["표지판","signpost, sign","Direction or warning signs on roads and trails.","**표지판**을 따라가면 길을 잃지 않아요.","If you follow the signs, you won't get lost."],["금강산도 식후경","even Geumgangsan after a meal (eat first)","Proverb: no matter how great the sight, food comes first. 식후경 = sightseeing after eating.","**금강산도 식후경**이라고, 등산 전에 김밥부터 먹어요.","As they say, food comes first. Let's eat gimbap before the hike."]],"x":[["고래 싸움에 새우 등 터진다","when whales fight, the shrimp's back bursts","Bystanders get hurt when the powerful fight.","부장님들이 싸우는 바람에 우리만 힘들어요. **고래 싸움에 새우 등 터진다**더니.","Because the managers are fighting, only we suffer. Like they say, the shrimp gets crushed when whales fight."],["고생 끝에 낙이 온다","after hardship comes joy","Encouragement: hard times will pay off.","**고생 끝에 낙이 온다**고, 열심히 준비한 만큼 좋은 결과가 있을 거예요.","After hardship comes joy. You prepared so hard, you'll get a good result."],["그림의 떡","pie in the sky (a rice cake in a picture)","Something you want but can't have.","돈이 없으니까 그 여행은 **그림의 떡**이에요.","I don't have money, so that trip is just pie in the sky."],["돌다리도 두들겨 보고 건너라","tap even a stone bridge before crossing","Be careful even when something seems safe.","**돌다리도 두들겨 보고 건너라**고, 계약하기 전에 다시 확인해 보세요.","Better safe than sorry. Double-check before signing the contract."],["믿는 도끼에 발등 찍힌다","the axe you trust chops your foot","Betrayed by someone you trusted.","제일 친한 친구가 비밀을 말했어요. **믿는 도끼에 발등 찍힌** 기분이에요.","My best friend spilled my secret. I feel betrayed by the person I trusted most."],["배보다 배꼽이 크다","the belly button is bigger than the belly","A side cost is bigger than the main thing.","물건값보다 배송비가 더 비싸요. **배보다 배꼽이 크네요**.","The shipping costs more than the item. The extra cost is bigger than the main thing."],["시작이 반이다","starting is half the battle","Encouragement to just begin.","**시작이 반이다**! 일단 둘레길 입구까지만 가 봐요.","Starting is half the battle! Let's at least walk to the trail entrance."],["호랑이도 제 말 하면 온다","speak of the tiger and it appears","Speak of the devil.","**호랑이도 제 말 하면 온다**더니, 마침 민수 씨가 왔네요.","Speak of the devil, here comes Minsu."]]},{"n":2,"t":"경제적인 여가 생활","g":[{"f":"-는다지요?","en":"I heard X, right? (checking hearsay)","core":"Short for -는다고 하지요? The speaker heard something and checks it with the listener: \"I heard that X, is that right?\"","forms":[["Verb","간다지요? · 빌려준다지요? · 했다지요?"],["Adjective","싸다지요? · 좋다지요?"],["Noun","무료라지요? · 학생이라지요?"]],"rules":["Quoted forms: verb -ㄴ/는다지요, adjective -다지요, noun -(이)라지요.","Spoken short form: <b>-는다죠?</b>","Rising intonation. It's a question to confirm hearsay, not to get new information.","Compare -대요 (just reporting) and -다면서요? (I heard…, right?, more surprised)."],"ex":[["한강공원에서 자전거를 싸게 **빌려준다지요**?","I heard they rent bikes cheaply at Hangang Park, right?"],["그 박물관은 매달 마지막 수요일에 **무료라지요**?","I heard that museum is free on the last Wednesday of every month, right?"],["요즘 구청에서 무료 운동 강좌를 **연다지요**?","I heard the district office is running free exercise classes these days, right?"]]},{"f":"-든지 -든지","en":"either X or Y (whichever, it doesn't matter)","core":"Presents options and says any of them is fine, or that the result is the same whichever happens. Similar to -거나, but -든지 stresses that the choice doesn't matter.","forms":[["Verb / adjective","가든지 말든지 · 걷든지 자전거를 타든지"],["Noun","N(이)든지: 산이든지 바다든지"],["Short","-든 -든"]],"rules":["Stem + 든지 for each option. Often ends with 하다: <b>-든지 -든지 하세요</b>.","<b>-든지 말든지</b> = whether you do it or not (can sound dismissive: 하든지 말든지 마음대로 해).","With question words: <b>무엇이든지, 언제든지, 어디든지</b> = anything, anytime, anywhere.","Don't confuse with <b>-던지</b> (past recollection: 얼마나 춥던지).","Compare -는다든가 (11과): that lists examples. -든지 offers choices."],"ex":[["주말에는 공원을 **걷든지** 자전거를 **타든지** 돈 안 드는 활동을 해요.","On weekends, I do things that don't cost money, like walking in the park or riding a bike."],["장비는 대여소에서 **빌리든지** 친구한테 **빌리든지** 하면 돼요.","For equipment, you can borrow it from a rental shop or from a friend. Either works."],["**언제든지** 시간 있을 때 연락 주세요.","Contact me anytime you have time."]]}],"v":[["경제적","economical; economic","Two meanings: <b>cheap, cost-effective</b> (경제적인 방법) and <b>related to the economy</b> (경제적 문제).","대중교통을 이용하는 게 더 **경제적**이에요.","Taking public transportation is more economical."],["대여소","rental shop, rental station","대여 (5과) + -소 (place). 자전거 대여소.","한강공원 **대여소**에서 자전거를 빌렸어요.","I rented a bike at the Hangang Park rental station."],["안전모","safety helmet","For bikes, construction, etc. Also 헬멧.","자전거를 탈 때는 꼭 **안전모**를 쓰세요.","Always wear a helmet when you ride a bike."],["장비","equipment, gear","등산 장비, 캠핑 장비, <b>장비를 갖추다</b>.","캠핑 **장비**는 빌려서 쓰면 돈을 아낄 수 있어요.","You can save money by renting camping gear."],["가르다","to cut through, split","Common in leisure phrases: <b>바람을 가르다</b> (cut through the wind), 물살을 가르다. Also 편을 가르다 (split into teams). 르 irregular: 갈라요.","자전거를 타고 바람을 **가르며** 달리면 기분이 좋아요.","Riding a bike and cutting through the wind feels great."],["마음껏","to one's heart's content","As much as you want: <b>마음껏 즐기다 / 먹다 / 놀다</b>.","무료 공연이라서 **마음껏** 즐길 수 있었어요.","It was a free concert, so we could enjoy it as much as we wanted."]],"x":[["만족시키다","to satisfy (someone)","Causative of 만족하다 (11과): <b>손님/고객을 만족시키다</b>.","이 공원은 아이와 어른을 모두 **만족시켜요**.","This park keeps both kids and adults happy."],["안정시키다","to calm, stabilize","<b>마음을 안정시키다</b>, 물가를 안정시키다.","숲길을 걸으면 마음을 **안정시키는** 데 도움이 돼요.","Walking a forest path helps calm your mind."],["오염시키다","to pollute, contaminate","Causative of 오염되다: 환경/물을 오염시키다.","쓰레기를 함부로 버리면 공원을 **오염시켜요**.","Throwing trash carelessly pollutes the park."],["이해시키다","to make (someone) understand","<b>N에게 N을/를 이해시키다</b>.","부모님께 제 취미를 **이해시키기**가 어려웠어요.","It was hard to make my parents understand my hobby."],["향상시키다","to improve, raise","Causative of 향상되다 (2과): 실력/능력을 향상시키다.","꾸준한 운동은 체력을 **향상시켜요**.","Regular exercise improves your stamina."],["훈련시키다","to train (someone or an animal)","<b>개를 훈련시키다</b>, 선수를 훈련시키다.","주말마다 강아지를 공원에서 **훈련시켜요**.","Every weekend I train my puppy at the park."]]}]});
GUIDE.en.push({"n":16,"t":"생활 속의 환경 문제","en":"Environmental issues in daily life","units":[{"n":1,"t":"재활용과 재사용","g":[{"f":"-게요","en":"(because) I'm going to X; (it's) so I can X","core":"Added after a request or statement to explain why: \"Don't throw it away. I'm going to reuse it.\" It gives the purpose or reason behind what was just said. (Compare 5과 -게요?, which asks about the listener's intention.)","forms":[["Verb stem","쓰게요 · 재사용하게요 · 만들게요"],["Casual","-게: 버리지 마. 다시 쓰게."]],"rules":["Verb stem + 게요, regardless of 받침. Usually follows a request: <b>-아/어 주세요. -게요.</b>","The subject is usually the speaker: \"so I can…\"","Casual form <b>-게</b>.","Same family as 5과 -게요? (asking someone's purpose) and 20과 -게² (purpose \"so that\")."],"ex":[["그 상자 버리지 마세요. 이사할 때 다시 **쓰게요**.","Don't throw that box away. I'm going to use it again when I move."],["유리병 좀 모아 주세요. 화분으로 **재사용하게요**.","Please collect the glass bottles for me. I want to reuse them as flower pots."],["A: 왜 그 옷을 안 버려요? B: 가방으로 **만들게요**.","A: Why aren't you throwing out those clothes? B: I'm going to make them into a bag."]]},{"f":"-던가요?","en":"How was X? (asking about the listener's experience)","core":"Asks the listener about something they personally saw or experienced in the past. The question version of -더라고요 (6과): \"When you went, was it X?\"","forms":[["Verb / adjective","많던가요? · 비싸던가요? · 하던가요?"],["Past completed","끝났던가요? · 왔던가요?"],["Noun","N(이)던가요?"]],"rules":["Stem + 던가요? Past completed: -았/었던가요?","Only for things the listener directly experienced: 그 가게 어떻던가요? (How was that shop, when you went?)","Not for asking about the listener's own actions or feelings in general. It's asking for their observation.","Sounds polite and soft. Casual: -던가? / -더나?"],"ex":[["재활용 센터에 가 보셨다면서요. 사람이 **많던가요**?","I heard you went to the recycling center. Were there a lot of people?"],["중고 시장에서 산 가구, 상태는 **괜찮던가요**?","The furniture you bought at the secondhand market, was it in good shape?"],["그 가게에서 정말 병을 **받던가요**?","Did that shop really take bottles back?"]]}],"v":[["개성","individuality, personality","<b>개성이 있다 / 강하다</b>, 개성 있는 디자인.","재사용한 물건으로 꾸미니까 방에 **개성**이 생겼어요.","Decorating with reused items gave my room some personality."],["사회적","social","-적 noun: 사회적 문제, 사회적 책임, 사회적으로.","플라스틱 쓰레기는 큰 **사회적** 문제가 되었어요.","Plastic waste has become a big social problem."],["심각하다","serious, grave","<b>문제/상황이 심각하다</b>, 심각하게 생각하다.","환경 오염이 생각보다 훨씬 **심각해요**.","Environmental pollution is much more serious than I thought."],["완성하다","to complete, finish","For making something: <b>작품을 완성하다</b>. Passive: 완성되다.","헌 청바지로 가방을 **완성했어요**.","I finished making a bag out of old jeans."],["증가하다","to increase","Formal for 늘다: <b>N이/가 증가하다</b>. Opposite: 감소하다.","배달 음식 때문에 일회용품 사용이 **증가했어요**.","The use of disposable items increased because of food delivery."],["갈수록","increasingly, as time goes on","<b>갈수록 -아/어지다</b>: 갈수록 심해지다.","쓰레기 문제가 **갈수록** 심각해지고 있어요.","The trash problem is getting more and more serious."],["환경 오염","environmental pollution","<b>환경 오염이 심하다</b>, 환경 오염을 줄이다.","**환경 오염**을 줄이기 위해 재활용을 열심히 해요.","I recycle diligently to reduce environmental pollution."]],"x":[["이익","profit, benefit","Opposite: 손해 (8과). <b>이익을 얻다 / 보다</b>.","재사용은 환경에도 좋고 경제적인 **이익**도 있어요.","Reusing things is good for the environment and has economic benefits too."],["묻다","to be stained (with); to get on","Different from 묻다 (ask) and 묻다 (bury). <b>N이/가 N에 묻다</b>: 옷에 기름이 묻다.","음식물이 **묻은** 용기는 씻어서 버려야 해요.","Containers with food stuck on them have to be washed before throwing them out."],["재사용하다","to reuse","Using something again as is.","택배 상자를 **재사용해서** 물건을 정리했어요.","I reused delivery boxes to organize my stuff."],["재활용하다","to recycle","Processing material to make something new. 분리수거 = sorting recycling.","페트병은 라벨을 떼고 **재활용해야** 해요.","You have to remove the label from PET bottles before recycling them."],["처리하다","to handle, dispose of, process","<b>쓰레기를 처리하다</b>, 일을 처리하다.","플라스틱을 **처리하는** 데 많은 비용이 들어요.","Disposing of plastic costs a lot."]]},{"n":2,"t":"환경과 생활 습관","g":[{"f":"-더니³ (-었더니)","en":"I did X, and (then I found / as a result) Y","core":"The speaker's own past action, followed by what they discovered or what resulted. Unlike -더니¹ and -더니², this one is about the speaker's own action and always uses the past form <b>-았/었더니</b>.","forms":[["Verb, ㅏ/ㅗ","갔더니 · 봤더니 · 줄였더니"],["Verb, other","먹었더니 · 썼더니"],["하다","했더니 · 사용했더니"]],"rules":["Always -았/었더니. The subject of the first clause is usually 저/나.","Second clause: a discovery (가 봤더니 문이 닫혀 있었어요) or a result (운동했더니 살이 빠졌어요).","The second clause is in the past, or a present state that resulted.","Compare: <b>-더니¹/²</b> = observing someone else (친구가 운동하더니 살이 빠졌어요). <b>-었더니</b> = my own action (내가 운동했더니…)."],"ex":[["텀블러를 가지고 **다녔더니** 일회용 컵 쓰레기가 확 줄었어요.","I started carrying a tumbler, and my disposable cup trash dropped sharply."],["장바구니를 **썼더니** 비닐봉지를 거의 안 받게 됐어요.","Once I used a shopping bag, I barely ended up getting plastic bags anymore."],["일주일 동안 쓰레기를 **모아 봤더니** 대부분이 포장재였어요.","When I collected my trash for a week, most of it was packaging."]]},{"f":"-도록 하다","en":"(1) make sure to X; (2) I'll make sure to X; (3) make someone X","core":"Three uses. (1) <b>Instruction</b> (polite, formal command): 일회용품 사용을 줄이<b>도록 하세요</b>. (2) <b>Speaker's resolve</b>: 앞으로 조심하<b>도록 하겠습니다</b>. (3) <b>Causative</b>: making someone do something: 아이가 직접 분리수거를 하<b>도록 했어요</b>.","forms":[["Instruction","-도록 하세요 / -도록 하십시오"],["Resolve","-도록 하겠습니다 / -도록 할게요"],["Causative","N이/가 -도록 하다"]],"rules":["Stem + 도록 하다. Related to -도록¹ (2과, \"so that\").","Instruction use sounds formal and official: notices, teachers, doctors.","Resolve use is common in apologies and promises: 다시는 늦지 않<b>도록 하겠습니다</b>.","Negative: <b>-지 않도록 하다</b> / <b>-지 말도록 하다</b>.","Causative use is softer than -게 하다 and implies arranging the situation."],"ex":[["되도록 일회용품을 쓰지 **않도록 하세요**.","Try not to use disposable items as much as possible."],["앞으로는 장바구니를 꼭 챙기**도록 하겠습니다**.","From now on, I'll make sure to bring a shopping bag."],["선생님께서 학생들이 직접 텀블러를 가져오**도록 하셨어요**.","The teacher had the students bring their own tumblers."]]}],"v":[["면","aspect, side; surface","<b>N 면에서</b> (in terms of N), 좋은 면, 여러 면. Also: 면 = cotton (면 소재).","환경**면**에서 보면 중고 물건을 사는 게 좋아요.","From an environmental standpoint, buying secondhand is good."],["일회용품","disposable items","일회용 = single-use: 일회용 컵, 일회용 젓가락.","카페에서 **일회용품** 사용이 많이 줄었어요.","Cafés use far fewer disposable items now."],["불필요하다","unnecessary","불- + 필요하다. <b>불필요한 포장 / 소비</b>.","**불필요한** 물건은 처음부터 안 사는 게 좋아요.","It's better not to buy unnecessary things in the first place."],["다소","somewhat, to some extent","Formal, softer than 좀/조금. Good for essays.","처음에는 **다소** 불편하지만 금방 익숙해져요.","It's somewhat inconvenient at first, but you get used to it quickly."],["되도록","as much as possible","Same as 가능한 한. <b>되도록 -(으)세요</b>.","**되도록** 대중교통을 이용하려고 해요.","I try to use public transportation as much as possible."]],"x":[["과대","excessive, oversized","Mostly in <b>과대 포장</b> (excessive packaging), 과대광고.","**과대** 포장 때문에 쓰레기가 많이 나와요.","Excessive packaging creates a lot of trash."],["구입","purchase","Formal for 사기: <b>구입하다</b>, 구입처.","물건 **구입** 전에 꼭 필요한지 생각해 봐요.","Before buying something, I think about whether I really need it."],["무절제하다","unrestrained, excessive","무- + 절제 (self-control). <b>무절제한 소비</b>.","**무절제한** 소비가 환경을 해칠 수 있어요.","Unrestrained consumption can harm the environment."],["자제하다","to refrain from, hold back","<b>N을/를 자제하다</b>: 사용/외출을 자제하다. Common in notices.","플라스틱 사용을 **자제해** 주시기 바랍니다.","Please refrain from using plastic."],["최소화하다","to minimize","Opposite: 최대화하다. <b>쓰레기/피해를 최소화하다</b>.","포장을 **최소화한** 제품을 고르려고 해요.","I try to choose products with minimal packaging."]]}]});
GUIDE.en.push({"n":17,"t":"개인과 공동체","en":"The individual and the community","units":[{"n":1,"t":"개인주의","g":[{"f":"-었을 텐데","en":"(1) would have X (counterfactual); (2) must have X (sympathetic guess)","core":"The past version of -을 텐데 (4과). (1) <b>Counterfactual</b>: what would have happened under different circumstances, often after -었으면 / -었더라면. (2) <b>Past assumption</b>: \"you must have been X\" as background for sympathy or thanks.","forms":[["Verb / adj, ㅏ/ㅗ","갔을 텐데 · 좋았을 텐데"],["Verb / adj, other","힘들었을 텐데 · 먹었을 텐데"],["Noun","N이었을 텐데 / 였을 텐데"]],"rules":["Counterfactual: <b>-었으면/-었더라면 … -었을 텐데</b>: 미리 말했으면 도와줬을 텐데.","Sympathy: <b>-었을 텐데 + thanks or concern</b>: 많이 바빴을 텐데 와 줘서 고마워요.","Ending a sentence with <b>-었을 텐데요</b> expresses regret: 같이 갔으면 좋았을 텐데요.","Compare -을 텐데 (4과) for present or future assumptions."],"ex":[["회의 때 다른 사람 눈치만 보지 말고 의견을 **말했으면** 좋**았을 텐데**.","It would have been better if you'd said your opinion at the meeting instead of just reading the room."],["혼자 이사하느라 많이 **힘들었을 텐데** 왜 도와 달라고 안 했어요?","You must have had a hard time moving by yourself. Why didn't you ask for help?"],["그 사람이 주위 사람들에게 조금만 귀를 기울였더라면 오해가 **없었을 텐데요**.","If he'd listened to the people around him just a little, there wouldn't have been a misunderstanding."]]},{"f":"-는 둥 마는 둥 하다","en":"to do X half-heartedly, barely X","core":"Something was done so carelessly or briefly that it hardly counts: \"to sort of do it, sort of not.\" Often used for eating, sleeping, listening, greeting, cleaning.","forms":[["Verb","먹는 둥 마는 둥 · 듣는 둥 마는 둥 · 자는 둥 마는 둥"],["Past (modifier)","인사를 하는 둥 마는 둥 하고 갔다"]],"rules":["Verbs only: <b>-는 둥 마는 둥 하다</b>. The verb appears once, then 마는.","Past: <b>-는 둥 마는 둥 했다</b> (keep -는 even for past events).","Often criticizes an attitude: 남의 말을 듣는 둥 마는 둥 해요.","Also with 하는 둥 마는 둥: 청소를 하는 둥 마는 둥 했어요."],"ex":[["회의 시간에 그 사람은 다른 사람 말을 **듣는 둥 마는 둥 했어요**.","During the meeting, he only half-listened to what others said."],["늦잠을 자서 아침을 **먹는 둥 마는 둥 하고** 나왔어요.","I overslept, so I barely ate breakfast before heading out."],["이웃이 인사를 **하는 둥 마는 둥 하고** 지나갔어요.","My neighbor barely said hello as he walked past."]]}],"v":[["사다","to invite, provoke (a reaction)","Besides \"buy\": <b>미움/오해/반감을 사다</b> = earn dislike, cause a misunderstanding.","너무 자기 생각만 하면 다른 사람들의 미움을 **살** 수 있어요.","If you only think about yourself, you can earn other people's dislike."],["참석하다","to attend","<b>N에 참석하다</b>: 회의/모임/결혼식에 참석하다. 참석자 = attendee.","요즘은 회식에 **참석하지** 않는 사람도 많아요.","Lots of people don't attend company dinners these days."],["귀를 기울이다","to listen carefully, lend an ear","Literally \"tilt the ear.\" <b>N에 귀를 기울이다</b>.","리더는 팀원들의 의견에 **귀를 기울여야** 해요.","A leader should listen carefully to team members' opinions."],["눈치를 보다","to read the room, be conscious of others' reactions","Watching others' moods so as not to stand out. Very Korean concept. 눈치가 빠르다 = quick to read situations.","상사 **눈치를 보느라고** 퇴근을 못 했어요.","I couldn't leave work because I was worried about what my boss would think."],["뭐라고 하다","to criticize, say something (negative) to","Literally \"say what\": usually scolding: <b>N에게 뭐라고 하다</b>.","혼자 밥을 먹어도 아무도 **뭐라고 하지** 않아요.","Even if you eat alone, nobody says anything about it."],["손발을 맞추다","to work in sync, coordinate","Literally \"match hands and feet\": teamwork.","팀원들과 **손발을 맞추는** 데 시간이 좀 걸렸어요.","It took some time to get in sync with my teammates."]],"x":[["시선","gaze; eyes (of others)","<b>남의 시선을 의식하다</b> = worry about how others see you. 시선을 끌다 = attract attention.","저는 다른 사람의 **시선**을 별로 신경 쓰지 않아요.","I don't really care how other people look at me."],["타인","others, other people","Formal for 남, 다른 사람. Common in essays.","**타인**의 생각을 존중하는 게 중요해요.","It's important to respect other people's thoughts."],["당당하다","confident, dignified","Standing tall, not ashamed: <b>당당하게 말하다</b>.","혼자 영화를 보는 것도 **당당하게** 즐겨요.","I confidently enjoy going to movies alone too."],["두렵다","afraid, fearful","Deeper or more abstract fear than 무섭다. ㅂ irregular: 두려워요.","처음에는 혼자 사는 게 **두려웠어요**.","At first I was afraid of living alone."],["외면하다","to turn away from, ignore","Deliberately not facing something: <b>현실/도움 요청을 외면하다</b>.","어려운 이웃을 **외면하면** 안 돼요.","We shouldn't turn away from neighbors in need."],["의식하다","to be conscious of","<b>N을/를 의식하다</b>: 남의 눈/시선을 의식하다.","너무 남을 **의식하면** 하고 싶은 걸 못 해요.","If you're too conscious of others, you can't do what you want."],["개의치 않다","to not mind, not care","Always negative or in questions. Formal: 남의 말에 개의치 않다.","그는 다른 사람들의 평가에 **개의치 않아요**.","He doesn't care about other people's judgments."]]},{"n":2,"t":"함께 사는 집","g":[{"f":"-는 만큼","en":"(1) as much as X; (2) since X (so naturally Y)","core":"Two uses. (1) <b>Proportion</b>: Y matches the degree of X: 노력한 만큼 결과가 나와요. (2) <b>Reason</b>: because X is the case, Y naturally follows, often formal: 함께 사는 만큼 서로 배려해야 해요.","forms":[["Verb (present)","사는 만큼 · 쓰는 만큼"],["Verb (past)","노력한 만큼 · 준비한 만큼"],["Adjective","중요한 만큼 · 비싼 만큼"],["Noun","N인 만큼 / N만큼 (proportion)"]],"rules":["Verb present -는, past -(으)ㄴ, future -(으)ㄹ, adjective -(으)ㄴ + 만큼.","Reason use sounds formal and logical: 공동생활<b>인 만큼</b> 규칙을 지켜야 합니다.","Proportion use: <b>-는 만큼 -다</b> (you get as much as you put in).","Don't confuse with N만큼 as a particle (as … as N): 형만큼 키가 커요."],"ex":[["여럿이 함께 **사는 만큼** 서로의 사생활을 존중해야 해요.","Since many people live together, we have to respect each other's privacy."],["공용 공간을 깨끗하게 **쓰는 만큼** 모두가 편해져요.","The cleaner the shared space is kept, the more comfortable everyone becomes."],["월세가 **싼 만큼** 불편한 점도 있어요.","Since the rent is cheap, there are some inconveniences too."]]},{"f":"-는다고¹","en":"(busy / tired) because of X (doing X)","core":"Gives a reason, usually an activity the subject was busy with or a stated intention. It often explains why the subject couldn't do something else or is tired: \"busy moving,\" \"saying they're on a diet.\" Short for -는다고 해서/하느라고.","forms":[["Verb","이사한다고 · 준비한다고 · 공부한다고"],["Adjective","바쁘다고 · 피곤하다고"],["Noun","시험이라고"]],"rules":["Quoted forms: verb -ㄴ/는다고, adjective -다고, noun -(이)라고.","Very common with: <b>바쁘다, 정신이 없다, 고생하다, 힘들다, 못 하다</b>.","Can carry the nuance that it's the subject's own stated reason: 다이어트한다고 밥을 안 먹어요 (says they're dieting).","Close in meaning to -느라고. Both explain busy-ness, but -는다고 can also report someone's intention."],"ex":[["새 집에 **입주한다고** 지난주 내내 정신이 없었어요.","I was frazzled all last week because I was moving into the new place."],["룸메이트가 시험 **준비한다고** 요즘 공용 거실을 거의 안 써요.","My roommate barely uses the shared living room these days because she's preparing for exams."],["동생이 **다이어트한다고** 저녁을 안 먹어요.","My younger sibling isn't eating dinner, saying they're on a diet."]]}],"v":[["공동생활","communal living","Living together in a group: 셰어하우스, 기숙사.","**공동생활**에서는 규칙을 지키는 게 제일 중요해요.","In communal living, following the rules is the most important thing."],["비교적","relatively, comparatively","Adverb or modifier: <b>비교적 싸다</b>, 비교적 조용한 동네.","셰어하우스는 원룸보다 월세가 **비교적** 저렴해요.","Share houses are relatively cheaper than studio apartments."],["여럿","many people, several","<b>여럿이(서)</b> = in a group: 여럿이 함께 살다.","**여럿**이 같이 살면 외롭지 않아서 좋아요.","Living with several people is nice because you don't get lonely."],["정기적","regular, periodic","정기적으로 (regularly), 정기 모임, 정기 점검.","하우스 메이트들과 **정기적**으로 회의를 해요.","I have regular meetings with my housemates."],["둘러보다","to look around","<b>집/가게를 둘러보다</b>. Taking a look at a place before deciding.","입주하기 전에 집을 꼼꼼히 **둘러봤어요**.","I looked around the house carefully before moving in."],["입주하다","to move in","Formal for 이사 오다: 아파트에 입주하다, 입주자.","다음 달 1일에 셰어하우스에 **입주할** 예정이에요.","I'm scheduled to move into the share house on the 1st of next month."],["쇠뿔도 단김에 빼랬다","pull the ox horn while it's hot (strike while the iron is hot)","Proverb: do it right away while you're motivated. 빼랬다 = 빼라고 했다.","**쇠뿔도 단김에 빼랬다**고, 마음에 들면 오늘 바로 계약해요.","Strike while the iron is hot. If you like it, let's sign the contract today."]],"x":[["공용","shared, common use","<b>공용 공간 / 주방 / 화장실</b>. Opposite: 전용 (private).","**공용** 주방은 쓴 다음에 바로 치워야 해요.","You have to clean up the shared kitchen right after using it."],["동거인","housemate, cohabitant","Legal or formal word for someone living in the same home. Neutral; doesn't imply romance.","**동거인**과 생활비를 반씩 나눠서 내요.","My housemate and I split living expenses in half."],["사생활","privacy, private life","<b>사생활을 존중하다 / 침해하다</b>.","같이 살아도 서로의 **사생활**은 지켜 줘야 해요.","Even living together, you have to respect each other's privacy."],["사적","private, personal","Opposite: 공적 (public, official). <b>사적인 질문 / 공간</b>.","**사적**인 공간에는 허락 없이 들어가면 안 돼요.","You can't enter someone's private space without permission."],["제약","restriction, constraint","<b>제약이 있다 / 많다</b>, 제약을 받다.","공동생활은 편하지만 생활에 **제약**도 있어요.","Communal living is convenient, but it also has restrictions."]]}]});
GUIDE.en.push({"n":18,"t":"변화하는 사회","en":"A changing society","units":[{"n":1,"t":"사고방식의 변화","g":[{"f":"꼴로","en":"at a rate of (once every…)","core":"Attaches to a quantity to express a rate or ratio: <b>N에 한 번꼴로</b> = about once every N. Also 다섯 명 중 한 명꼴로 = about one in five people.","forms":[["Frequency","일주일에 한 번꼴로 · 한 달에 두 번꼴로"],["Ratio","세 명 중 한 명꼴로 · 열 명에 한 명꼴로"]],"rules":["Attaches to a number + counter: <b>한 번꼴로, 한 명꼴로</b>. Written without a space.","Typical frame: <b>[period/group]에 [number]꼴로</b> or <b>[group] 중 [number]꼴로</b>.","Common in statistics and news: 직장인 세 명 중 한 명꼴로…","Similar to 정도 / 씩 but focused on rate."],"ex":[["요즘 젊은 사람들 세 명 중 한 명**꼴로** 결혼을 꼭 해야 한다고 생각하지 않는대요.","They say about one in three young people today don't think they necessarily have to get married."],["저는 한 달에 한 번**꼴로** 부모님께 연락해요.","I contact my parents about once a month."],["직장인 다섯 명 중 한 명**꼴로** 부업을 하고 있다고 해요.","They say about one in five office workers has a side job."]]},{"f":"-는 수가 있다","en":"(something bad) could happen; there's a chance that X","core":"Warns that an undesirable result might happen: \"you might end up X.\" Different from -는 수밖에 없다 (8과), which means \"no choice but to.\" 수 here = possibility.","forms":[["Verb","실패하는 수가 있다 · 후회하는 수가 있다 · 잃는 수가 있다"]],"rules":["Verbs only: <b>-는 수가 있다</b>. (Also -(으)ㄹ 수가 있다 with a similar warning tone.)","Usually a negative or unwanted result: 손해를 보는 수가 있어요.","Often after a condition: -(으)면 / -다가는 … -는 수가 있어요.","Sounds like friendly advice or a gentle warning."],"ex":[["너무 무리하게 투자하면 큰 손해를 **보는 수가 있어요**.","If you invest too aggressively, you could take a big loss."],["기성세대의 생각만 고집하다가는 변화에 뒤처지**는 수가 있어요**.","If you only cling to the older generation's way of thinking, you might fall behind the changes."],["미리 대비하지 않으면 나중에 후회하**는 수가 있어요**.","If you don't prepare in advance, you might regret it later."]]}],"v":[["개념","concept, idea","<b>N에 대한 개념</b>, 개념이 바뀌다. Slang: 개념이 없다 = has no common sense.","요즘은 '가족'에 대한 **개념**이 많이 바뀌었어요.","The concept of 'family' has changed a lot these days."],["경향","tendency, trend","<b>-는 경향이 있다</b> = tend to.","젊은 세대는 자신의 행복을 중시하는 **경향**이 있어요.","The younger generation tends to prioritize its own happiness."],["기성세대","the older (established) generation","기성 = already established. Contrast: 젊은 세대, MZ세대.","**기성세대**와 젊은 세대의 가치관 차이가 커요.","There's a big gap in values between the older and younger generations."],["투자","investment","<b>투자하다</b>, 주식 투자, 시간 투자. Also figurative: 자기 계발에 투자하다.","요즘은 자기 계발에 **투자**하는 사람이 많아요.","Lots of people invest in self-development these days."],["현실적","realistic","-적 noun: 현실적인 목표, 현실적으로 생각하다. Opposite: 이상적.","젊은 사람들은 결혼보다 **현실적**인 문제를 먼저 생각해요.","Young people think about practical issues before marriage."],["대비하다","to prepare for (future events)","<b>N에 대비하다</b>: 노후/미래/위기에 대비하다. Planning ahead for risk.","노후에 **대비해서** 지금부터 저축하고 있어요.","I'm saving now to prepare for retirement."]],"x":[["개방적","open-minded","-적 noun. Opposite: 보수적.","젊은 세대는 다른 문화에 **개방적**인 편이에요.","The younger generation tends to be open to other cultures."],["보수적","conservative, traditional","Not only political: 보수적인 부모님 = traditional parents.","우리 부모님은 결혼에 대해서 좀 **보수적**이세요.","My parents are a bit conservative about marriage."],["비합리적","irrational, unreasonable","비- + 합리적.","나이만으로 사람을 판단하는 건 **비합리적**이에요.","Judging people only by their age is unreasonable."],["이상적","ideal","Opposite: 현실적. 이상 = ideal.","**이상적**인 직장은 월급보다 분위기가 좋은 곳이에요.","My ideal workplace is somewhere with a good atmosphere rather than high pay."],["진보적","progressive","Opposite: 보수적. Politics and ideas.","그 교수님은 생각이 아주 **진보적**이세요.","That professor's thinking is very progressive."],["집단","group, collective","집단주의 (collectivism) vs 개인주의 (individualism, 17과).","한국 사회는 예전에 비해 **집단**보다 개인을 중시하게 됐어요.","Compared to before, Korean society has come to value the individual over the group."],["합리적","rational, reasonable","<b>합리적인 가격 / 선택</b>. Very common in ads: 합리적인 소비.","가격을 비교해 보고 **합리적**으로 결정했어요.","I compared prices and made a reasonable decision."]]},{"n":2,"t":"도시의 변화","g":[{"f":"-으려나 보다","en":"it looks like (someone/something) is going to X","core":"A guess about what is about to happen or what someone intends, based on what the speaker sees: \"Looks like they're going to tear it down.\" Combines intention -(으)려 with guessing -나 보다.","forms":[["Verb, no 받침","하려나 보다 · 오려나 보다 · 부수려나 보다"],["Verb, 받침","닫으려나 보다 · 지으려나 보다 (짓다, ㅅ irregular)"]],"rules":["Verb + -(으)려나 보다. Present tense ending: <b>-(으)려나 봐요</b>.","Based on evidence: 공사 차량이 많은 걸 보니 건물을 새로 <b>지으려나 봐요</b>.","Often with -는 걸 보니(까) for the evidence.","Also used for weather: 비가 <b>오려나 봐요</b> (looks like it's going to rain).","Compare -나 보다 (it seems X is the case) and -(으)ㄹ 것 같다 (more general guess)."],"ex":[["오래된 시장 앞에 공사 차량이 많은 걸 보니 건물을 **부수려나 봐요**.","Seeing all the construction vehicles in front of the old market, it looks like they're going to tear down the building."],["하늘이 어두워지는 걸 보니 비가 **오려나 봐요**.","The sky's getting dark, so it looks like it's going to rain."],["저 가게가 짐을 다 빼는 걸 보니 문을 **닫으려나 봐요**.","That shop is moving everything out, so it looks like it's going to close."]]},{"f":"하면","en":"when it comes to N; speaking of N (what comes to mind)","core":"<b>N 하면</b> introduces a topic and says what it's known for or what you associate with it: \"When you think of Seoul, you think of…\" Spaced from the noun. Same as N(이)라고 하면.","forms":[["Noun","서울 하면 · 한국 음식 하면 · 이 동네 하면"]],"rules":["<b>N 하면 (떠오르는 것은) N이다</b>: 부산 하면 바다지요.","Often followed by 떠오르다, 생각나다, 유명하다, 대표적이다.","Spoken and casual-neutral. In writing: N(이)라고 하면.","Spacing: <b>서울 하면</b> (space), unlike 하면 as a conditional ending."],"ex":[["예전에 이 동네 **하면** 오래된 시장이 먼저 떠올랐어요.","In the past, when you thought of this neighborhood, the old market came to mind first."],["서울 **하면** 고층 건물이 생각나지만 사실 산과 공원도 많아요.","Seoul makes people think of skyscrapers, but there are actually lots of mountains and parks too."],["요즘 성수동 **하면** 카페 거리가 유명하지요.","These days, when it comes to Seongsu-dong, the café streets are famous."]]}],"v":[["원래","originally, by nature","<b>원래 -었다</b> (it used to be), 원래 그래요 (that's how it always is).","이 카페는 **원래** 오래된 공장이었어요.","This café was originally an old factory."],["꾸미다","to decorate; to make up (a story)","<b>집/방/거리를 꾸미다</b>. Also 이야기를 꾸미다 (make something up).","오래된 골목을 예쁘게 **꾸며서** 관광지가 됐어요.","They decorated the old alley nicely and it became a tourist spot."],["둘러싸이다","to be surrounded","Passive of 둘러싸다: <b>N(으)로 둘러싸이다</b>.","우리 동네는 산으로 **둘러싸여** 있어서 공기가 좋아요.","My neighborhood is surrounded by mountains, so the air is good."],["떠올리다","to recall, bring to mind","Transitive: <b>추억을 떠올리다</b>. Intransitive: 떠오르다 (come to mind).","옛날 사진을 보면 어릴 때 살던 동네를 **떠올리게** 돼요.","Looking at old photos makes me recall the neighborhood I lived in as a kid."],["부수다","to break, tear down, demolish","<b>건물을 부수다</b>. Passive: 부서지다.","오래된 아파트를 **부수고** 새 아파트를 짓고 있어요.","They're tearing down old apartments and building new ones."],["꼼짝없이","helplessly, with no way out","Stuck with no option: <b>꼼짝없이 갇히다 / 기다리다</b>.","공사 때문에 길이 막혀서 **꼼짝없이** 한 시간을 기다렸어요.","The road was blocked by construction, so I was stuck waiting an hour."]],"x":[["개선","improvement","<b>개선하다 / 개선되다</b>, 환경 개선. For fixing problems.","주민들의 의견으로 공원 시설이 **개선**됐어요.","The park facilities were improved based on residents' feedback."],["발달","development, advancement","<b>발달하다</b>: 교통/기술이 발달하다. Natural growth over time.","교통이 **발달**해서 서울 어디든 쉽게 갈 수 있어요.","Transportation has developed, so you can easily go anywhere in Seoul."],["확장","expansion","<b>확장하다 / 확장되다</b>: 도로 확장, 사업 확장.","도로 **확장** 공사 때문에 길이 자주 막혀요.","The roads are often jammed because of road widening construction."],["변화하다","to change, transform","Formal for 바뀌다 / 변하다. 변화 = change.","10년 동안 이 도시는 크게 **변화했어요**.","This city has changed greatly over ten years."],["쾌적하다","pleasant, comfortable (environment)","For spaces and air: <b>쾌적한 환경 / 공간</b>.","새로 생긴 도서관은 넓고 **쾌적해요**.","The new library is spacious and pleasant."],["활기차다","lively, vibrant","<b>활기찬 거리 / 분위기</b>. 활기 = vitality.","시장이 새로 단장한 뒤로 거리가 더 **활기차졌어요**.","Since the market was renovated, the streets have become livelier."]]}]});
GUIDE.en.push({"n":19,"t":"나의 삶","en":"My life","units":[{"n":1,"t":"선택","g":[{"f":"-는다며","en":"saying that X, (someone) did Y; (casual) I heard X, right?","core":"Reports what someone said, usually as their reason, together with what they then did or said they'd do: 존 씨는 집에 초대할 수 있다며 자기 집에서 파티를 하겠다고 했어요. It's short for -는다면서. The X part is the person's own words or reason, and the second clause is their action or what they said they'd do. A second, casual use turns it into a question about hearsay: 독립한다며? (I heard you're moving out?)","forms":[["Verb","독립한다며 · 이사했다며 · 간다며"],["Adjective","힘들다며 · 비싸다며"],["Noun","N(이)라며 (학생이라며)"],["Polite question","-는다면서요?"]],"rules":["Quoted forms: verb -ㄴ/는다며, adjective -다며, noun -(이)라며.","Main pattern: <b>[person]은/는 X-는다며 Y-겠다고 했어요 / Y-았/었어요</b>.","X is what the subject said (often their reason). The subject of both clauses is usually the same person.","For offers and intentions: -겠다며, -(으)ㄹ 수 있다며. For commands and suggestions: -(으)라며, -자며.","Side use (casual question): <b>-는다며?</b> = I heard X, right? Polite: -는다면서요? Compare -는다지요? (15과)."],"ex":[["에릭 씨는 집 앞에 맛있는 빵집이 **있다며** 케이크를 사 오겠다고 했어요.","Eric said there's a great bakery in front of his place, so he'd pick up the cake."],["친구가 집세가 너무 **비싸다며** 결국 부모님 집으로 돌아갔어요.","My friend said the rent was too expensive and ended up moving back to her parents' place."],["동생이 혼자 살아 보고 **싶다며** 독립하겠다고 했어요.","My younger sibling said they wanted to try living alone and announced they'd move out."]]},{"f":"-을 따름이다","en":"(I) just / only X (humble, nothing more)","core":"Emphasizes that this is the only thing, nothing more. Very common in formal or humble expressions of feeling: 감사할 따름입니다 (I'm simply grateful), 최선을 다했을 따름입니다 (I just did my best).","forms":[["Verb / adj, no 받침","감사할 따름이다 · 기쁠 따름이다"],["Verb / adj, 받침","놀라울 따름이다 · 했을 따름이다"],["Past","-었을 따름이다 (했을 따름이에요)"]],"rules":["-(으)ㄹ 따름이다. Formal and a bit literary; common in speeches, interviews, and written Korean.","Feelings: <b>감사할 / 죄송할 / 기쁠 / 놀라울 따름입니다</b>.","Modesty: <b>제 할 일을 했을 따름이에요</b> (I just did my job).","Similar: -(으)ㄹ 뿐이다. -을 따름이다 is more formal."],"ex":[["제 선택을 믿고 응원해 주신 부모님께 **감사할 따름이에요**.","I'm simply grateful to my parents for trusting and supporting my choice."],["저는 제 형편에 맞는 선택을 **했을 따름이에요**.","I just made the choice that fit my circumstances."],["이렇게 큰 상을 받게 되어 그저 **놀라울 따름입니다**.","I'm simply amazed to receive such a big award."]]}],"v":[["독립","independence; moving out on one's own","<b>독립하다</b> = to become independent, move out of your parents' home. 경제적 독립.","대학을 졸업하고 바로 부모님한테서 **독립했어요**.","I moved out of my parents' place right after graduating."],["집세","rent","Everyday word for 월세 / 임대료. <b>집세를 내다</b>, 집세가 오르다.","서울은 **집세**가 너무 비싸서 혼자 살기 힘들어요.","Rent in Seoul is so expensive that living alone is hard."],["고려하다","to consider, take into account","<b>N을/를 고려하다</b>: 형편/조건을 고려하다. More formal than 생각하다.","이사할 때는 집세뿐만 아니라 교통도 **고려해야** 해요.","When moving, you have to consider not just rent but transportation too."],["신중하다","careful, prudent","For decisions: <b>신중하게 결정하다</b>. Opposite: 경솔하다 (rash).","인생에서 중요한 선택일수록 **신중하게** 해야 해요.","The more important the life decision, the more carefully you should make it."],["철없다","immature, childish","철 = good sense that comes with age. <b>철이 없다 / 철들다</b> (grow up).","어렸을 때는 **철없이** 부모님께 고집만 부렸어요.","When I was young, I immaturely just argued with my parents."]],"x":[["권유","recommendation, suggestion","<b>권유하다</b>, N의 권유로 (at N's suggestion). Softer than 강요 (forcing).","선배의 **권유**로 이 학교에 지원하게 됐어요.","I ended up applying to this school at an upperclassman's suggestion."],["사항","matters, items, particulars","Formal: <b>주의 사항</b> (precautions), 고려 사항, 참고 사항.","집을 계약하기 전에 확인해야 할 **사항**이 많아요.","There are lots of things to check before signing a lease."],["여건","conditions, circumstances","Practical conditions that allow or limit something: <b>여건이 되다 / 허락하다</b>.","**여건**이 되면 해외에서 공부하고 싶어요.","If circumstances allow, I'd like to study abroad."],["주위","surroundings; people around (you)","<b>주위 사람들</b> = the people around you. Also 주변.","**주위** 사람들의 말보다 제 생각을 따르기로 했어요.","I decided to follow my own thinking rather than what the people around me said."],["형편","circumstances (often financial)","<b>형편이 어렵다 / 좋다</b>, 형편에 맞다 (within one's means).","제 **형편**에 맞는 집을 찾느라 고생했어요.","I had a hard time finding a place within my means."]]},{"n":2,"t":"현재의 나, 미래의 나","g":[{"f":"과연 -을까요?","en":"I wonder if X will really… (doubt)","core":"Expresses doubt or wondering about whether something will really happen or is really true. 과연 = really, indeed. Often rhetorical, implying \"probably not\" or genuine uncertainty.","forms":[["Verb / adj","과연 이루어질까요? · 과연 행복할까요?"],["Past","과연 잘했을까요?"],["Self-talk","과연 -을까? (casual)"]],"rules":["<b>과연 + -(으)ㄹ까요?</b> Rising or wondering intonation.","Can be a real question or rhetorical doubt, so context decides.","Also used positively as \"as expected\": <b>과연</b> 소문대로 맛있네요 (just as rumored). That's a different use.","Good for presentations and essays to raise a question: 과연 돈이 행복의 전부일까요?"],"ex":[["10년 후의 나는 **과연** 지금 꿈꾸는 일을 하고 **있을까요**?","Will I really be doing the work I dream of now, ten years from now?"],["돈을 많이 벌면 **과연** 행복**할까요**?","Would you really be happy if you made a lot of money?"],["이 계획이 **과연** 이루어질 수 **있을까** 걱정돼요.","I'm worried whether this plan can really come true."]]},{"f":"-어 가면서","en":"while gradually (continuing to) X","core":"-아/어 가다 (an ongoing process moving forward) + -면서 (while). Something is done while another process gradually continues or develops: \"while slowly building up experience.\"","forms":[["Verb, ㅏ/ㅗ","알아 가면서 · 쌓아 가면서"],["Verb, other","배워 가면서 · 만들어 가면서"],["하다","해 가면서 · 준비해 가면서"]],"rules":["Verb + -아/어 가면서. The first action is a gradual, ongoing process.","Common verbs: 배우다, 알다, 쌓다, 이루다, 만들다, 준비하다, 고치다.","Also with adjectives using -아/어지다: 익숙해져 가면서.","Compare -아/어 오다 (from past up to now) vs -아/어 가다 (from now going forward)."],"ex":[["저는 경험을 하나씩 **쌓아 가면서** 꿈을 이루고 싶어요.","I want to achieve my dream while building up experience one step at a time."],["실수를 **고쳐 가면서** 조금씩 성장하는 거지요.","You grow little by little while fixing your mistakes."],["한국 생활에 **익숙해져 가면서** 앞날이 더 기대돼요.","As I'm getting used to life in Korea, I'm looking forward to the future more."]]}],"v":[["앞날","the future, days ahead","More personal and warm than 미래: <b>앞날이 밝다</b>, 앞날을 걱정하다.","젊은 사람들의 **앞날**이 밝았으면 좋겠어요.","I hope young people have a bright future."],["내세우다","to put forward, insist on, promote","<b>의견/조건/장점을 내세우다</b>. Can mean promoting something as a strength.","면접에서 제 장점을 자신 있게 **내세웠어요**.","I confidently put forward my strengths in the interview."],["이루어지다","to come true, be achieved","Passive of 이루다: <b>꿈/소원이 이루어지다</b>.","언젠가 제 꿈이 **이루어지면** 좋겠어요.","I hope my dream comes true someday."],["펼쳐지다","to unfold, spread out","Scenery (바다가 눈앞에 펼쳐지다) or the future (새로운 삶이 펼쳐지다).","졸업 후에는 새로운 인생이 **펼쳐질** 거예요.","A new life will unfold after graduation."],["한창","the height of, in full swing","<b>한창 -을 때</b> (in the middle of / at the peak of), 한창 바쁘다, 한창나이.","지금은 공부를 **한창** 열심히 할 때예요.","Now is the time to be studying hard."]],"x":[["예감","premonition, hunch","<b>예감이 들다 / 좋다</b>, 좋은 예감, 불길한 예감.","이번에는 잘될 것 같은 **예감**이 들어요.","I have a feeling it'll go well this time."],["예고","advance notice; preview","<b>예고하다</b>, 예고편 (trailer), 예고 없이 (without warning).","비가 **예고** 없이 갑자기 쏟아졌어요.","It suddenly poured without any warning."],["예방","prevention","<b>예방하다</b>, 예방 접종 (vaccination), 사고 예방.","건강한 습관이 병을 **예방**하는 데 도움이 돼요.","Healthy habits help prevent illness."],["예비","preliminary, spare; future (person)","예비 신부 (bride-to-be), 예비 대학생 (incoming student), 예비 부품.","저는 대학원 **예비** 신입생으로서 준비를 하고 있어요.","As an incoming grad student, I'm getting ready."],["예상","expectation, prediction","<b>예상하다</b>, 예상대로 (as expected), 예상 밖 (unexpected).","시험이 **예상**보다 쉬웠어요.","The exam was easier than expected."]]}]});
GUIDE.en.push({"n":20,"t":"한국의 명절","en":"Korean holidays","units":[{"n":1,"t":"설날","g":[{"f":"이야","en":"N? That's no problem / easily solved (brushing off a worry)","core":"Picks out one thing (N) and says it's not a big deal, because there's an easy fix or it's obviously fine: 밥이야 사 먹으면 돼요 (Food? I can just buy it). Typically used to reassure someone or downplay a worry. The second clause usually gives the easy fix (-(으)면 되다) or says it's obviously fine.","forms":[["Noun, 받침","밥이야 · 옷이야 · 돈이야"],["Noun, no 받침","빨래야 · 친구야 · 영어야"]],"rules":["<b>N(이)야</b>: 이야 after a consonant, 야 after a vowel.","Typical pattern: <b>N(이)야 -(으)면 되지요 / 돼요</b>: 옷이야 거기서 사면 돼요.","Also for things that will obviously work out: 친구야 금방 사귀겠지요 (Friends? I'll make them quickly).","It can set up a contrast: 돈이야 있지만 시간이 없어요 (Money I have; it's time I don't).","Don't confuse it with the casual ending -(이)야 (= -이에요 in 반말): 이건 밥이야 (This is rice)."],"ex":[["A: 빨래를 밀리지 않고 할 수 있겠어? B: **빨래야** 주말에 한꺼번에 하면 돼요.","A: Will you keep up with the laundry? B: Laundry? I can just do it all at once on weekends."],["**친구야** 학교에 다니다 보면 금방 생기겠지요.","Friends? I'll make them soon enough once I'm going to school."],["**옷이야** 부족하면 거기서 사면 되니까 걱정하지 마세요.","Clothes? If I run short, I can just buy some there, so don't worry."]]},{"f":"-으라고","en":"so that (someone) will X; hoping (someone) X (purpose when giving)","core":"Gives the purpose or wish behind something you do for someone else, usually a gift: 시험에 붙으라고 찹쌀떡을 사 줬어요 (I bought chapssaltteok so they'd pass the exam). It comes from the quoted command -(으)라고, as if you're saying \"pass!\" as you hand it over. The same form can also just quote a command: 엄마가 일찍 오라고 했어요.","forms":[["Verb, no 받침","쓰라고 · 보라고 · 마시라고"],["Verb, 받침","붙으라고 · 먹으라고 · 입으라고"],["Wishes (adjectives)","건강하라고 · 행복하라고"],["Negative","-지 말라고: 감기 걸리지 말라고"]],"rules":["Main pattern: <b>[purpose]-(으)라고 N을/를 사 주다 / 주다 / 선물하다 / 보내다</b>.","The purpose is what you want the receiver to do or become: 붙으라고, 잘 쓰라고, 따뜻하게 지내라고.","Adjectives work in set wishes: 건강하라고, 행복하라고.","The same form quotes commands: 선생님이 숙제를 하라고 하셨어요. A giving verb after it signals the purpose meaning.","Compare -게 (20과) and -도록 (2과): also purpose, but -(으)라고 sounds like a wish or encouragement aimed at the other person."],"ex":[["동생이 시험에 **붙으라고** 찹쌀떡을 사 줬어요.","I bought my younger sibling chapssaltteok so they'd pass the exam."],["결혼한 친구 부부가 커피를 같이 **마시라고** 커피잔 세트를 선물했어요.","I gave my newlywed friends a coffee cup set so they could have coffee together."],["아버지께서 대학교에서 공부 열심히 **하라고** 노트북을 사 주셨어요.","My dad bought me a laptop so I'd study hard in college."]]}],"v":[["덕담","words of good wishes, blessings","Mostly at New Year's: <b>덕담을 하다 / 나누다</b>. 새해 복 많이 받으세요 is the classic.","세배를 하면 어른들이 **덕담**을 해 주세요.","When you bow, the elders give you good wishes."],["마찬가지","the same, likewise","<b>N와/과 마찬가지이다</b>, 저도 마찬가지예요 (same here).","설날에 고향에 가는 건 외국인도 **마찬가지**예요.","Going home for Seollal is the same for foreigners too."],["세뱃돈","New Year's money (given after bowing)","세배 (New Year's bow) + 돈. <b>세뱃돈을 받다 / 주다</b>.","어렸을 때는 **세뱃돈** 받는 게 제일 좋았어요.","When I was a kid, getting New Year's money was the best part."],["맞이하다","to welcome, greet (a time or person)","<b>새해/설날/손님을 맞이하다</b>. Formal: 새해를 맞이하여.","가족들과 함께 새해를 **맞이했어요**.","I welcomed the new year with my family."],["쓸쓸하다","lonely, desolate","A quiet, empty loneliness, often seasonal or about places: 쓸쓸한 명절, 쓸쓸한 가을.","명절에 혼자 있으니까 좀 **쓸쓸했어요**.","Being alone for the holiday was a little lonely."],["간신히","barely, just barely","Managed with great difficulty: <b>간신히 -았/었다</b>. Same as 겨우.","명절이라 기차표를 **간신히** 구했어요.","Because of the holiday, I barely managed to get a train ticket."],["설마","surely not; no way","Disbelief, expecting a \"no\": <b>설마 -겠어요? / 설마 -는 건 아니지요?</b>","**설마** 설날에도 일하는 건 아니지요?","Surely you're not working on Seollal too?"]],"x":[["국가적","national","-적 noun: 국가적 행사, 국가적 차원.","설날은 **국가적**인 명절이라서 사흘 동안 쉬어요.","Seollal is a national holiday, so we get three days off."],["문화적","cultural","문화적 차이, 문화적 배경.","명절에는 한국의 **문화적** 특징이 잘 드러나요.","Korea's cultural characteristics really show during holidays."],["배경","background","Story or context: <b>역사적 배경</b>, 배경 지식, 배경 음악.","설날의 역사적 **배경**을 알면 더 재미있어요.","It's more interesting if you know the historical background of Seollal."],["종교적","religious","-적 noun: 종교적 의미, 종교적 이유.","한국 명절은 **종교적**인 의미보다 가족 모임의 의미가 커요.","Korean holidays are more about family gatherings than religious meaning."],["풍습","custom, tradition","Folk customs: <b>설날 풍습</b>, 풍습을 지키다.","세배는 설날의 대표적인 **풍습**이에요.","The New Year's bow is the most representative Seollal custom."]]},{"n":2,"t":"추석","g":[{"f":"-게²","en":"so that I/we can X (purpose, usually before a request)","core":"Gives the purpose behind a request or action: 뉴스 좀 듣게 말소리 좀 줄여 줄래? (Can you keep it down so I can hear the news?) The -게 clause is what the speaker (or someone) wants to be able to do, and the main clause is usually a request: -아/어 줄래?, -아/어 주세요, -아/어 봐. 16과 -게요 says the same purpose after the request instead.","forms":[["Verb / adjective stem","듣게 · 공부하게 · 쉬게 · 편하게"],["Ability","-(으)ㄹ 수 있게: 집중할 수 있게"],["Negative","-지 않게: 늦지 않게"]],"rules":["Stem + 게, regardless of 받침.","Typical pattern: <b>X-게 Y-아/어 줄래? / 주세요</b>: 뉴스 좀 듣게 소리 좀 줄여 줄래?","X is usually what the speaker wants to do, so the subject is 나/저 and often left out.","Same meaning as 16과 -게요, in the opposite order: 소리 좀 줄여 줄래? 뉴스 좀 듣게. ↔ 뉴스 좀 듣게 소리 좀 줄여 줄래?","Compare -도록¹ (2과): same purpose meaning but more formal. -게 is everyday speech, especially with family and friends."],"ex":[["시험공부 좀 **하게** 문 좀 닫아 줘.","Close the door, would you? I need to study for my exam."],["청소 좀 **하게** 잠깐 일어나 봐.","Get up for a sec so I can clean."],["케이크 **사게** 2만 원만 더 주세요.","Give me just 20,000 won more so I can buy the cake."]]},{"f":"-으랴 -으랴","en":"busy doing X and doing Y (juggling)","core":"Lists two (or more) things someone was doing at the same time, to show how busy or overwhelmed they were. Usually followed by 바쁘다, 정신이 없다, 힘들다.","forms":[["Verb, no 받침","하랴 · 보랴 · 치우랴"],["Verb, 받침","먹으랴 · 씻으랴 · 만들랴 (ㄹ-stem)"]],"rules":["Verb + -(으)랴, repeated for each activity: <b>-(으)랴 -(으)랴 바쁘다</b>.","Verbs only. No tense on the -(으)랴 parts.","Second clause: <b>바쁘다, 정신이 없다, 힘들다, 시간이 없다</b>.","Expressive and a bit literary, very natural for holiday stories: 음식 하랴 손님 맞으랴…"],"ex":[["추석에 엄마는 음식을 **만들랴** 손님을 **맞으랴** 정말 바쁘셨어요.","On Chuseok, my mom was really busy making food and welcoming guests."],["일**하랴** 대학원 준비**하랴** 쉴 시간이 없어요.","Between work and preparing for grad school, I have no time to rest."],["설거지**하랴** 아이들 **보랴** 정신이 하나도 없었어요.","Between washing dishes and watching the kids, I was totally frazzled."]]}],"v":[["보름달","full moon","보름 = 15th day of the lunar month. Chuseok falls on 8월 보름. <b>보름달을 보며 소원을 빌다</b>.","추석 밤에 **보름달**을 보면서 소원을 빌었어요.","On Chuseok night, I made a wish while looking at the full moon."],["조상","ancestors","<b>조상을 모시다</b> (honor ancestors), 조상님.","추석에는 **조상**께 감사하는 마음으로 차례를 지내요.","On Chuseok, people perform ancestral rites to thank their ancestors."],["커다랗다","huge, very big","More vivid than 크다. ㅎ irregular: 커다래요, 커다란.","하늘에 **커다란** 보름달이 떠 있었어요.","A huge full moon was hanging in the sky."],["송편","songpyeon (half-moon rice cakes)","Chuseok's signature food. <b>송편을 빚다</b> (shape songpyeon by hand).","가족들이 모여서 **송편**을 빚었어요.","My family got together and made songpyeon."],["차례상","table for ancestral rites","차례 = ancestral rite on holidays. <b>차례상을 차리다</b>; 차례를 지내다.","아침 일찍 일어나서 **차례상**을 차렸어요.","We got up early in the morning and set the ancestral rite table."]],"x":[["조그맣다","tiny, little","Cute or vivid version of 작다. ㅎ irregular: 조그매요, 조그만.","**조그만** 손으로 송편을 빚는 아이들이 귀여웠어요.","The kids shaping songpyeon with their tiny hands were adorable."],["번쩍번쩍","sparkling, flashing","Repeated flashing light: <b>번쩍번쩍 빛나다</b>.","불꽃놀이가 하늘에서 **번쩍번쩍** 빛났어요.","The fireworks flashed and sparkled in the sky."],["볼록","bulging slightly (small, round)","Small rounded bulge: 배가 볼록 나오다. Lighter, cuter feel than 불룩.","송편을 너무 많이 먹어서 배가 **볼록** 나왔어요.","I ate so much songpyeon that my belly popped out."],["불룩","bulging (big)","Larger, heavier version of 볼록: 가방이 불룩하다.","선물을 많이 넣어서 가방이 **불룩**해졌어요.","I put so many gifts in that the bag bulged."],["소곤소곤","whispering softly","Gentle, quiet whispering. Neutral or cute.","아이들이 이불 속에서 **소곤소곤** 이야기를 나눴어요.","The kids whispered to each other under the blanket."],["수군수군","whispering (gossiping)","Whispering behind someone's back. Negative nuance compared to 소곤소곤.","친척들이 제 결혼 이야기를 **수군수군**했어요.","My relatives whispered about my marriage behind my back."],["쏙","(slipping in / out) neatly, smoothly (small)","Small thing slipping in or popping out: 쏙 들어가다, 쏙 빼다. Lighter than 쑥.","송편 속에 깨를 **쏙** 넣었어요.","I tucked the sesame filling right into the songpyeon."],["쑥","(sliding in / out) deeply, quickly (big)","Bigger or stronger version of 쏙: 쑥 들어가다, 키가 쑥 크다.","오랜만에 만난 조카가 키가 **쑥** 컸어요.","My nephew had shot up since I last saw him."],["졸졸","trickling (small stream); following closely","(1) Water trickling. (2) Following someone around: 졸졸 따라다니다.","조카가 하루 종일 저를 **졸졸** 따라다녔어요.","My niece followed me around all day."],["줄줄","streaming, flowing (a lot); fluently","(1) Water or sweat streaming. (2) Reciting fluently: 줄줄 외우다.","송편을 빚다가 땀이 **줄줄** 흘렀어요.","Sweat was streaming down while I was making songpyeon."],["콩콩","pitter-patter, light thumping","Light, small thumps: 아이가 콩콩 뛰다, 심장이 콩콩 뛰다.","아이들이 마루에서 **콩콩** 뛰어다녔어요.","The kids were pattering around on the wooden floor."],["쿵쿵","thud, heavy thumping","Bigger, heavier version of 콩콩. Familiar from 8과 쿵쿵거리다.","윗집에서 **쿵쿵** 소리가 났어요.","There was a thudding sound from upstairs."],["퐁당","plop (small thing into water)","Small object dropping into water lightly.","아이가 연못에 돌을 **퐁당** 던졌어요.","The kid tossed a pebble plop into the pond."],["풍덩","splash (big thing into water)","Larger, heavier version of 퐁당.","친구가 장난으로 수영장에 **풍덩** 뛰어들었어요.","My friend jumped into the pool with a big splash as a joke."]]}]});
